1 NOTE http://www.burningviolin.org/family/Web%20Cards/wc05/wc05_237.htm list
2 CONC s him as Arthur Elliott Barton.
2 CONT
2 CONT This is supported in Emily's Memoir, p44-45, which also gives his birt
2 CONC h day, and christening details.
2 CONT
2 CONT p97-98:
2 CONT "[1890] As we sat one morning at breakfast under the trees an Indian p
2 CONC ostcard was brought to me, addressed simply "Titisee - Switzerland"! (
2 CONC ?). It was from Arthur telling us of his engagement to Lilian Wyatt (4
2 CONC 2), daughter of our S.P.G. Missionary friend, and grand-daughter of th
2 CONC e excellent Bishop Caldwell, of Tinnevelly.  Father and he had met the
2 CONC  family at Kodaikanal in the Palni Hills - and I believe they were eng
2 CONC aged a month after.  We received much fuller news of course by the fol
2 CONC lowing mail, but this was my first intimation of the first daughter-in
2 CONC -law to be."
2 CONT
2 CONT In Rev. John Barton's Family Tree book, p1,2,18,85, with note: "51st K
2 CONC ings Own L.I. - 4th Bo.n Rifles: Captain in Punjab Commn. India."
2 CONT
2 CONT VERY POSSIBLY THE REAL AUTHOR OF MOST OF THE ABOVE BOOK- which he appe
2 CONC ars to initial on p49
