1 NOTE ?Is he the Lawrence Rowe who was church warden at South Tawton in 1784
2 CONC  - see notice board inside church and the Lawrence Rowe who was buried
2 CONC  at South Tawton on 11 Dec 1793  Mr Lawrence Rowe is listed in the Lan
2 CONC d Tax  Assessments for South Tawton from 1780 - 1793.  He paid taxes f
2 CONC or Oxenham from 1780-1790, apparently as the occupier.  It appears tha
2 CONC t Madam Elizabeth Acland was the owner and the tax was 3 pounds and 1
2 CONC shilling - one of the highest in the neighbourhood.  From 1791 - 1793
2 CONC he appears to have been the owner of Addlehole at a tax rate of 3 poun
2 CONC ds, nine shillings and five pence.  In 1995 Addlehole was owned by a W
2 CONC illiam Rowe.  (In the 1780 returns there is an Upper and a Lower Addle
2 CONC hole, listed as part of the Acland estate and paying tax of 16/4 and 1
2 CONC 4/4.)
2 CONT
2 CONT There was another Lawrence Rowe, chr South Tawton in 1736 who could ha
2 CONC ve been some or all of the above
2 CONT
2 CONT Needs following up:
2 CONT Will of Lawrence Rowe in Public Record Office, publication  by Br Rec
2 CONC Soc of Devonshire Wills, 1540-1799, page 558
