1 NOTE from http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Barton_(quaker):
2 CONT
2 CONT John Barton (1755 - 1789) was one of the nine English Quaker members o
2 CONC f the "Society for the Abolition of the Slave Trade" set up in 1787 by
2 CONC  William Wilberforce and two other Anglicans . Their efforts ultimatel
2 CONC y led to the passing of the Abolition of the Slave Trade Act, 1807 by
2 CONC British Parliament on 25 March in that year.
2 CONT
2 CONT BUT
2 CONT Year of birth given as 1754 in 'Barton Family Tree' from Robert Barton
2 CONC 's biography of John Barton of Chicester, and also in NJB Papers: "The
2 CONC  Hornes and Jansons" tree, and also (as c1754) in "The Hack Family Doc
2 CONC uments by Chris Durrant", p5.
2 CONT
2 CONT A lot more is in this article:
2 CONT http://www.chichesterquakers.org/John%20Barton.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT He left Carlisle for London in 1783.
