1 NOTE wherry boat owner and merchant.
2 CONT Marriage witnesses: Wm Crane, Wm Odel
2 CONT Homes; 41 Market Row, Repps.
2 CONT        51 wife a  widow with farm of 3 acres.
2 CONT John bap Burgh St Margaret, the rest at Repps.
2 CONT
2 CONT In January 1841 William was attacked and robbed whilst driving home fr
2 CONC om Yarmouth in a gig.  See the account of the trial in the Norfolk chr
2 CONC onicle on 10th April 1841.
2 CONT
2 CONT Repps Vestry Book
2 CONT 1835 - 1843 Wm Bessey in list of ratepayers, assessed on value of  pro
2 CONC perty?
2 CONT      1837-8  property value 2 pounds, paid 1 shilling  (6d in the poun
2 CONC d)
2 CONT      1839-40 property value 4 pounds, paid 1 shilling (lower rate of 3
2 CONC d in the pound)
2 CONT      1841 property detailed - house & land 6 pounds 10 ten shillings,
2 CONC allotment 15  shillings, marsh land 5 shillings..
2 CONT               paid 1 shilling and 3 pence
2 CONT      1843  property 6 pounds & 10 shilllings plus 1 pound
