1 NOTE She met James Bond while on a trip around the world (presumably sent o
2 CONC ff to find a husband), returned to England and then returned to NZ to
2 CONC marry him in 1905. More details in the James Bond notes. For a more ge
2 CONC neral discussion of my ancestor Grahams (for those who care) look at h
2 CONC ttp://www.burningviolin.org/family/, and follow the Grahams link. A lo
2 CONC t of information about the Grahams of Edmond Castle can be found in th
2 CONC e writings of THB Graham, Ellen Octavia’s brother. See especially Tran
2 CONC s. Cumb. Westmor. Ant. Arch. Soc. New Series VII (1907) The Old Villag
2 CONC e of Edmond Castle.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her son-in-law Pop always called her a wonderful old lady. Emphasis on
2 CONC  lady. One gets the impression he was told this many times. I wouldn’t
2 CONC  be surprised. He knew her when he was courting her daughter, old Gran
2 CONC ny, at Victoria Ave. I must find her birth and death dates.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pop told me (in  2006) that Ellen Octavia was very interested in Botan
2 CONC y, and they would often go for trips into the New Zealand countryside
2 CONC to look for new plants.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was cremated and buried in the same plot as James Shiner Bond (Wai
2 CONC kumete cemetery, Anglican Division A, Row 7, Plot 7). The grave marker
2 CONC  is still there (in October, 2008), with her details and James’ detail
2 CONC s. A little battered, but still legible. It had a stone cross on the t
2 CONC op which fell off at some stage, but has been partially replaced. In t
2 CONC he cemetery notes, her occupation was listed as “House Duties”. I also
2 CONC  have a copy of her death notice in the paper.
