1 NOTE Raised in Dargaville (I think), her brother, Harold Anderson, owned th
2 CONC e sawmill there. Wedding details in family Bible. Suffered from rheuma
2 CONC toid arthritis? Buried at the Mangere Cemetery. Pop always said that s
2 CONC he was born in Dargaville, but her birth certificate shows Christchurc
2 CONC h. But her parents were married in Auckland, so I guess they moved aro
2 CONC und a bit.
2 CONT
2 CONT A quote from a web page about Dargaville (http://www.kauricoast.co.nz)
2 CONT “Built many  years prior to the First World War, this mill continued t
2 CONC o operate up until the  1950's. The greater part of its life span was
2 CONC catering for local needs rather  than export. The mill was established
2 CONC  by Anderson and Sundberg, and was known as Anderson's Mill for many y
2 CONC ears. In the latter part of its life it was owned by  the Rope Family.
2 CONC  In 1954 a new company was formed by Morse and Ramsey which  continued
2 CONC  until 1970, when the mill was dismantled and re-erected at Parore, a
2 CONC  little North of Dargaville. The original mill site was upgraded and n
2 CONC ow forms  part of the waterfront area of Dargaville. The extent of the
2 CONC  site was from the  Northern Wairoa Boating Club to that land now occu
2 CONC pied by Woolworths  supermarket. “
