2 CONC  published a large number of articles in the Transactions of the Cumbe
2 CONC rland and Westmorland Antiquities and Archaeological Society (he was t
2 CONC he editor from 1926-1934), many about the Grahams, others about local
2 CONC Cumberland history. I have copies of some of them, especially those pe
