1 NOTE [BBB]:  b 1842, probably in South Africa, when his father was on furlo
2 CONC ugh there.   Ensign 90th Foot, 1861;  Lt ca. 1863.   d 1864 at Mian Mi
2 CONC r (Lahore) in the Punjab, a notoriously unhealthy station.    No activ
2 CONC e service.    He was godson of John Peter iv, who approved of him.
2 CONC He was a good artist, and used to send home clever sketches of his sur
2 CONC roundings.
2 CONT
2 CONT [Is he the author of the few sketches and letter we have at home? Almo
2 CONC st certainly. The author of the letter calls himself Uncle Jack, and h
2 CONC e was indeed the Uncle of Ellen Leah, who ended up with the letter. Yo
2 CONC u should be able to view a copy of this letter by clicking on the mult
2 CONC imedia link on Despreaux’s web card.]
2 CONT
2 CONT [BBB]: “Despreaux John _, Thomas Ebenezer John's son, enjoyed only a s
2 CONC adly short career with his British regiment, for after but three years
2 CONC  in India he died at Mian Mir, the new name for the old Lahore cantonm
2 CONC ents, with their terrible reputation for unhealthy conditions.”
