1 NOTE Lart is certainly wrong on one thing, as he has Magdalena Elizabeth, b
2 CONC orn in 1720, the daughter of Theophile de la Coeur, born circa 1721. I
2 CONC  don’t think so. It’s most likely that Lart got confused (as Magdalena
2 CONC ’s father seems also to have been called Samuel) and inserted a spurio
2 CONC us generation.
2 CONT
2 CONT BBC gives her name as de Brize, thus suggesting a link to the famous F
2 CONC rench family of that name, but BBB claims this is certainly incorrect,
2 CONC  and that the two families are entirely unconnected. It’s not clear wh
2 CONC at information was used to get this conclusion. However, it seems clea
2 CONC r that there is no direct evidence to connect these Desbrisay to the f
2 CONC amous French family, except for a lot of wishful thinking and assumpti
2 CONC ons about unknown children. For example, “The Family DesBrisay”, a fam
2 CONC ily history compiled by Reverend Henry de la Cour DesBrisay about 1884
2 CONC , is full of “Presuming therefore...”, “it is probable that ...”, “We
2 CONC may presume that ...” etc. Not very convincing.
