1 NOTE [Lart, II, 13]
2 CONT According to the Red Book: m. 1st: Dorothy Gladwell (1766) 2nd: Lucy S
2 CONC later (1792). Continuation of descent down to 1867 shown in the chart
2 CONC in possession of Mrs Graham of Edmond Castle. This must surely mean [B
2 CONC BC].
2 CONT Details also given in [Lart, II, 14].
2 CONT
2 CONT [BBB] calls this branch the first English branch and gives a lot of de
2 CONC tails.
2 CONT “Solomon entered the Army, being commissioned as an ensign at the age
2 CONC of 13.   He was in the expedition to Belle Ile in France three years l
2 CONC ater, and then took part in the capture of Martinique, where he was wh
2 CONC en his uncle Peter died.   At the end of the Seven Years' War, he was
2 CONC placed on half pay, and later became cashier of the Dublin Bank.   Thi
2 CONC s branch, being the senior one, produces the Head of the family, (curr
2 CONC ently Raymond Etienne of Rampisham) and a number of remarkable soldier
2 CONC s.”
2 CONT
2 CONT [BBB]: Ensign 76th Foot (Rufane's) 21 Oct 1758;  2 Lt 27 Aug 1760.   H
2 CONC e was with the regt on,9 Mar 1761, and therefore probably with it duri
2 CONC ng operations at Belle Isle (W coast of France) Mar-Nov 1761, and late
2 CONC r in those at Martinique in 1762 when Peter d there on 28 Oct of that
2 CONC year.   Solomon was Peter's heir.   He went to half-pay on the disband
2 CONC ment of the regt at the end of the Seven Years' War, 1763, and later b
2 CONC ecame cashier of the Dublin Bank.
2 CONT
2 CONT He m 1st, in Dublin, 3 May 1766, Dorothea, dau of Francis Gladwell, of
2 CONC  Dublin;  they had issue 17 children : Magdalene ii, Dorothea i, Anne
2 CONC iv, Frances, Simeon Peter, Henrietta ii, Charles John, Dorothea ii, Lu
2 CONC cy, Charlotte, Alicia i, Jasper Desbrisay i, Solomon Hugh, Richard, Ma
2 CONC ria Jane, Lestock Frances i, John Peter Wilson and Henry.   Dorothea d
2 CONC  4 days after the birth of the last child in 1789, and Solomon m 2nd,
2 CONC at Liverpool, 4 Apr 1792, Lucy (Lucinda), dau of John Slater, of Liver
2 CONC pool;  they had issue : Dorothy i.   Solomon was drowned in the River
2 CONC Dee at Chester, where he resided latterly, when going home in a great
2 CONC storm at night, 21 Dec 1810.
2 CONT
2 CONT ___
2 CONT DB:
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p17173.htm#i171723 gives his wife's name as
2 CONC Dorothy Gradwell, not Gladwell, and gives parentage for both wives.
