2 CONC turn to India where he was born, from England where he was raised. (Re
2 CONC call that his mother raised him at Bury St. Edmunds).
2 CONT
2 CONT [BBB] says: “b in Calcutta, 26 Dec 1796.  Appointed a Writer in the Ma
2 CONC dras Civil Service, HEICS, 1815;   Assistant Registrar, Provincial Cou
2 CONC rt, S Division, Madras Presidency, 1818;  Acting Judge 1824;  Asst Jud
2 CONC ge, Canara 1827.   Thereafter continued in judicial appts in the Presi
2 CONC dency, until his retirement in 1851, as Civil & Sessions Judge, Northe
2 CONC rn Circuits.  Furlough to South Africa, Sep 1841 to end 1843.”
