1 NOTE [RBB]: m. Charlotte Hanson (m. 1834?)
2 CONT Gracey Tovey (m. 1850?)
2 CONT (I can’t quite figure out what the book says, so this could be wrong.)
2 CONT
2 CONT [BBB]: b posthumously at Calcutta, 1807.   Generally known as Henry.
2 CONC Admitted as a cadet at Addiscombe, the EIC's Military Academy, 1823-4.
2 CONC    Arrived in India, as 2 Lt from 1824;  Lt 1827;  Capt 1839;  Bvt Maj
2 CONC or 1847;  Lt Col 1849;  Col 1856;  Major General 1860.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joined Bengal Sappers & Miners 1825;  took part in siege of Bhurtpore
2 CONC 1825-26, and commanded two companies of the S&M during the storming.
2 CONC Carried out surveys of the lower part of the Doab 1827, and of Bhurtpo
2 CONC re Territory 1830-32.   Shekhawat expedition 1834.  In 1835 he was sel
2 CONC ected to go on a mission to Jaisalmer and Bahawalpur, states in Wester
2 CONC n India, with another officer, to settle various border disputes, and
2 CONC to collect information on the geography of the country, its inhabitant
2 CONC s and the military resources of the states.   His particular qualifica
2 CONC tions made him a most successful observer;  his competence in the nati
2 CONC ve languages, his habit of constant mixing with native all ranks and g
2 CONC reat mental and bodily activity, enabled him to do more than merely ad
2 CONC d to geographical knowledge.  In fact, the two young officers were ins
2 CONC trumental in bringing about peaceful settlements of several disputes,
2 CONC and they consorted amicably with various rulers and with Shah Shuja, t
2 CONC he dispossessed king of Kabul.
2 CONT
2 CONT After this, Henry continued to be employed on survey work in the Benga
2 CONC l Presidency and went to China on leave in 1837.   He was then transfe
2 CONC rred to the Calcutta area, as Agent for suspension bridges and Superin
2 CONC tendent of canals.   He managed these very well, and after five years
2 CONC took charge of those at Delhi.   From 1846 to 1850 he was Superintendi
2 CONC ng Engineer, Central Provinces, after which he went on leave to the UK
2 CONC  for what seems to have been the first time in 25 years.   He was then
2 CONC  Superintending Engineer, PWD NW Provinces 1854-56, and CE PWD Nagpur
2 CONC Territory for the next five years.   By 1862 he was extra Superintende
2 CONC nt in charge of the 200-mile-long road from Saugor to Kalpi, and also
2 CONC Comdt of Engrs as Colonel.   One supposes that he might have received
2 CONC some award had he survived to retire in the ordinary way;  as it was,
2 CONC he had only the Bhurtpore medal to show for his 38 years of useful ser
2 CONC vice.
2 CONT
2 CONT m 1st 1834, at Agra, UP, India, Charlotte, dau of Capt William Hanson,
2 CONC  of the Pay Dept, and had a dau, Charlotte Bosanquet.   Charlotte d at
2 CONC  Barrackpore, Bengal 1840 and Henry m 2nd at Paignton, Devon, Matilda
2 CONC Grace, dau of Alexander Tovey, 20th Foot;  they had a son and a dau, A
2 CONC rthur C T and Mary Hamilton.
2 CONT
2 CONT He d of dysentery in 1862 at Cawnpore.
2 CONT
2 CONT [BBC] gives the date of death as 1866.
