1 NOTE [BBC]
2 CONT
2 CONT Continuation of descent down to 1869 is shown on chart drawn and ?? by
2 CONC  W. and A. K. Johnston, Edinburgh. So says [RBB], and Granny must have
2 CONC  been talking about [BBC].
2 CONT
2 CONT Here’s a copy of a letter he wrote in 1781 (sent to me by Vince O’Grad
2 CONC y). He was obviously working in India, and in touch with his Hardy cou
2 CONC sins and with Thomas Boileau, his cousin.
2 CONT -------------------
2 CONT Cossimbuzar Oct 6 1781
2 CONT My Dear Cousin,
2 CONT as I do not know how soon the Swallow Packet now under dispatch may sa
2 CONC il I sit £255 down to acknowledge the receits of your letter of the 26
2 CONC  Dec & to assure you that I will do everything in my power to promote
2 CONC your brother Peters views in this Country. tho I sincerely wish he had
2 CONC  come out in some appointment for as affairs are now situated in India
2 CONC  very little is to be hoped for without one. I have the pleasure to te
2 CONC ll you that he is safe arrived in Calcutta and in the house of an cous
2 CONC in Tom Boileau who is doing very well in the Law line - I have wrote t
2 CONC o him to come here as soon as he can with convenience & when I have th
2 CONC e pleasure to see him we will consult together how to proceed & let yo
2 CONC u know the results. my family write in affectionate love & best wishes
2 CONC  to you & yours & I remain
2 CONT My dear Simeon
2 CONT Your Ever Devoted
2 CONT Kinsman
2 CONT Simeon Droz
2 CONT Mr Simeon Henry Hardy
2 CONT Cork
2 CONT Should Captain Tober Hall who commands the Swallow Packet & has charge
2 CONC  of this letter fall in your way I request you will shew him every Civ
2 CONC ility on my account & should he put into your care a parcel addressed
2 CONC to my Dear sister Louisa I entreat you will forward it to her by the s
2 CONC afest conveyance.
2 CONT -------------------------
