1 NOTE Jean Boileau, 2nd Baron went with many other nobles and gentlemen to t
2 CONC he succour of the Emperor Sigismund, and was killed at the battle of N
2 CONC icopolis in 1396.
2 CONT
2 CONT C-D does not cover any of the generations between Jean II and the firs
2 CONC t Etienne. Presumably he agreed with Lart that the documentation was i
2 CONC nadequate.
2 CONT [C-D, III, 384] “Jean Boileau, II of that name, descended from Etienne
2 CONC , was killed at the battle of Nicopolis, where the Christians fought t
2 CONC he Sultan Amurat, on the 28 September, 1396. He was among the 2000 Gen
2 CONC tlemen Volunteers who went with the Duc of Nevers to the aid of the Em
2 CONC peror Sigismond. As a consequence of this Crusade he was ordered by th
2 CONC e Duc to carry on his arms trois croix en sautoir; he never did this.”
