1 NOTE [BBB]: There is a good deal of uncertainty about the three or four ind
2 CONC ividuals, all named Jean, who follow next.   There is no evidence to s
2 CONC ubstantiate the existence of a Jean, as son of Robert and who, it is s
2 CONC uggested, was born in 1270 and died in 1352.    The first to appear in
2 CONC  '1754' is Jean, Notaire du Roi, who, with his son Jean, was ennobled,
2 CONC  as well as their posterity, by King Charles V of France, in September
2 CONC  1371, and is shown by the Letters of Nobility given to them and regis
2 CONC tered in the Chambre de Comptes of Paris.   A copy of this entry was o
2 CONC btained in 1667, perhaps with the idea of using it in support of the f
2 CONC amily's claim to 'Noblesse', and it is reproduced in full in '1754'.
