1 NOTE Robert Boileau son of Etienne, accompanied Louis IX on his expedition
2 CONC to the Crusades in 1270, and perished at the siege of Tunis.
2 CONT [BBB]: According to '1754', Etienne's son Robert took the Cross, and w
2 CONC ent with St Louis on the Crusade to the Holy Land, dying there in 1270
2 CONC .   In fact, this, the eighth and last Crusade, went only as far as Tu
2 CONC nis in North Africa.   The army was decimated by disease, among the vi
2 CONC ctims being the King himself;  and it is said that he was shriven on h
2 CONC is deathbed by a priest named Geoffroi Boileau.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nothing else is known of Robert or of his children.   No connection be
2 CONC tween him and Jean, the next in order, is stated either in '1754' or i
2 CONC n the pedigree produced by Nicolas Boileau-Despreaux, the poet, when h
2 CONC e was called upon to prove his nobility.
