1 NOTE Eighth daughter of Sir David Carnegie, 4th Bt., grandfather of sir Jam
2 CONC es Carnegie, 6th Bt. and 9th Earl of Southesk. See what I mean about a
2 CONC ll the details, when a title is involved. Yukkity doo da.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir David Carnegie (E001, by D003) was born about 1754, the fourth Bar
2 CONC onet and seventh Earl of Southesk. He succeeded his father at age twel
2 CONC ve. David was educated at Eton, St. Andrews, and Christ Church, Oxford
2 CONC , where he was distinguished for his literary attainments.
2 CONT     The trustees paid off all his father's debts, and the estates were
2 CONC  conveyed to him free of burdens. He purchased the lands of Arnhjall a
2 CONC nd Leuchars, but later sold these. He rebuilt Kinnaird in 1791 and 179
2 CONC 2.
2 CONT     In 1784 David was elected Member of Parliament for the Montrose Bu
2 CONC rghs; in 1796 he was elected for the county of Forfar, which he repres
2 CONC ented until his death.
2 CONT     David married Agnes Murray Elliot on a contract dated 29 Apr 1783
2 CONC at Edinburgh. Agnes was 16 Dec 1763 in Edinburgh, the daughter of Andr
2 CONC ew Elliot of Greenwells and Elizabeth Plumstead. Agnes died 9 June 186
2 CONC 0 at Leamington.
2 CONT     David died 25 May 1805 in London; he was buried in the Church of S
2 CONC t. Martin-in-the-Fields.
