1 NOTE http://jmw.dynip.com/Genealogy/. Also called Samuel. Theophilus is lis
2 CONC ted in the 1735 Dublin Directory and was stationed at Cork Hill. He wa
2 CONC s Agent for the 2nd Regiment of Foot on the Irish Establishment also a
2 CONC t Cork Hill, according to the "List of General and Field Officers as T
2 CONC hey Rank in the Army 1754," which is in the Library of the British Mus
2 CONC eum. In "Freeman's journal' of the 13th September 1763 issue, he appea
2 CONC rs as a Captain, crossing to Ireland by the Holyhead Packet.
2 CONT He was the first of the name to come to England after the Edict of Nan
2 CONC tes was revoked.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1769, Theophilus wrote a letter to his son, Thomas, on the occasion
2 CONC  of Thomas leaving for his assignment on Prince Edward Island.  Theoph
2 CONC ilus was in London at the time.  It can be found at http://www.islandr
2 CONC egister.com/letters/desbrisay1769.html
