1 NOTE 4th Dragoons. Born about 1729 and died on 22 Nov 1818 in Worcester, EN
2 CONC G, UK aged about 89.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death Notes:P.E.I Gazette February 13, 1819:
2 CONT
2 CONT DIED. At the city of Worcester, England, 22d Novr. 1818, Jasper DesBri
2 CONC say, Esq, aged 89, elder brother of Col. DesBrisay of this Town. He wa
2 CONC s an officer at the battle of Culloden, 1745. He married a second wife
2 CONC  at the age of 45 (?), daughter of Sir John Davie, by whom he had one
2 CONC son who inherited his Estate.
