1 NOTE Ma. I remember her a lot better, as she didn’t die until I was a lot o
2 CONC lder. I was overseas, living in LA, when she died, so I missed most of
2 CONC  her last years. Lived up Ravensbourne Rd, in that house with a pictur
2 CONC e window looking over St. Clair and St. Kilda. Her health bothered her
2 CONC  a lot and boy did she complain. Not always free with her money. Dad w
2 CONC ould tease her unmercifully (but not maliciously) about her legs being
2 CONC  like those of a plucked chicken. She kind of brought it on herself. S
2 CONC he’s buried in Anderson’s Bay cemetery and I’ve never visited her grav
2 CONC e. That’s rather sad, I suppose.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was a Home Economics teacher, at Marlborough College, starting in
2 CONC 1928. She insisted that we always wash our hands before doing any cook
2 CONC ing. As I remember, we never listened to her.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was very good at sewing (after all she had a Dip.Home Science, one
2 CONC  of the youngest in the class) and always dressed her children beautif
2 CONC ully.
2 CONT
2 CONT She studied at Otago University, and stayed at Studholm Hall, and was
2 CONC the youngest in her class. After graduating, she taught up in the Nort
2 CONC h Island for a while (Napier or Hastings?) and then came back to teach
2 CONC  at Marlborough College, where she met Robert Adair McPherson. In Blen
2 CONC heim, she boarded with Mrs. Elvey, and Gummy made fun of her only givi
2 CONC ng half a banana for lunch. She had a reputation for being miserable a
2 CONC nd not feeding them properly.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kate and Grandfather (i.e., John Neal) didn’t approve of Mum’s father
2 CONC (Freda’s husband) at all. They called him Simpkins. Don’t know why. In
2 CONC  retaliation, Robert’s father called Freda, Freezer. What a giggle the
2 CONC y all must have had. Freda only met Robert’s father once, because he d
2 CONC ied shortly after they met (note how Benjamin died when Freda was only
2 CONC  22 or so).
2 CONT
2 CONT Freda was married in a pale ice-blue dress. NOT in white, as Valerie w
2 CONC as born less than nine months after the wedding. Ho Ho Ho. Mum thinks
2 CONC this is very funny.
