1 NOTE Educated at Spring Creek Public School. Was shearing sheep by the age
2 CONC of 15. Lucky him. In 1898 he went into partnership with his brother Fr
2 CONC ank in the Spring Creek property, “Burnlea”, previously owned by their
2 CONC  father. AFter a few years, Frank sold his share to John and shifted t
2 CONC o Marshlands. John continued to crop this heavy agricultural land unti
2 CONC l his brother, Albert, purchased the property for 100 pounds per acre
2 CONC in 1918. John purchased “Lucknow”, 740 acres of rolling tussock countr
2 CONC y at Starborough, where he farmed until his death. “Lucknow” was appar
2 CONC ently named by the former owner who won it in a land ballot, and excla
2 CONC imed at her luck. Hmmmm...... sounds plausible. Probably nothing to do
2 CONC  with India.
2 CONT
2 CONT John was a keen sportsman, representing Marlborough in rugby, and play
2 CONC ing cricket and shooting guns and things.
