1 NOTE [C-D, XVII, 406]. One of the principal witnesses in an act of 1084, by
2 CONC  which Raimond, Count of Toulouse, abandonned the right to depose the
2 CONC Bishop of Béziers. In a charter of that count, in 1094, Pierre-Guillau
2 CONC me and Arnault, his brother, made a gift to the Abbey of St.-Victor de
2 CONC  Marseille, of the lands which they possessed along the Rhone. In 1096
2 CONC , Count Raimond gave the church of Beaucaire to the Abbey of Chaise-Di
2 CONC eu, by the advice, so he said, of the illustrious men Pierre-Guillaume
2 CONC  de Rochemore & Arnault, his brother.
2 CONT
2 CONT [C-D, XVII, 406] gives a short history of the Rochemore antecedents. I
2 CONC n the XI century two branches of the family lived on the banks of the
2 CONC Rhone; one, in the castle and town of Beaucaire; the other, in the tow
2 CONC n of Arles, extinct by the XVI century. The first branch was establish
2 CONC ed by the XV century in the town of Lunel.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arms, according to [C-D, XVII, 416] and Rietstap: d’azur, à trois rocs
2 CONC  d’échiquier d’argent. Pour devise: Rupibus Firmior.
