1 NOTE of Tenterden. He had other children besides Jeremiah but Burke’s doesn
2 CONC ’t list them.
2 CONT
2 CONT [CT]: In the South Aisle.
2 CONT 510. Over the arch leading to the South Chancel. Arms. Curteis impalin
2 CONC g Beale.
2 CONT Edward CURTEIS, gent, died 3rd October, 1777, aged 65 years. He marrie
2 CONC d Sarah, third daughter of Richard BEALE, gent, and had issue three so
2 CONC ns and two daughters Jeremiah, Richard, William, Sarah, wife of Mr. Th
2 CONC omas JACKSON and Mary, wife of Mr. George JEMMETT. Sarah Jackson died
2 CONC 5th July, 1779, aged 38 years, and was buried in her Father’s vault. S
2 CONC he left issue two daughters Sarah and Eleanor, Eleanor died an infant.
2 CONC  Sarah, the widow of Edward Curteis, died 20th February, 1791, aged 78
2 CONC  years. Elizabeth, wife of William Curteis, died 29th December, 1795,
2 CONC aged 43 years. She was the surviving daughter and heiress of Mr. Franc
2 CONC es WHITFELD of Bethersden. Jane, wife of Jeremiah Curteis, died 1st Ma
2 CONC rch, 1796, aged 54 years. She was one of the three daughters and co-he
2 CONC iresses of Mr. Searles GILES, late of Biddenden. Jane, daughter of Mr.
2 CONC  Jeremiah Curteis and Jane his wife, died 11th June, 1796, aged 20 yea
2 CONC rs. Edward Jeremiah Curteis, eldest son of Edward Jeremiah Curteis of
2 CONC Windmill Hill, Sussex, and Mary [BARRETT] his wife, died 7th August, 1
2 CONC 795, aged 4- years. The said Jeremiah Curteis [of Rye] Esq., died Dece
2 CONC mber, 31st, 1806, aged 71 years. He left surviving issue Edward Jeremi
2 CONC ah Curteis of Windmill Hill, Sussex, Esq., Martha [MASCALL], Anne [COL
2 CONC LET] and Katherine Sarah [LUNFORD].
