1 NOTE Mayor of Tenterden, 1622.
2 CONT
2 CONT [CT]: 477. Here lyeth interred the body of Stephen CVRTEIS Esq., Maior
2 CONC  of this Towne and Hundred, who died the 12th of August, 1654. Having
2 CONC ……….. sonne named Nathaniel and onely davghter named Elizabeth. Being
2 CONC aged 28 years.Registers. Stephen Curteis Esqre. Major, buryed the 12th
2 CONC  day August, 1654.
2 CONT
2 CONT It seems that the father of Nathaniel and Elizabeth is not the same as
2 CONC  the Stephen, father of Samuel, who appears in the Curteis pedigree. E
2 CONC ither that, or the pedigree made a big mistake somewhere. Wouldn’t sur
2 CONC prise me. The father of Nathaniel was the Mayor of Tenterden, for sure
2 CONC , which would tend to identify him with my Curteis’s. However, his wil
2 CONC l seems to say that his wife was called Mary Stark, not Short, if I’m
2 CONC reading it correctly.
2 CONT
2 CONT I haven’t yet transcribed the full will, but some of people listed are
2 CONC  (I think):
2 CONT Dear and loving wife, Mary Curteis
2 CONT Sisters Elizabeth Curteis and Martha Whitfeld[?]
2 CONT Brothers Samuel Stark and Robert Stark
2 CONT Son Nathaniel Curteis
2 CONT Daughter Elizabeth Curteis
2 CONT Brothers Mr. William Randall and Mr. George Whitfeld
