1 NOTE Main source is [BC]. Amelia Neal and family came to Nelson on the infa
2 CONC mous Lloyds (sailed London September 11th 1841 - arrived Nelson Februa
2 CONC ry 9th 1842), about which a great deal has been written. Conditions on
2 CONC  the ship were appalling. Sixteen families lost all their children, an
2 CONC d a total of 67 children died on the voyage, bad even for the usual im
2 CONC migrant ship.
2 CONT The Neal family was
2 CONT Amelia - 25;  William - 9;  George - 6;   Charles - 4;  Ellen - 2;
2 CONC Henry - 11 months
2 CONT Ellen died on 20 September, Henry on 25 Sept, and Charles on the 7th o
2 CONC f November.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/%7Eourstuff/Maryann.htm says t
2 CONC hat Daniel Matthew, age 22, Farm Labourer, brother of Mrs Neal in the
2 CONC preliminary expedition, came to Nelson on the Mary Ann, in 1842: Saile
2 CONC d Downs September 24th 1841 - arrived Nelson Tuesday February 8th 1842
2 CONC  at 8.30am.
