1 NOTE [BBB]: “In Nîmes, during the winter of 1683-84, which was extremely ri
2 CONC gorous, the dragoons committed the most odious excesses.   While there
2 CONC  is no actual proof that the Boileau family suffered under this persec
2 CONC ution, there is no reason to think that they did not share in the gene
2 CONC ral misery.  It is at any rate on record that an old man, M. de la Cas
2 CONC sagne, son of Daniel d'Arnaud and Anne i Boileau, had fifty dragoons b
2 CONC illeted on him, who kept him awake until he at last bought one hour's
2 CONC sleep for fifty crowns, and in the end, worn out, he abjured.”
