1 NOTE Lieut.-Col. of Cavalry, drowned at Naples
2 CONT
2 CONT [C-D, III, 386] : successively Captain in the Regiment of Roussillon,
2 CONC Major in the Regiment of the Cardinal of Sainte-Cecile, and finally Li
2 CONC eutenant-Colonel of Cavalry in that of Estrigi (?), in which position
2 CONC he drowned at Naples.
2 CONT
2 CONT [BBB]: b 1620-25, and still under 30 when his father made his will on
2 CONC 3rd January, 1648.  Capt in the Regt de Rousillon, his father having b
2 CONC een given a King's commission of a company of 100 foot-soldiers in the
2 CONC  regt of M le Comte de Rousillon, dated 10th January, 1642.
2 CONT
2 CONT The regt was disbanded in 1645.  During the period  1642-45, it was en
2 CONC gaged in Catalunya 1642-43, with the Army of the Rhine 1644, including
2 CONC  the battle of Fribourg and the siege of Philipsburg, and in Catalunya
2 CONC  again in 1645, but there is no information to show if François was pr
2 CONC esent with the regt throughout.   This may be assumed since he had fol
2 CONC lowed a military career.   In 1648 he was Capt-Major in command of the
2 CONC  Regt de Ste Cecile, and was certified as having served throughout the
2 CONC  campaign of that year in Catalunya.   He is known to have become late
2 CONC r a Lieut Col in the Cavalry Regt of Destrigi, but nothing can be lear
2 CONC nt about this unit.   He was drowned on a voyage to Naples, which must
2 CONC  have been before his father's death in 1657, as it is stated that Jac
2 CONC ques ii, the second , then succeeded as Seigneur de Castelnau.
