1 NOTE He entered the army.
2 CONT
2 CONT [C-D, III, 386]  He served in les Galères and in Anjou, Cavalry.
2 CONT
2 CONT [BBB]: “Sieur de Vignargues.   Served in 'Les Galeres', which appears
2 CONC to have been the regt of that name, and not the actual vessels propell
2 CONC ed by galley-slaves, to which many Huguenots were condemned for trying
2 CONC  to escape from France, or for some other offence as obdurate Protesta
2 CONC nts;  his name does not appear in any list of such individuals.  He al
2 CONC so served with the cavalry regt of Anjou.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was living at Nîmes in 1668, and maintained his nobility with other
2 CONC  members of the family.   After the Revocation, he at first abjured, a
2 CONC nd is included in a list of 'nouveaux Converts', the Intendant comment
2 CONC ing on him that he was a bad convert.  Later Charles and his wife (Mar
2 CONC garet de Galtier de Pomperdu) whom he m 1673 (no issue) escaped to Swi
2 CONC tzerland, where he d at Lausanne in 1707, and his wife in 1709.”
