1 NOTE First cadet-gentilhomme, and then Captain in the grenadiers-a-cheval o
2 CONC f Brandenburgh, killed at the siege of Tournai, 1709. [This is word-fo
2 CONC r-word identical in Lart and [C-D, III, 386]. I bet that Lart just cop
2 CONC ied. What a naughty man.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Lart and CD conflate Francois and Henri into one person. I follow BBB
2 CONC here.
2 CONT
2 CONT [BBB]: “The first of the Boileau family to leave France were the two e
2 CONC ldest surviving sons of Jacques ii, Henri iii and Jean-Louis i.   They
2 CONC  were in one of the 'Compagnies des Cadets' established in France for
2 CONC the sons of Nobles or of former officers whose fortune was not equal t
2 CONC o their birth, and to whom military service offered more opportunities
2 CONC  than other vocations.   They were trained in all the knowledge and dr
2 CONC ills necessary, and then placed in the subaltern ranks of the army.
2 CONC  Among them were a large number of young Huguenots, and after the Revo
2 CONC cation many of these escaped to Brandenburg.   Some of the companies,
2 CONC including that at Besançon, where Henri and Jean-Louis were stationed,
2 CONC  were near to the frontier, and so it was easy for a crowd of cadets t
2 CONC o get over.   The two young Boileaus did so on 7th December, 1685, and
2 CONC  went to Brandenburg, where the Elector was making the Huguenots welco
2 CONC me, and especially those who were officers and soldiers.”
