2 CONT
2 CONT [BBB]: “Became a wine merchant in Portugal, no doubt engaged in the po
2 CONC rt wine trade, in conjunction with the family wine importing business
2 CONC in Dublin.   He was in the Lisbon earthquake of 1755, and survived, co
2 CONC ntrary to mistaken reports that a Charles had perished.   He was a sig
2 CONC natory to a memorandum to King George II, and a petition to the Secret
2 CONC ary of State in London, from British merchants in Portugal, asking for
2 CONC  assistance to put their affairs on a sound footing again.   The answe
2 CONC r is not known.
2 CONT
