2 CONC in 1804, he bought a house on the south bank of the Thames at Mortlake
2 CONC , which he named 'Castelnau Place'.   This was his principal residence
2 CONC  until his death in 1837, at the age of 91.   It them passed to his da
2 CONC ughter Henrietta Maria, and was later occupied successively by Sir Hen
2 CONC ry Willock, who had married the daughter of Henrietta ii and Samuel Da
2 CONC vis, and by their son, husband of Mary Elisabeth i.   The house was ev
2 CONC entually demolished.
