1 NOTE Chev. governor of the Chateau Stenay. Sgr. de la Touche, in Touraine.
2 CONC This family came originally from the Bourbonnais.
2 CONT He lived in the parish of Chillé, near Chinon. He and his brother, Ren
2 CONC é de La Valette, Sgr. de La Brosse, living at St. Laurent-du-Lin, near
2 CONC  Angers, maintained their noblesse since the year 1532, commencing wit
2 CONC h their grandfather, in 1668.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arms: D’azur, à la fasce d’or surmontée de 3 etoiles de même.
2 CONT
2 CONT There are lots and lots of de la Valette in C-D, but I can’t find a Sg
2 CONC r. de la Touche, or de la Brosse, and the coat-of-arms seems quite dif
2 CONC ferent. In addition, the ones in C-D go back a long way, which doesn’t
2 CONC  square with the information in Lart that they were a recently ennoble
2 CONC d family. So Pierre must have been from a quite different family I thi
2 CONC nk. There are claims on the web that this Pierre de la Valette was dir
2 CONC ectly related to the Valettes in C-D, but C-D doesn’t agree and the cl
2 CONC aims are highly implausible in my opinion. I think it’s far more likel
2 CONC y they were minor, recent, nobility.
