1 NOTE [C-D, IV, 602]. Paid homage to the King for the lands of Saint-Côme (C
2 CONC osme) on 23 March, 1552, and acquired, by a contract of 19 September 1
2 CONC 557, the lands and Seigneurie of la Boissière, from Jacques de Bouzène
2 CONC , Chevalier, Seigneur of the preceding. He distinguished himself in th
2 CONC e Protestant party during the wars of the League, in which he served a
2 CONC broad as Ensign in the Company of Pierre Susu [?], called Captain Boui
2 CONC llarge, in 1567, surprising [?] the town of Nimes on the 15th of Novem
2 CONC ber, 1569, and made Governor of that town on 11 June, 1580. He went to
2 CONC  the aid of Montpellier to lift the siege of that town by the Marshal
2 CONC Montmorency-Damville, Governor of the Province, being there in person
2 CONC [?] on 1 Oct. 1577. He was made Gentilhomme ordinaire de la Chambre du
2 CONC  Roi, by Brevet on 22 Jan 1581.
