1 NOTE Seems she had 8 children in 8 years, and then died. No bloody wonder.
2 CONC Poor woman.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lart gives details of a few other Primaudayes, but the relationship to
2 CONC  Marguerite is not clear. Possibly she was the sister of Gabriel de la
2 CONC  Primaudaye, granddaughter of Nicolas de la Primaudaye, conseiller and
2 CONC  secretaire du Roy, in 1540.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arms: Semé de France, à l’écu d’or en abîme, chargé d’un tourteau de s
2 CONC able traversé d’une patte de griffon d’or. These are different from th
2 CONC e arms given by [SF], which are probably more reliable as the pictures
2 CONC  are also given in the Collot D’Escury portrait, i.e., France ancient,
2 CONC  in bend sinister a lion’s gamb couped or armed gules, over all an ine
2 CONC scutcheon or. [Seems like SF forgot about the tourteau de sable which
2 CONC appears in the picture but not the blazon].
