1 NOTE We know from [BHSP] that Renée was killed at the massacre of Vassy, in
2 CONC  1562. (The Duc de Guise, travelling to his estates, stopped in Vassy
2 CONC on a Sunday. A few of his servants got into a scuffle with some Huguen
2 CONC ots who were attending a service in a nearby church, and the whole thi
2 CONC ng escalated until the Guise faction set the church on fire, and kille
2 CONC d a number of the congregation.)
2 CONT
2 CONT She was murdered in front of her two young sons, aged 14 and 15. Accor
2 CONC ding to my crappy translation of [BHSP]:
2 CONT “Everything that we have been able to learn about the origins of her h
2 CONC usband, was told to my grandmother, Marie Le Noir, by her late husband
2 CONC  David Collot, esquire, seigneur d'Escury. He said to her that when he
2 CONC  was about 15 years old, and his brother a year younger, his mother wa
2 CONC s killed in the massacre in the church at Vassy, a small town in Champ
2 CONC agne, on the Bloise, in the first religious civil war in the reign of
2 CONC Charles IX. His mother perished in the church at the hands of the army
2 CONC  of the duc de Guise. While they were chanting Psalm 88, the barbarian
2 CONC s entered the church, sword in hand, and massacred everybody there, an
2 CONC d he and his brother could hear their mother, who was a widow, asking
2 CONC God many times to save her children, for the sake of her who was dying
2 CONC  for his holy name”.
2 CONT
2 CONT If I read it correctly, the two young boys were saved because they had
2 CONC  white in their hats. I think. White was the colour of the troops of t
2 CONC he Duc de Guise.
