1 NOTE [DHSP, 153]: Dit de Maltortel. Seigneur d'Uzès en partie, d'Ansouis, d
2 CONC e Cucuron, de Vaugine, de la Motte etc. He followed the count Charles
2 CONC of Anjou to the conquest of Naples in 1266. On the 12th of January, 12
2 CONC 76, he made homage for the castle d’Andouis and for his other fiefs, t
2 CONC o Gauthier d’Aunay, Sénéchal de Forcalquier, for Charles, King of Sici
2 CONC ly and Count of Provence. He was still living on the 18th of March, 12
2 CONC 97, when his souverain adressed to his Sénéchal de Provence some lette
2 CONC rs patent according to which Elzéar de Sabran, Chevalier, was given pe
2 CONC rmission not to pay 500 ducats a year to his creditors.
2 CONT
2 CONT [C-D, XVIII, 11]. With his eldest son, Ermengaud, he followed Charles
2 CONC I d’Anjou to the conquest of Naples, and, returning to Provence, he so
2 CONC ld, on 29 June 1280, an eighth part of the Seigneurie d’Uzès to the Bi
2 CONC shop of that town.
2 CONT
2 CONT [ES, XIV, 183]
