1 NOTE [DHSP, 152]: Dit de Malotortello, a corruption of Martorel. Seigneur d
2 CONC ’Uzès en partie (pour un huitième), d’Ansouis & de Cucuron, au Comtat-
2 CONC Venaissin. In April 1207, by a contract made at Saint-Paul-lès-Conneau
2 CONC x, he sold to the chartreuse de Valbonne, for 300 sols, the enclosure
2 CONC de Cabraceriis, dit Sabranencs, situated in the parish of Saint-Clémen
2 CONC t de Seleraco.  He had to get the approval of his mother, without ment
2 CONC ion of his father, who was still alive at that time.  He was among the
2 CONC  witnesses at the arbitration sentence of the 29 June, 1220, on the su
2 CONC bject of  the Count of Forcalquier, under the name Guillaume de Maltor
2 CONC tel, Dauphinois (...Guillelmo de Malotortello, Dalfineto), and the sam
2 CONC e in the act of homage of Guillaume de Sabran, Comte de Forcalquier, t
2 CONC o the Comte de Provence, on the 26 January, 1228. He was present there
2 CONC  in the capacity of one of the two Judges instituted by the souverain
2 CONC for the Count of Forcalquier (Rostaing de Sabran, Bishop of Riez, was
2 CONC the other Judge). On the 20 May 1237, Raimond, Count of Toulouse, in a
2 CONC  war with the Count of Provence, gave la bastide de Montalvagne to Gui
2 CONC llaume de Sabran and his children, by a contract done at Avignon in th
2 CONC e presence of the Count of Forcalquier, and of Rostaing d’Agoult, Chan
2 CONC oine de Marseille, and of Giraud IV Amic de Sabran “Dauphinois”. .....
2 CONC .. In May 1251 he rendered homage to Alphonse, Count of Poitiers & of
2 CONC Toulouse, Marquis de Provence, for the castle Montalvagne.
2 CONT
2 CONT [C-D, XVIII, 11]. Contributed to the agreement made on 21 March 1247 b
2 CONC etween Guillaume Dalmas, Bishop of Apt and Bertrand-Rambaud de Simiane
2 CONC , Seigneur de St. Martin.
2 CONT
2 CONT [ES, XIV, 183].
