1 NOTE [C-D, IX, 330] writes: One finds (so says the author of  The Heroic Hi
2 CONC story of the Noblesse de Provence, I, 492) in the charters of the chur
2 CONC ch of Apt, that there were Counts of Glandevès in Provence in the X an
2 CONC d XI centuries. The Abbé Robert, in addition, says that they were the
2 CONC original ancestors. He is wrong. The name of Féraud [something about t
2 CONC he marriage of the last inheritor of the family of Féraud], was the or
2 CONC iginal patrynomic, and the author shows here, in the Genealogy followi
2 CONC ng, that the name Glandevès only came into the family after the marria
2 CONC ge of Anselme.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arms from [C-D, IX, 337]. Fascé d’or & de gueules de 6 pièces.
