1 NOTE [DHSP, 136]. Seigneur du Thor de Chateauneuf de Robion et de Jonquière
2 CONC s, co-Seigneur de Caumont.
2 CONT The second son of Guiraud II-Amic de Sabran, the constable of Toulouse
2 CONC  (but only temporarily, as I write a bit about above). He appears on a
2 CONC  number of contracts, sometimes as Geraudetus Amici, the first on the
2 CONC 20 May 1202. He was among the witnesses at the marriage contract (June
2 CONC , 1202) of his cousin Béatrix de Sabran with André de Bourgogne, Dauph
2 CONC in de Viennois. In December 1209, he assisted his brother, the Count o
2 CONC f Forcalquier, in the act of affiliation with the Order of the Templar
2 CONC s. On 14 July, 1210, he was a witness in a treaty between Guillaume I
2 CONC de Baux, Prince d’Orange, and Raimond VI, Count of Toulouse. And so it
2 CONC  goes.
