1 NOTE [DHSP, 123]. Seigneur de Chateauneuf du Thor et de Jonquières, co-Seig
2 CONC neur de Caumont.  He was present at some treaty concluded in 1195 betw
2 CONC een Guillaume, Comte de Forcalquier, & Raimond VI, Comte de Toulouse,
2 CONC but the details were too difficult to translate. Obviously there was s
2 CONC ome big bust-up. In 1202 and 1204 he was one of the four judges, with
2 CONC his cousin germain, Rostaing de Sabran, the Constable, to end the figh
2 CONC ting between the Comte de Forcalquier and several other Seigneurs. Aft
2 CONC er the death of his cousin germain, Rostaing de Sabran, who left no ch
2 CONC ildren of age, the dignity of Constable devolved on him temporarily, a
2 CONC nd it was in this capacity that he assisted, on the 16 February, 1208,
2 CONC  with the act of remission accorded by the Count of Toulouse to the in
2 CONC subordinate inhabitants of Nîmes, an act that was performed in the chu
2 CONC rch so St.-Sauveur de Caissargues, where he was called Guiraldus Amici
2 CONC . He died the same year.
2 CONT [ES XIV:179]
