1 NOTE [DHSP, 17]. Sire de Sault co-Seigneur d'Agoult, d'Apt, de Roussillon,
2 CONC de Murs, d’Entrevennes, de Lioux, de Simiane, du Revest &c. First docu
2 CONC mentary appearance in 1172, in the plenary court held at the castle of
2 CONC  Beaucaire, where he was part of a group who tried to negotiate a peac
2 CONC e between the Count of Toulouse and the King of Aragon. Finally, at th
2 CONC e conclusion of the peace treaty, in the island of Argence, 18 April 1
2 CONC 176, Raymond, Count of Toulouse ceded all his rights in Provence and G
2 CONC évaudan to Alphonse, King of Aragon. This treaty was renewed in Februa
2 CONC ry, 1185. In 1176 he was named, by the Count of Provence, as Governor
2 CONC and Count of Nice, and received, on the 6 August 1178, from the Empero
2 CONC r Frederic Barbarossa, the investiture of the valley of Sault and of a
2 CONC ll his possessions in the diocese (Diois).
2 CONT [FM,616,619]
2 CONT [ES, XIV, 10].
