1 NOTE [RW], quoting [ES, III, 764]. Comte de Toulouse, Duc de Narbonne. Marr
2 CONC iage repudiated 1193.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ermessende was Raymond VI's first wife. Beatrix was Raymond VI's secon
2 CONC d wife. Married in 1193 France: Bourgogne de Lusignan; Bourgogne was R
2 CONC aymond VI's third wife. Repudiated Beatrix de Beziers in 1193. Between
2 CONC  1195 and 1218: Raimond VI was the Count of Toulouse, Languedoc, Franc
2 CONC e from 1195. After his defeat at the Battle of Muret, he was stripped
2 CONC of his estates by Simon de Montfort. They fought again in 1216, and Ra
2 CONC ymond de Toulouse defended the city against Simon de Montfort in 1218.
2 CONC  Repudiated Bourgogne de Lusignan in 1196. Married in Oct 1196 Joanna,
2 CONC  Princess of England, daughter of Henry II, King of England and Eleono
2 CONC re, Duchess d'Aquitaine; Joanna was Raymond VI's fourth wife. Married
2 CONC in 1200: N? Komnene, daughter of Isaac Dukas Komnenos and N?, Princess
2 CONC  de Sicile; She was Raymond VI's fifth wife. Divorced N? Komnene: in 1
2 CONC 202. Married in Jan 1203: Leonor de Aragon, daughter of Alfonso II, Ki
2 CONC ng de Aragon and Sancha, Princess de Castile; Leonor was Raymond VI's
2 CONC sixth wife. Died: 2 Aug 1222 France at age 65. Upon the death of Raymo
2 CONC nd VI, his young son, Raymond VII would take up the banner of the Albi
2 CONC gensians and fight energetically against the French.
