1 NOTE [ES II:46]. Comte de Blois, Chartres, Chateaudun, Sancerre et Meaux. T
2 CONC heir son was King Stephen of England. He played a major role in the fi
2 CONC rst crusade and died during the siege of Ramulah. Hallam (amusingly) n
2 CONC otes: “Stephen Henry, Count of Blois and Meaux, appears, like his poss
2 CONC essions, to have  been governed by his wife, Adela, daughter of Willia
2 CONC m the Conqueror. When he went on crusade in 1096 she was officially ma
2 CONC de his regent, and although he returned from the east with extreme rap
2 CONC idity she soon sent him back again. He died in Outremer in 1102.”
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT From: "William A. Reitwiesner" < wrei@LOC.GOV >
2 CONT Subject: Re: HELP: Who was Stephen Henry of Blois?
2 CONT Date: Fri, 3 Nov 1995 14:41:29 EDT
2 CONT elcontob@telepost.no (Tom Bjornstad) posted:
2 CONT
2 CONT >According to my knowledge Stephen Henry of Blois was married to Adele
2 CONC  of Blois
2 CONT >(ca. 1062 - Mar 8th 1138), the daughter of William the Conqueror and
2 CONC his wife
2 CONT >Matilda.
2 CONT >
2 CONT >Stephen Henry and Adele had to my knowledge 3 children, Stephen I (ca
2 CONC .
2 CONT 1096-Oct
2 CONT >25th 1154) King of England, Matilda (?-1120) and William (?-?).  What
2 CONC  I don't
2 CONT >know anything about is the parents of Stephen Henry and I also would
2 CONC most
2 CONT >gracefully appreciate any information of Stephen I's brother and sist
2 CONC er.
2 CONT
2 CONT Stephen Henry (or Etienne Henri), Count of Blois (1046-1102), was the
2 CONC only
2 CONT child of Thibaut III, Count of Blois (-1089) by his second wife Gundra
2 CONC da.
2 CONT Thibaut III's ancestry can be traced back a ways (his great-grandmothe
2 CONC r was
2 CONT a Carolingian Vermandois), but Gundrada's origin is unknown.  Thibaut
2 CONC III
2 CONT had other children by his third wife and none by his first wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT Of King Stephen's siblings, Matilda married Richard d'Avranches, Earl
2 CONC of
2 CONT Chester; Lithuaise married (and was divorced from) Milon II de Monthle
2 CONC ry,
2 CONT Vicomte de Troyes; Henry was Bishop of Winchester; Thibaut IV succeede
2 CONC d his
2 CONT father as Count of Blois (and was ancestor of the later Counts of Cham
2 CONC pagne
2 CONT and Kings of Navarre); William (see below); and Eudes.  All of this is
2 CONT from *Europaeische Stammtafeln*, edited by Detlev Schwennicke, Band II
2 CONC ,
2 CONT Tafel 46.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT William Addams Reitwiesner wrei@loc.gov
2 CONT ------------------------------------------
