1 NOTE [DHSP, 113]:
2 CONT “Émenon III de Sabran, who participated, with his brother (Guillaume)
2 CONC in the acts of violence perpetrated by Bertrand, Count of Toulouse, ag
2 CONC ainst the abbey of Saint Gilles, and was excommunicated in 1107. After
2 CONC  having been relieved (?. Forgiven? Reinstated?) he seems to have kept
2 CONC  away from later conflicts between the two parties. In 1125, he affixe
2 CONC d his seal (S. Emenonis de Sabra) immediately after that of Alphonse-J
2 CONC ourdain, Count of Toulouse, at the bottom of an act of engagement made
2 CONC  by Gauzbert de Fumel, Abbé séculier de Moissac, with regard to that m
2 CONC onastery. Finally, in 1138, with Rostaing, his other brother, he was a
2 CONC t the head of the witnesses in an act of donation to the Count of Toul
2 CONC ouse.”
