1 NOTE [FM, 648]
2 CONT [DHSP, 114]:
2 CONT “Pierre de Sabran, qui était auprès de Bernard-Aton, Vicomte of Bezier
2 CONC s. [Not sure how to translate this.] On the 9th of January, 1116, he a
2 CONC ffixed his seal on an act of donation made by that prince [i.e., by th
2 CONC e Vicomte], and also on the Vicomte’s will, made at Carcassonne on the
2 CONC  7th of May, 1118. It’s likely that he was in Holy Orders, and is the
2 CONC same Pierre de Sabran who appears, in the position of Doyen [Senior?]
2 CONC (Petrus de Sabrano, Decanus) in a charter of donation made by the Coun
2 CONC t of Toulouse to the Abbey of Saint Andre of Avignon, in 1133. This sa
2 CONC me Pierre Sabran, with the title of Prior of Todone, was a witness for
2 CONC  two other donations made by the same Prince to the same Abbey, in1140
2 CONC  and 1142. Elected, in 1143, Bishop of Sisteron, he appears beside Gui
2 CONC llaume de Sabran, the Constable [i.e., Pierre’s nephew] in an act of 1
2 CONC 157, giving a concession to the Order of Saint Jean for a chapel at Sa
2 CONC int Gilles, and, in 1168, on an act of accession to that Order by Guil
2 CONC laume and Bertrand, brothers, Counts of Forcalquier. He made a pilgrim
2 CONC age to Jerusalem, and died at Forcalquier on the 7th of December, 1171
2 CONC .”
