1 NOTE [DHSP, 146].  From what I can glean from D’Hozier, when Garsinde de Sa
2 CONC bran married Alphonse II, Comte de Provence (son of Alphonse I, Comte
2 CONC de Provence et Roi d’Aragon), the Forcalquier title reverted to Alix a
2 CONC nd thence to Guillaume Sabran, the son of Alix. Her son was Raymond-Be
2 CONC renger, Comte de Provence & de Forcalquier (how could he also be the c
2 CONC omte de Forcalquier? I’m confused). One of his daughters, Marguerite d
2 CONC e Provence married Saint Louis, Roi de France, in 1234, another daught
2 CONC er, Éléonore de Provence married Henry III of England.
2 CONT
2 CONT [C-D, XVIII, 10] mentions some of her progeny. Her son Raimond-Berenge
2 CONC r, Count of Provence, married Beatrix de Savoie, and his daughter Marg
2 CONC uerite married Saint Louis, King of France. Etc.
2 CONT [C-D, VIII, 358].
