1 NOTE [FM,616]. Gives the same children as [DHSP] does. A bloody miracle!
2 CONT [DHSP, 11]. The first to have taken the name D’Agoult. Co-Seigneur d’A
2 CONC pt, Baron de Caseneuve, Seigneur d’Agoult, de Castillon, de Gordes, de
2 CONC  Barret, de Tourrettes, de Nice, &c &c. Church donations listed by D’H
2 CONC ozier, the first in 1048. He was first married to Constance, supposedl
2 CONC y from the family of the Vicomtes de Marseille, but later (between 103
2 CONC 5 and 1044) married Gisla, or Gilla. With Gisla he had more than six s
2 CONC ons and several daughters.
2 CONT [C-D, XVIII, 596]. Qualified as Prince of Apt in the titles concerning
2 CONC  his brother Alfan, Bishop of Apt. He contributed, with his brother Gu
2 CONC illaume, to repairs to the church of that town, by an act of 27 June 1
2 CONC 056, in which he was referred to as Prince.
2 CONT [ES, XIV, 9].
