1 NOTE [FM,616]
2 CONT [DHSP, 10]. Baron de Caseneuve, premier Seigneur d’Agoult, Seigneur de
2 CONC  Simiane &c. D’Hozier lists the church donations. In a charter of dona
2 CONC tion, of 1018, made by the Comtesse of Provence (widow of Guillaume II
2 CONC ) to the abbey of Saint-Victor de Marseille, he appears immediately af
2 CONC ter the sovereign, and even before the sons of the Comtesse, which sho
2 CONC ws clearly his high status at court. The  castle and territory of Agou
2 CONC lt (which became their family name) appears first on 30 Nov 1031 or 10
2 CONC 32, in another church donation.
2 CONT [C-D, XVIII, 596]. Seigneur d’Agoult & de Caseneuve. Took the surname
2 CONC d’Agoult. He confirmed, with his mother, the gift that his father made
2 CONC  to the church of Apt in 1008. He gave, with his wife Alix, or Adelaid
2 CONC e, to the Abbey of St. Victor of Marseille, several churces situated i
2 CONC n the territory of Cavaillon, in January 1009.
2 CONT [ES, XIV, 9].
