2 CONT [DHSP, 15]. Took the name and arms of Simiane, although his descendant
2 CONC s kept the name d’Agoult for four generations. His descendants formed
2 CONC numerous branches in Dauphiné, Piémont, and the Countship of Venaissin
2 CONC . They produced three Chevaliers des Ordres du Roi, and many other emi
2 CONC nent personages. Extinct at the beginning of the XIX century. I bet th
2 CONC ey were as pompous as D’Hozier himself. D’Hozier quotes Anselm for the
2 CONC  rest of the descent.
2 CONT [C-D, XVIII, 597]. He was named before his brothers in the titles of h
2 CONC is uncle, Laugier, Bishop of Apt, in 1113 and 1120.
2 CONT [ES, XIV, 9] gives no wives or children of Guiran.
