1 NOTE [C-D, XVI, 128] gives only Barral as descendant.
2 CONT [DHSP, 25]. Principal heir of Douceline de Pontevès and took the arms
2 CONC and name of Pontevès. On 13 Feb 1244 he came to an agreement with his
2 CONC two brothers for his share of the paternal inheritance (Bernard Girard
2 CONC , in Rians, was the notary). He was Seigneur of Pontevès, Montmeyan, E
2 CONC sparron, Artignosc, Bargème, Callas, Brovès, Tavernes, Lussan, Sillans
2 CONC , Barjols, Beauvezet, la Bastide-de-Bersille, Comps, Auriac, Blioux, &
2 CONC c, by virtue of this inheritance.
2 CONT Following Meynir, Histoire de la Noblesse de Provence, he took part in
2 CONC  the seventh crusade, was present at the taking of Damiette with King
2 CONC Saint Louis in 1249, and at the battle of Massoure in 1250. On 22 Nov
2 CONC 1251, he and his brother Isnard stood as security for Barral de Baux,
2 CONC against the Count of Provence. His signature appears at the bottom of
2 CONC this act. Buried in the church of Barjols.
2 CONT
2 CONT [DHSP] gives him two wives, Mathilde de Rheza, and Felipe des Porcelle
2 CONC ts, neither of which agree with [FM]. I shall follow [FM].
2 CONT [FM,619,623] calls him Fouque I de Pontevès and lists 8 children, incl
2 CONC uding Maragda, Isoarda, Béatrix, Mabilia, Barral and Guillem.
