2 CONC Requêtes de l’Hôtel, by provision of the King, given at Millau, 10 May
2 CONC  1437, for which he took oath [?] between the hands of the Bishop of M
2 CONC aguelonne (now Montpellier), the 16th of the same month. He rendered h
2 CONC omage, on the 10th of July, 1462, for the lands of Saint-Veran, to Jea
2 CONC n, Comte d’Armagnac, Vicomte de Creissels. Later, having been accused
2 CONC of taking the part of the Comte d’Armagnac, he was imprisoned and take
2 CONC n to Tours, with Guillaume and Gaillard de Montcalm, two of his childr
2 CONC en, and all his possessions, including those of his eldest son, were c
2 CONC onfiscated. But Louis XI, better informed, recognised his innocence an
2 CONC d restored his possessions by Letters Patent given at Montils on the 2
