1 NOTE [C-D, XIV, 136]. Petite-niece of Dieudonné de Gozon, Grand Master of R
2 CONC hodes, known for the death of the dragon from which he delivered that
2 CONC island [?. Now this is weird. A dragon?!]
2 CONT [C-D, IX, 626] gives a list of Gozons, but later than Jeanne and her d
2 CONC addy. Most likely starts with her brother, or other close relative, bu
2 CONC t C-D doesn’t say. All he says is that they were from Rouergue, and an
2 CONC  ancient noble family, taking their name from the lands of Gozon in th
2 CONC e same province. Surprised he didn’t say they were excessively disting
2 CONC uished also, just like everybody else seems to be.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arms according to [C-D, IX, 628]:  de gueules, à la bande d’azur, bord
2 CONC ée d’argent; à la bordure componée d’argent & de gueules. Compare this
2 CONC  to the Gozon arms listed as part of the Montcalm arms: de gueules, à
2 CONC la bande d’azur, bordée d’argent, & une bordure componée de billettes
2 CONC d’argent, qui est DE GOZON. Pretty good agreement, really.
