1 NOTE [C-D, XIV, 135]. Seigneur du Viala, de Cornus, de Saint-Veran. Rendere
2 CONC d homage on the 7th of September, 1428, to Jean d’Armagnac, Vicomte de
2 CONC  Creissels, for the lands of Saint-Veran. On 4th February, 1441, he bo
2 CONC ught from Bertrand de Vissec, some dependencies of Saint-Veran.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to [PL], Raymond was the doctor to Comte d’Armagnac and was
2 CONC ennobled in 1439. As seems to have been very common (for instance, the
2 CONC  Boileau family did the same thing, as did the de Pierre family), it’s
2 CONC  almost certain that the traditional ancestry of the family was fabric
2 CONC ated to hide their non-noble origins. Judging by the information in [C
2 CONC -D] it seems almost certain that Raymond purchased his lands and title
2 CONC , and that his forebears were not ennobled.
