1 NOTE [C-D, IV, 597]. Antoine and Raymond de Calvière were brothers, Chevali
2 CONC ers, residing at Montfrin, in the Diocese of Uzès, on the 4th of Augus
2 CONC t, 1508. They bought their lands in the Seigneurie of Montfrin from br
2 CONC other Charles-Alleman de Roche-Chinard, Grand Prior of Saint-Gilles, b
2 CONC y a contract dated 10 May 1510. It’s not known if Antoine was married.
2 CONC  [It appears he was, according to .]
2 CONT
2 CONT Arms according to [C-D, IV, 607]: D’or, à trois fasces de sable, charg
2 CONC ées chacune de deux besans d’argent; au chef de même chargé d’un sangl
2 CONC ier passant de sable. Mémoire envoyé.  It’s not clear which of the fam
2 CONC ily used these arms, or whether all branches did. I’ll just use them f
2 CONC or the lot.
