1 NOTE [C-D, XIV, 812]. [ES,III:444]
2 CONT I need to read Archibald R. Lewis' "The Guillems of Montpellier: A Soc
2 CONC iological Appraisal",_Viator_ 2 (1971), but haven’t done so yet.
2 CONT
2 CONT [CD, XIV, 445] says that the Montpelliers were an ancient family of Ba
2 CONC s-Languedoc, based in the ancient town of Maguelonne, ruined by the Sa
2 CONC racens. The Montpellier heiress, named Beatrix [Guillemette’s daughter
2 CONC ] took the two large fiefs with her when she married Bernard Pelet, an
2 CONC d their posterity was the family of Narbonne-Pelet. The first Seigneur
2 CONC  of Montpellier was Guy, or Guillaume, one of the Knights of the Count
2 CONC  of Melguel. At the end of the 10th century he obtained the town of Mo
2 CONC ntpellier as a fief from the Count and the Bishop. His descendants all
2 CONC  took the name Guillaume.
2 CONT
2 CONT I have a version of the Montpellier ancestry [MP] which seems reliable
2 CONC  from the times I have checked it against [ES], so I shall follow it h
2 CONC ere.
