1 NOTE [C-D, XIV, 812]. This entry is a bit of a puzzle. C-D says that she ma
2 CONC rried, firstly, Pierre Bermond, Seigneur de Sauve, and secondly (in 11
2 CONC 73) Raymond VII, Count of Toulouse, oldest son of Raymond VI, Count of
2 CONC  Toulouse, and Constance of France, daughter of Louis VI the Fat, King
2 CONC  of France.
2 CONT The second husband creates problems. According to [RW], quoting [ES, I
2 CONC II, 764], Constance of France was married to Raymond V of Toulouse, NO
2 CONC T Raymond VI, but was divorced in 1165. All other sources I’ve seen, i
2 CONC ncluding Hallam agree that it was Raymond V who married Constance. So
2 CONC it seems pretty certain that C-D means Raymond VI and V respectively.
2 CONC That’s what I’ve run with here.
2 CONT
2 CONT [CD, XII, 739] gives the exact marriage date, and actually says she ma
2 CONC rried Raymond VI (so CD himself wasn’t consistent with the numbering).
