1 NOTE [C-D, XIV, 812]. Called le Croisé. He went, in 1096, to the Holy Land.
2 CONC  According to l’Hist. génér. du Languedoc, II, 310, he commanded the e
2 CONC leventh of twelve Corps in the army at the battle of Antioch. He took
2 CONC Tortose, in Phoenicia, with the troops that he had assembled from his
2 CONC dependants. On his return from the Hoy Land he became Seigneur of Alai
2 CONC s, in Languedoc, which he got by marriage. He gave, in 1131, to the Co
2 CONC mmander of Gap-Francs a Mas de Sal [?], and, together with his wife, A
2 CONC gnès, gave, in March 1140, a gift to Albert, Commander of the Hospital
2 CONC  of Saint-Jean of Jerusalem.
2 CONT
2 CONT [ES, XIV, 147]. The first of the Pelet lot in [ES], and called Bermond
2 CONC , to boot. Doesn’t inspire me with confidence in the earlier ones give
2 CONC n in C-D.
