1 NOTE [C-D, XIV, 806-807] gives a short blurb about the counts, vicounts, et
2 CONC c, of Narbonne. An ancient and flourishing family since before the fir
2 CONC st Roman conquests in Gaul. Yeah. Right. We believe you. He quotes le
2 CONC Diction. des Gaules, book V. He also quotes Catel in the Mémoires sur
2 CONC l’Hist. du Languedoc, p. 565.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to C-D, the first member of the family of the Viscounts of N
2 CONC arbonne was Guillaume, surnamed au Court-Nez, Constable of France, who
2 CONC  distinguished himself by his valour in chasing the Saracens of the to
2 CONC wns of Orange, Nimes, and the whole country of Languedoc. He founded a
2 CONC  Monastery in the Diocese of Lodève, of the Order of Saint-Benoit, tod
2 CONC ay called Saint Guillaume. He left several children, among others: Aim
2 CONC eri, the first Vicomte de Narbonne, from whom descends Mayeul.
2 CONT
2 CONT For the genealogy of Mayeul, C-D quotes Catel, l’Hist. des Grands Offi
2 CONC ciers de la Couronne.
2 CONT
2 CONT Arms of ancient Narbonne according to [C-D, XIV, 833]: de gueules plei
2 CONC n. Now that is the simplest blazon I’ve ever seen. Neato.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------------------
2 CONT From: Nat Taylor < ntaylor@FAS.HARVARD.EDU >
2 CONT Subject: Sancha: viscounts of Narbonne
2 CONT Date: Fri, 13 Oct 1995 05:23:03 GMT
2 CONT
2 CONT There is no good recent scholarly study of the viscounts of Narbonne,
2 CONC but
2 CONT there are a couple of basic starting places.  Europaische Stammtafeln
2 CONT doesn't have them.
2 CONT
2 CONT A graphic pedigree can be found in the _Gran enciclopedia catalana_ (1
2 CONC 7
2 CONT vols. Barcelona: Fundacio Enciclopedia Catalana, 1970-1986), s.v.
2 CONT "Narbona".  This is one of several tabular pedigrees compiled for this
2 CONT encyclopedia by Armand de Fluvia, a prominent Barcelona genealogist an
2 CONC d
2 CONT herald.
2 CONT
2 CONT The previous best discussion of the family is in Claude Devic & Jean
2 CONT Vaissete's _Histoire generale de Languedoc_ (3d, revised ed.; ed. Moli
2 CONC nier
2 CONT et al., 16 vols., Toulouse: Privat, 1872-1904), in vols. 2 and 4.
2 CONT
2 CONT More recent discussions of the interrelated comital and vicecomital
2 CONT families in this area treat the viscounts of Narbonne as they are
2 CONT intermarried with the comital families of Toulouse, Barcelona and othe
2 CONC rs:
2 CONT
2 CONT Szabolcs de Vajay, "Comtesses d'origine occitane dans la Marche d'Espa
2 CONC gne
2 CONT aux 10e et 11e siecles: essai sur le rattachement de Richilde, de Gars
2 CONC ende
2 CONT et de Letgardis, comtesses de Barcelone, et de Thietberge, comtesse
2 CONT d'Urgel, au contexte genealogique occitan," _Hidalguia_ 28 (1980),
2 CONT 585-616, 755-788.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marti Aurell i Cardona (in French form, Martin Aurell) "Jalons pour un
2 CONC e
2 CONT enquete sur les strategies matrimoniales des comtes catalans (IXe - XI
2 CONC e
2 CONT s.)," in _Symposium internacional sobre els origens de Catalunya (segl
2 CONC es
2 CONT VIII-XI)_ (2 vols., Barcelona: Commissio del Mil.lenari de Catalunya:
2 CONT Generalitat de Catalunya, 1991). Vol. i, pp. 281-364.  His recent book
2 CONC ,
2 CONT _Les noces du comte: mariage et pouvoir en Catalogne, 785-1213_ (Paris
2 CONC :
2 CONT Sorbonne, 1995) expands on his historical interpretations but the
2 CONT biographical register of noble women in his article is not published i
2 CONC n
2 CONT the book.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note that these two articles by Marti Aurell and Szabolcs de Vajay oft
2 CONC en
2 CONT disagree.  Other works with varying interpretations of links between
2 CONT Narbonne, Toulouse and Barcelona are:
2 CONT
2 CONT Maria-Merce Costa, "Les genealogies comtals catalanes," also in _Sympo
2 CONC sium
2 CONT internacional sobre els origens de Catalunya (segles VIII-XI)_, i:447-
2 CONC 462,
2 CONT and
2 CONT
2 CONT Helene Debax, "Strategies matrimoniales des comtesses de Toulouse
2 CONT (850-1270); Notices biographiques," _Annales du Midi_ 100 (1988), 131-
2 CONC 152,
2 CONT 215-234.
2 CONT
2 CONT Aurell's work (and Debax's) is very rigorously based on citations to
2 CONT original documentary evidence; often Vajay reflects a consensus which
2 CONC is
2 CONT generally held but is without evidentiary foundation.  Costa and Vajay
2 CONT offer conflicting onomastic hypotheses for identities in a couple of
2 CONT cases.  Fluvia usually follows Vajay, and has also sometimes turned
2 CONT conjectural identifications into facts in his charts.
2 CONT
2 CONT The most comprehensive historical treatment focusing on Narbonne is
2 CONT Elisabeth Magnou-Nortier's _La Societe laique et l'Eglise dans la prov
2 CONC ince
2 CONT ecclesiastique de Narbonne (zone cispyreneenne) de la fin du VIIIe a l
2 CONC a
2 CONT fin du XIe siecle_ (Toulouse: Pubs. Toulouse-le Mirail, 1974).  She
2 CONT discusses the earlier generations well.
2 CONT
2 CONT Here is the lineage of the viscounts, from the first known member of t
2 CONC he
2 CONT dynasty down to the Mayor Manrique de Lara, wife of Comez Gonzales de
2 CONT Manzanedo.  Mayor Manrique is shown with a question mark in the Fluvia
2 CONT pedigree of the viscounts of Narbonne.  I do not know of the sources f
2 CONC or
2 CONT this identity, which is given in Garcia Carraffa.  Of course, if her
2 CONT identity is incorrect (and if the Manzanedo-Guzman marriage is incorre
2 CONC ct)
2 CONT then these birds fly chirping away.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sancha has another shot at part of this ancestry (including most of th
2 CONC e
2 CONT Catalan counts, but not the Carolingian Italian ancestry behind Maud o
2 CONC f
2 CONT Apulia-Calabria) if a descent from count Armengol V of Urgell can be
2 CONT squeezed in somewhere.
2 CONT
2 CONT Franco I, + bef. 852, vc Narbonne.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maieul, + 878/911, vc Narbonne; m. Raimonda.
2 CONT
2 CONT Franco II, + 924, vc Narbonne; m. Arsenda (identified as dau. Sunyer I
2 CONC I,
2 CONT count of Ampurias/Roussillon by Fluvia (also appears in (excuse me for
2 CONT mentioning him) Stuart, line 218, ref'ing Moriarty), but not supported
2 CONC  by
2 CONT Aurell or even ES)).
2 CONT
2 CONT Odo, + 933, vc Narbonne; m. Riquilda, daughter of Guifred Borrell, cou
2 CONC nt
2 CONT of Barcelona (see ES II:68.  The identity of Guifred Borrell's wife,
2 CONT Garsenda, is an open question with at least 3 suggestions in print).
2 CONT
2 CONT Matfred I, + 966/969, vc Narbonne; m. Adalais, + 990 (I'm not convince
2 CONC d
2 CONT that Matfred is the son of the above.  It is possible that instead Ada
2 CONC lais
2 CONT was their daughter.  She acted as viscountess after Matfred's death an
2 CONC d
2 CONT willed the viscounty outright to their son in a written testament.  Th
2 CONC is
2 CONT suggests to me that it was hers by right, not his).
2 CONT
2 CONT Raimond I, + 1018/1023, vc Narbonne; m. Ricarda of Rodez (as given by
2 CONT Fluvia--I'll have to dig further for her identity).
2 CONT
2 CONT Berenguer I, + 1067, vc Narbonne; m. Garsenda, daughter of Bernat
2 CONT Taliafero, count of Besalu (ES III:137; note that the identity of Bern
2 CONC at's
2 CONT wife Tota, Garsenda's mother, is questioned by Marti Aurell).
2 CONT
2 CONT Bernard I, + 1077/1080, vc Narbonne; m. Fides, dau. Hugh count of Roue
2 CONC rgue
2 CONT by Fides, dau. Guifred of Cerdanya, brother of Bernat Taliafero above
2 CONC (ES
2 CONT III:763; III:137).  Note that the earlier genealogy of the counts of
2 CONT Rouergue, and their relation to the counts of Toulouse, is felt to be
2 CONC very
2 CONT unclear by Debax and others.  These counts of Besalu and Cerdanya are
2 CONT clearly known, but their wives are mostly unidentified.
2 CONT
2 CONT Amalric I, + c. 1106, vc Narbonne; m. Maud of Apulia-Calabria (dau. of
2 CONT Robert Guiscard and Sikelgaita of Salerno and widow of Ramon Berenguer
2 CONC  II
2 CONT of Barcelona, see ES II:205 and Charles Evans in TAG 52 (1976).
2 CONT
2 CONT Amalric II, + 1134, vc Narbonne, lord of Peyrepertuse and Fenouillet;
2 CONC m.
2 CONT Ermessend (2d wife, unidentified).
2 CONT
2 CONT Amalric's surviving children were Ermengard (child of his first wife,
2 CONT Ermengard of Carcassonne), who was viscountess until her death in 1194
2 CONC ,
2 CONT and Ermessend (child of second wife, Ermessend), who married the Casti
2 CONC lian
2 CONT Manrique de Lara, lord of Molina y Mesa.  In her will, viscountess
2 CONT Ermengard left Narbonne to her nephew Pedro Manrique, who became the f
2 CONC irst
2 CONT of this Castilian family to have the title viscount of Narbonne.
2 CONT Putatively Mayor Manrique, wife of Gomez Gonzales de Manzanedo, was hi
2 CONC s
2 CONT sister.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nat Taylor
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------
