2 CONT [C-D, XIV, 813]. Co-Sgr. d’Alais , Seigneur de Boucoiran, de Lascours
2 CONC &c. He succeeded his elder brother, and, being a minor of 25 years [?!
2 CONC ], he paid homage on 3 February 1240, to Pons, Bishop of Uzès, for Rou
2 CONC sson, le Mandement & le Château de Peyremale. He had an argument with
2 CONC the Abbey of Cendras about the jurisdiction of that valley, which was
2 CONC ended by arbitration on 12 November 1246. He made his will on 1 Sept 1
2 CONC 252, wrote a codicil on the 5th of Sept, and died a few days afterward
2 CONC s. In his will he named Tiburge, his mother, who was still living, and
2 CONC  all his children, for whom he named as tutors, Bernard de Barres, Ber
2 CONC nard de Soucanton, Guillaume de Pontis & Jean Boffolas, with express o
2 CONC rders to do nothing without the advice of the Bishop of Uzès and of Be
2 CONC rnard do Soucanton, Abbot of Cendras.
