1 NOTE [C-D, IV, 204].
2 CONT [C-D, XVII, 297].  Seigneur de Mortemart, de St.-Germain, de Cercigné
2 CONC &c, Councillor and Chamberlain to the King. Knighted by the Prince de
2 CONC Galles, during a voyage to Spain where he went in service to the King;
2 CONC  he helped fight the English in Poitou and Guyenne, and was the Senesc
2 CONC hal of Limousin on 21 November 1384. Paid homage to the Duc de Berry,
2 CONC Comte de Poitiers, on 17 August 1386; made Captain-General of Poitou a
2 CONC nd Saintonge by letters of 19 December 1392.
2 CONT [ES, III, 786]
