1 NOTE [BBB]: Educ at Dulwich College and RMC Sandhurst.   Commissioned to Ro
2 CONC yal Corps of Signals : 2 Lt, 27 Aug 1924.  After service at Maresfield
2 CONC  and Catterick, went to India and served mostly on the NW Frontier, wh
2 CONC ere he took part in operations in 1930-31.   ADC to the GOC-in-C, West
2 CONC ern Command, India, Jun 1931-June 1932.  Chitral relief Force, 1932;
2 CONC Mohmand - Bajaur Expedition 1933.   IGSM with two clasps.    On return
2 CONC  to UK, appt Adjt, School of Signals at Catterick, Oct 1934 to Sep 193
2 CONC 7.   Promoted Captain Aug 1935.  Comd Apprentice Boys Training Company
2 CONC , 1937-39.
2 CONT
2 CONT War of 1939-45 : BEF France, from Dec 1939 Adjt HQ Signals, GHQ and to
2 CONC ok part in the campaign of 1940, 10-31 May, being evacuated through Du
2 CONC nkirk.  Mentioned in despcthes: "Owing to the frequent moves of HQ and
2 CONC  with many scattered signal offices and detachments to control, the Ad
2 CONC jt's task was arduous, and during operations necessitated long periods
2 CONC  without sleep; but his excellent organisation made the most efficient
2 CONC  use of the available communications, and ensured the evacuation of th
2 CONC e unit"
2 CONT
2 CONT He became Senior Instructor, School of Signals, July 1940, with the ra
2 CONC nk of Major (subs Aug 1941), and Comd Div Signals, 9th Armoured Div, w
2 CONC ith rank of Lt Col, May 1941.   Chief Military Signal Officer, with ra
2 CONC nk of Col on the Staff of Admiral Lord Louis Mountbatten, Supreme Alli
2 CONC ed Commander, SE Asia Command, Dec 1943, serving in Delhi and Ceylon,
2 CONC until the end of the war against Japan in 1945.  OBE, 1946;  1939-45 S
2 CONC tar, Defence and War Medals.
2 CONT Then to 13 Corps as Chief Signal Officer, and later CO Signals, 1st Ar
2 CONC moured Div Signals, Trieste.   OC Western Comd Signal regt, Chester, 1
2 CONC 947-50.   Subs Lt Col; Aug 1945.  OC L of C Signals, TA, in Western Co
2 CONC md, with HQ at Chester, 1950.  Retd with Hon rank of Col: 29 Nov 1953.
2 CONC   County Comdt, Army Cadet Force, Cheshire, 1953-56 in rank of Col.
2 CONT
2 CONT City Councillor, Chester, 1953-62.
2 CONT
2 CONT m 30 Aug 1945, Hon Margaret Marion, dau of Lord Kindersley, and widow
2 CONC of Capt A Belmont, RA.   No issue.   (Four step-children).
2 CONT
2 CONT Resided for some years at Ewhurst, Sussex, then Headley, Hants and fin
2 CONC ally Hove.   He d. in 1990.
