1 NOTE [CT]: 511. On south wall. Above is Curteis Arms and Crest. Sacred to t
2 CONC he memory of Richard CURTEIS, Esq., who died August, 21st, 1814, aged
2 CONC 76 years. Mary his wife, eldest daughter of Mr. Searles GILES, of Bidd
2 CONC enden, who died April 10th, 1806, aged 66. Having issue two sons, who
2 CONC died in their infancy and two daughters, Sarah and Mary. Mary, wife of
2 CONC  J.B. PROMFRET, Esq., and daughter of Richard and Mary CURTEIS, died 2
2 CONC 6th December, 1804, aged 36 years. Leaving five sons and two daughters
2 CONC , John Dewe, Virgil, Richard Curteis, Charles Wilson, Mary Catherine,
2 CONC Harriett and Edward Giles aged 6 weeks. Charles Wilson died March 26th
2 CONC , 1808, aged 9 years. Edward Giles died August 26th, 1812, aged 7 year
2 CONC s. John Dewe died 6th March, 1820, aged 30 years. John Butler Pomfret,
2 CONC  Esq., died 12th February, 1834, aged 69 years. Mary Catherine died 31
2 CONC st May, 1862, aged 62 (Buried at Ashford). Richard Curteis died 6th Ma
2 CONC y, 1867, aged 70. (Buried at Rye). Harriett Pomfret died 28th July, 18
2 CONC 70, aged 68 years. Virgil Pomfret died 18th May, 1875, aged 79 years.
2 CONC Sarah the eldest daughter, married William CROUGHTON, Esq., of London.
2 CONC  Having issue two sons and one daughter, Richard Curteis, Samuel and S
2 CONC arah Curteis. Samuel died 3rd April, 1814, aged 24 years. Richard Curt
2 CONC eis Croughton died 22nd April, 1822 aged 34. He married Hester, daught
2 CONC er of Thomas PEEL of Manchaster, Esq., by whom he had issue, William P
2 CONC eel, Ann Curteis, Hester and Sarah Bradshaw. Sarah, wife of William Cr
2 CONC oughton, died 30th September, 1827, aged 63 years. William Croughton,
2 CONC Esq., died 2ndNovember, 1827, aged 70 years. [see No. 442].
