1 NOTE Of Biddenden. There are a few Giles, and at least one Searles Giles, i
2 CONC n the Biddenden MIs, but the identification with any particular one is
2 CONC  not certain.
2 CONT
2 CONT Almost certainly this one (which I shall assume to be the case):
2 CONT 29  (Altar) North side: Mary wife of Searles GILES of this parish, Gen
2 CONC t. died ye 14th September 1760 aged 44 leaving issue three daughters,
2 CONC Mary, Jane and Ann. South side: Searles Giles died 22nd April 1777 age
2 CONC d 71. West end: Arms- a Griffin stataont, impaling on a chevron three
2 CONC fleur de lys. Crest a seahorse (?) sejeant.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note that the Tenterden MIs say that there were three daughters and co
2 CONC -heiresses (i.e., that Jane had two sisters, just as shown in this MI)
2 CONC .
