1 NOTE Of the city of Canterbury. A surgeon in Canterbury, and mayor of Cante
2 CONC rbury in 1727-1728.
2 CONT
2 CONT One son, another Edward Jacob, was a surgeon also, and mayor of Favers
2 CONC ham a number of times. He was apparently an eminent naturalist and ant
2 CONC iquary.
2 CONT
2 CONT From the monumental inscriptions of Tilmanstone Church, it seems that
2 CONC he married twice. (Confirmed by the obituary of Edward Jeremiah Curtei
2 CONC s in the Gentleman’s Magazine). Edward was a son of his first marriage
2 CONC , while his second wife was Mary, who died in 1727, aged 33. The Mary
2 CONC who married Stephen Barrett was the daughter of the second wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------
2 CONT From :
2 CONT
2 CONT 28. A flatstone without the [altar] rails to the memory of Jane, daugh
2 CONC ter of Rev Strangford VIOL, rector of Upminster in Essex and Jane his
2 CONC wife, daughter of Richd. Fogge late of this Parish Esquire. She marrie
2 CONC d Edward Jacob of Canterbury surgeon, and left issue 8 children. Ob. M
2 CONC arch 16 1719, aetat 33.  (Information kindly provided by Kathleen Holl
2 CONC ingsbee:- Jane, senior married in 1684 to the Rev. Strangford VIOL of
2 CONC Upminster, co. of Essex, from whom the JACOBS of Faversham are descend
2 CONC ed (Hasted).     From Tilmanstone parish registers and BTs: Mistress J
2 CONC ane FOGGE of Tilmanstone married Mr Strangford VIOLL Rector of Upminst
2 CONC er, Essex. 7 Jan 1683-4    (Cowper licence lists: Mr Strangford VIALL,
2 CONC  of Upminster in Essex, Clerk, widr, and Jane FOGGE of Tilm. spr 24 at
2 CONC  Tilm. or Whitfield. Jacobus BURVILL of Tilmanstone, Clerk, bondsman l
2 CONC icence 3 Jan 1683-4)
2 CONT
2 CONT 39. On Another Flat Stone. Sacred to the Memory of Jane, Daughter of t
2 CONC he Revd. Mr STRANGFORD VIAL, late Rector of Upminster, in Essex, and J
2 CONC ane his Wife, Daughter of Richard FOGGE, late of this Parish Esq. She
2 CONC married Edward JACOB, Surgeon (now) of Canterbury, by whom She had Iss
2 CONC ue eight Children; 4 of whom viz – Sarah, Edward, Richard, and Anne, s
2 CONC urvive; the rest lie here together interred, near their tender Mother.
2 CONC  obijt Mar 16 Anno Salut 1718/19. Aetat 33. 
2 CONT -----------------------------
