1 NOTE First married to George Chin, later separated and remarried Mr Chew. T
2 CONC his marriage did not last, according to Mary probably because he wante
2 CONC d to have children of his own.
2 CONT Veronica died while in a diabetic coma. I [says Monique] visited her w
2 CONC ith Aunt Helen and my mother while James and I were living in NYC.(hav
2 CONC ing moved to NYC in Dec.1985), so visited her in hospital some time af
2 CONC ter that.
2 CONT I’d heard my father tease my mother about being a Chew (?spelling) whi
2 CONC le we were living in Africa, so on separate occasions I asked both Aun
2 CONC t Helen and mother Mary how come her maiden name is down as being Chev
2 CONC insky and where does the Chew fit in? I learnt that Veronica had first
2 CONC  married George Chin and had her 4 children but divorced him and told
2 CONC the children that their father was dead. Not sure if this happened whe
2 CONC n she discovered that he had a Chinese wife and son back in Hong Kong
2 CONC and was regularly sending them money. So she had all 4 children change
2 CONC  their surname to Chew (?spelling) when she remarried. When Mr Chew le
2 CONC ft she then changed their names as well as her own back to her maiden
2 CONC name of Chevinsky. Aunt Helen pointed out though that by then she was
2 CONC a newly wed (think she got married at the age of 16) and so she never
2 CONC took the name of Chevinsky. My mother was born a Chin, changed to Chew
2 CONC , then Chevinsky and then her married name Bahizi.
