1 NOTE She was seven months pregnant when she dropped dead very suddenly (may
2 CONC be from rheumatic fever). Robert Adair remembered her complaining abou
2 CONC t a pain in her chest. They found her with little Graham, aged about t
2 CONC wo, sitting next to her on the floor, crying.
2 CONT She is buried in Lot 3, Block 103A of the Southern Cemetery, Dunedin.
2 CONC The cemetery record says that she died in 1909, aged 39 years. Wife. R
2 CONC esident of Howard St. Born Dunedin. The  grave is still labeled “C. Mc
2 CONC Pherson” (although no formal gravestone exists).
1 _UID 2E4F657C7455471DA45AC9B281621D212580
