1 NAME Marion /Waugh/
2 DISPLAY Marion Waugh
2 GIVN Marion
2 SURN Waugh
1 POSITION -3730,-1580
2 GENOMAP Thomas Boileau's descendants and related
2 BOUNDARYRECT -3756,-1547,-3704,-1627
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ~1823
2 PLAC Redding, Stirling
3 _XREF @place00963@
1 NOTE Came from Muiranside (Muiravonside) in Stirling, Scotland. Pronounced
2 CONC Moranside, apparently. It’s a parish in East Stirlingshire, and there
2 CONC is an interesting statistical account of the parish, written in 1841.
2 CONC The population was around 1700, included one insane person under restr
2 CONC aint, and three too weak in mind to be employed in labour. Ha. Maybe t
2 CONC hey were teenagers. Coal mining was clearly a major activity, and the
2 CONC people were poor. However, according to the Reverend James McFarlan, M
2 CONC inister, who wrote the 1841 statistical account, “The people are indus
2 CONC trious, sober, and kind, especially to other in distress.” Yeah, right
2 CONC , as the Tui ad would say.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Joyce McPherson’s notes, she and Robert (and children) ar
2 CONC e listed in the 1861 census of West Lothian, Polmont area (Polmont was
2 CONC  right next to Muiravonside).
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert McPherson, Head, 35, b. 1826, Brusher in Mines, Wallacetown, St
2 CONC irling
2 CONT Marion, nee Waugh, Wife, 33, Redding, Stirling.
2 CONT Binnie McPherson, son, 10, b. 1851, Scholar, New Monkland, Lanark
2 CONT Margaret McPherson, daughter, 8, 1853, Muiravonside, Stirling
2 CONT Marion McPherson, daughter, 6, 1855, Stonerig, Stirling
2 CONT Janet b. 4/3/1857, dead.
2 CONT Janet b. 14/2/1860, Daughter, 1, Bathgate, West Lothian.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to “A Topographical Dictionary of Scotland”, written by Samu
2 CONC el Lewis in 1846, Wallacetown is in the parish of St. Quivox, district
2 CONC  of Kyle, county of Ayr. It was a new village, established only around
2 CONC  1760 due to the new coal mines, and the people living there were most
2 CONC ly engaged in the mines and in weaving. However, Robert’s date of birt
2 CONC h doesn’t match with his death certificate. In addition, Wallacetown i
2 CONC s in Ayr, not in Stirling, so this doesn’t make a lot of sense. Not cl
2 CONC ear exactly where he was born, as Joyce’s notes are not completely cle
2 CONC ar. I need to look at the original entries myself.
2 CONT
2 CONT I have not been able to trace Marion at all in NZ. No death certificat
2 CONC e, no grave, no burial record, no anything. (She was definitely Robert
2 CONC ’s wife, as she is named on his death certificate.) Maybe she just die
2 CONC d at the goldfields and was dug into a ditch.
