2 PLAC Dunedin
3 _XREF @place00758@
2 SOURCE @S32@
1 ISDEAD Y
1 NOTE Engineer. Buried in Lot 19, Block 29 of the Southern Cemetery, Dunedin
2 CONC , the same plot as his wife. The cemetery records say that he was an E
2 CONC ngineer, died 28 Aug 1904. Resident of Nisson? St. Lived in Otago 46 y
2 CONC ears.
2 CONT
2 CONT I have a copy of his F98 form (from 1898 I think) in which he provided
2 CONC  some details about himself. I saw the original in the Otago Settlers
2 CONC Museum (thanks to Bob Matthews at the Settlers Museum, who provided mu
2 CONC ch of this information). In this F98 he says he came to NZ on the “Geo
2 CONC rge Canning” in 1857. Further, it says:
2 CONT “Born about 1837 at Edinburgh - married Janet Peddie (daughter of Jame
2 CONC s Peddie N.S. Stirling - married at Dunedin in 1860. Wife, 2 (?) sons
2 CONC and 2 daughters living, 2 daughters married, 4 G children. Was Chief E
2 CONC ngineer of P.S. Geelong, Captain Boyce, and other Steamers.” The ship
2 CONC list for the “George Canning”, arrival into Dunedin in 1857, has a Mr.
2 CONC  Clarke on board.
2 CONT
2 CONT However, the Southern Cemetery burial record says that he was born bet
2 CONC ween 1833 and 1834. I don’t know which to believe.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~ourstuff/ElectoralDunedin1862
2 CONC .htm shows him on the Dunedin Electoral Roll in 1862.
2 CONT A copy of the Electoral Roll from 1865-66 (in the Otago Settlers  Muse
2 CONC um) gives his  address as 1 Hanover St.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the Otago Witness of 2 October, 1875, Adam Sprott Clark was a bankr
2 CONC upt (in court on 27 September), and his case was set to stand over. Cl
2 CONC early, he didn’t do all that well. Same in the Otago Witness of 14 Aug
2 CONC ust, 1875, he was declared a bankrupt.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the Otago Witness of 14 September, 1904, a notice was put in that A
2 CONC dam Sprott Clark (70) had died. Doesn’t give the exact date, but this
2 CONC supports a birth date of between 1833 and 1834, in agreement with the
2 CONC burial record.
2 CONT
2 CONT I now (2008) have a copy of his death certificate, which gives the dat
2 CONC e of death as August 28, 1904. Place of residence; 61 Union St. Cause
2 CONC of death: Senile gangrene (1 week) and heart failure. (Sounds like it
2 CONC could have been almost anything.) His father’s name was given as Adam
2 CONC Clark, Builder, and mother’s name was listed as unknown. Born in Leith
2 CONC , Scotland. Five surviving children (2 males, 40, 37, 3 females, 34, 2
2 CONC 6, 23).
