2 DATE 26 SEP 1900
2 PLAC Dunedin
3 _XREF @place00758@
2 SOURCE @S32@
1 ISDEAD Y
1 NOTE Janet was the second daughter of James Peddie Esq. At the time of her
2 CONC death, she had five living children. Christina was the eldest.
2 CONT
2 CONT Buried in the Southern Cemetery, Dunedin, Lot 19, Block 29. The cemete
2 CONC ry record says: Died Sept 26, 1900, aged 62 years, of Dropsy. Resident
2 CONC  of Union St. Born Stirling. Lived in Otago 41 years. This agrees with
2 CONC  the arrival date of the Gloucester, at the end of 1858.
2 CONT
2 CONT A George Peddie is buried in the same plot and is almost certainly her
2 CONC  elder brother. He was only 4 years older than Janet. George died Sept
2 CONC  14, 1863 of Dropsey.  Aged 29. Draper. Resident of Dunedin. Born Scot
2 CONC land. Lived 5 years in Otago.
2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~nzbound/nzbound/gloucester.ht
2 CONC m says that the “Gloucester”, arrived in Port Chalmer Dec 28 from Lond
2 CONC on had, as passenger, Peddie, G. and Janet. This has to be the same Ge
2 CONC orge Peddie that is buried with Janet and her husband, Adam Sprott Cla
2 CONC rk. The Peddies came out as Second Cabin passengers, not Steerage, so
2 CONC they must have had a bit more money. This squares with the description
2 CONC  of Janet’s father as a writer, Esq.
2 CONT
2 CONT Janet married Adam Sprott on 26 April, 1861. The record is in the Otag
2 CONC o Daily Times BDM, as reproduced on http://freepages.genealogy.rootswe
2 CONC b.com/~nzbound/nzbound/otago_bdm1861.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT May 4th, 1861
2 CONT At Maclaggan-street, Dunedin, on the 26th ult., by the  Rev. Dr. Thoma
2 CONC s  Burns, Mr  Adam S. Clark, to Janet, second daughter of  James Peddi
2 CONC e, Esq., Writer, Stirling.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Marriage Certificate says the marriage occurred “In the dwelling h
2 CONC ouse of James Feddie, McLagan Street, Dunedin.” Clearly James Peddie i
2 CONC s meant, and this confirms that the James Peddie, 8 years older than J
2 CONC anet, was her older brother.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to her death certificate, she died of Bright’s Disease of Ki
2 CONC dney - 6 years (i.e., chronic nephritis), Uroemie [sic] Coma - 48 Hour
2 CONC s. (What the transcriber meant is Uroemic, or Uremic, coma.)
