1 NOTE A builder, according to [BT], although no source is given. [BT] contin
2 CONC ues: “After the revocation of the Edict of Nantes many French Protesta
2 CONC nts fled their country to settle in the south of England. They were fo
2 CONC r the most part merchants and skilled tradesmen and included lace make
2 CONC rs, tapestry makers and cloth weavers. They intermarried with the sout
2 CONC hern English and tradition maintain that there was a strong French str
2 CONC ain in the Bond family.
2 CONT A lot of early Bond records are lost due to fire in local (Shipton?) p
2 CONC arish church. Some information may be available in Beaminster Cathedra
2 CONC l.”
