1 NOTE [C-D, XI, 791]. Seigneur de Lauzières, de Montagnac, de Cones, etc. He
2 CONC  founded, during the life of his father, in 1350, the Abbey of Nuns of
2 CONC  Saint-Etienne-de-Gourgas, of the Order of Saint-Benoit, near to Clerm
2 CONC ont-Lodève. It was founded with the consent of Pope Clement VI and of
2 CONC Bertrand Dumas, the Bishop of Lodève, and given a dowry of 6000 golden
2 CONC  florins of Florence. Following the bull of the same Pope, given at Po
2 CONC itiers, the patronage of this abbey was gifted to the house of Lauzièr
2 CONC es. Anglesian was elected by the Estates of Languedoc as conservator [
2 CONC of their deliberations?!], and, by Letters of 15 April 1359 was confir
2 CONC med as the Governor of Languedoc by Jean de France, Comte de Poitiers.
