1 NOTE [BC] writes: When she was 17 months old her older brother, Charles, no
2 CONC ticed her playing outside in the garden just before midday. Later, Sel
2 CONC ina asked where she was and a search began. Charles found her in the c
2 CONC reek near the house. She had been in the habit of going to the creek t
2 CONC o collect water in a tin and must have slipped in and drowned.
2 CONT
2 CONT I remember my great-grandmother Kate (Edith Norgrove) often talking ab
2 CONC out the little girl who drowned in Spring Creek. This must have been w
2 CONC hom she was talking about. I never knew before who it was. It was Kate
2 CONC ’s husband’s little sister.
