1 NOTE Named after famous Australian cricketers, Algy Gears and Vernon Ransfo
2 CONC rd. I remember Uncle Algy a little bit. As a child I was fascinated by
2 CONC  how he ate leeks in white sauce. I hated them, and yet he attacked th
2 CONC em with such enthusiasm. Slurping noises and all. I would sit and watc
2 CONC h, enthralled. He was a large man, very strong, with a deep voice, sor
2 CONC t of burry as I remember.
2 CONT
2 CONT Details and descendants in [BC]. One daughter was Helen, another was G
2 CONC lenis. Mum’s cousins I suppose. We visited Helen once on a farm somewh
2 CONC ere, when I was quite young. I remember nothing more about them, excep
2 CONC t that Mum would often talk about them. Oh, and Colin was a son also.
2 CONC He visited us once, much to everybody’s amusement. Tighter than a duck
2 CONC ’s arse (to use Mum’s phrase) and did painting by numbers. And thought
2 CONC  it was great art. Oh boy, I remember that visit. It went down into fa
2 CONC mily lore.
