1 NOTE Of Clapham Common, Surrey.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------------------------
2 CONT From :
2 CONT John Davenport (ca.1719-1789) of The Hall, Clapham Common, North Side,
2 CONC   Surrey. (See Map of Clapham families in C. Smith's "Actual Survey of
2 CONC  the Road from London to Brighthelmston" 1800 [reproduced in The Londo
2 CONC n Rich, by Peter Thorold,1999].
2 CONT Ref. Robert Bevan 1865-1925, A Memoir by His Son - "An ancestor on his
2 CONC  mother's side, John Davenport, wrote an amusing Hints for Bad Horseme
2 CONC n, published in 1786 under the pseudonym Charles Thompson."
2 CONT A letter from R[ichard?] Davenport to his mother from Eton (21st March
2 CONC  1779) was addressed to 432 Strand. In 1794 that address was occupied
2 CONC by Gilpin & Newton, Woollen Drapers and by Davenport & Gilpin, Army Cl
2 CONC othiers.
2 CONT Musgrave's Obituaries prior to 1800 records John Davenport, Clothier 1
2 CONC 6 July 1789 aged 70.
2 CONT He was mentioned in Jonathan Eade's will of 1762.  I [PB] have a copy
2 CONC of his will from the PRO - Prob 11/1181. Left his three unmarried chil
2 CONC dren £10,000 each.”
2 CONT ---------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Lambeth Archives Department:
2 CONT “ John [Davenport], a wealthy merchant (he was Master of the Merchant
2 CONC Taylors' Company in 1775) and woollen draper to the King had bought a
2 CONC large estate on Clapham Common Northside, near the present Sugden Road
2 CONC . ”
