1 NOTE From Kate: Arthur went to sea in “Temple Knight” and the first boat to
2 CONC  pick up signals from the Titanic. Killed soon after returning. Intend
2 CONC ed settling down. Went to Auckland to look for a job. Had a temporary
2 CONC job on a coal hulk. Helped friend to close hatch and fell down 45 ft a
2 CONC nd broke his neck.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Evening Post (20 June, 1914) has a short article:
2 CONT ------------
2 CONT SAILOR KILLED
2 CONT Falls down a hold.
2 CONT
2 CONT Auckland, 19th June.
2 CONT A sailor named. A. Norgrove fell down the hold of the collier Kauri at
2 CONC  the Queen’s Wharf this afternoon and was killed. The doctor of HMS Ps
2 CONC yche went to th eman’s assistance, but death had been instantaneous. D
2 CONC eceased was single, about 24 years of age, and belonged to Blenheim.
2 CONT ------------
