1 NOTE The website of the village of Sutton-in-Craven (http://www.sutton-in-c
2 CONC raven.org.uk/historyofsteeton1886.asp) has extracts from the History o
2 CONC f Steeton, by John Clough (written in 1886), which contains a bit of i
2 CONC nformation about the Cloughs of Sutton. Not enough to trace a definite
2 CONC  genealogy, mind you.
2 CONT
2 CONT Neither are the Kildwick-in-Craven parish registers very useful, as th
2 CONC ere are just too many Cloughs, all with the same name. For example, on
2 CONC e Maria Clough was baptised on 12 December, 1675, daughter of Michael
2 CONC and Mary Clough, of Kildwick. But another Maria Clough was baptised on
2 CONC  29 August, 1686, daughter of Robert and Elizabeth, of Sutton. Even th
2 CONC e later one is dicey as the mother of our Stephen, as she would have b
2 CONC een 35 in 1719. Not impossible, mind you. I can’t find any record of h
2 CONC er marriage, either.
