1 NOTE There is some confusion over the wife of this Richard Beale. For a lon
2 CONC g time I thought it was Elizabeth Henden, but it now appears that Eliz
2 CONC abeth Henden married a different (related) Richard Beale, but in the s
2 CONC ame year. Elizabeth Henden and the other Richard Beale apparently had
2 CONC two sons only, Charles and John.
2 CONT
2 CONT The monumental inscription in Biddenden church just says that Richard
2 CONC Beale’s wife was Elizabeth, without giving her maiden name. However, B
2 CONC erry’s Pedigrees shows Newington as the wife, and a number of reliable
2 CONC  researchers have seen the marriage entry in the parish register of Wa
2 CONC dhurst church. The marriage of Richard Beale (the other one) and Eliza
2 CONC beth Henden is in the parish register of Biddenden church, also in 170
2 CONC 5, but in January.
2 CONT
2 CONT Geoff West writes:
2 CONT “..........I had another look at Richard Beale's will ... -as you say
2 CONC it refers to his wife as Elizabeth Beale throughout also the MI in Bid
2 CONC denden churchyard does not give a surname.The dates on the MI seem to
2 CONC tie up closer to the Newington side however.
2 CONT The LDS site gives Richard's birth as 29 May 1683 and his parents as J
2 CONC ohn Beale and Joanna Nepecker.The Biddenden parish register entry for
2 CONC Richard Beale that I found gives his baptism on 18 October 1668 as fol
2 CONC lows "Richard ye sonn of William Beale & Elizabeth his wife was borne
2 CONC the 9th day ". This makes him 89 years old at his death on 10th Novemb
2 CONC er 1757 which is the age given on the MI. Also Elizabeth's baptismal e
2 CONC ntry in the Wadhurst parish register on 12 May 1680 reads "Baptized El
2 CONC izabeth daughter of Mr. Samuel and Elizabeth Newington "This would mak
2 CONC e her 84 if she died on 28 June 176(?4).The MI says 8(?1).Elizabeth He
2 CONC nden born 27 June 1690 would only have been in her 70's.
2 CONT Another clue is that one of the sons is named Seaman (a name that cont
2 CONC inues to be used in succeeding generations) and that would indicate a
2 CONC descent from Simon Seaman which Richard ( who marries Elizabeth Newing
2 CONC  ton) has and Richard( who marries Elizabeth Henden) does not.”
2 CONT
2 CONT I agree that there’s little doubt that my Richard Beale married a Newi
2 CONC ngton, not a Henden.
