1 NOTE of Biddenden. A clothier.
2 CONT From :
2 CONT “Under this Tombe lieth ye Body of Richard BEALE of Biddenden, Clothie
2 CONC r, who died October 30th 1691 aged 72 years and nine months. He was tw
2 CONC ice married, his first wife was Mary daughter of Mr SEAMAN, Minister o
2 CONC f Bredgate (sic) By whom he left one son William. His second wife was
2 CONC widow of John NEWENDEN by whom he left another son, John, who erected
2 CONC this tomb. A………94. North side. Here also lieth Mary second wife of Ric
2 CONC hard Beale who died July ye sixth 1696 aged 73 years and four months.”
2 CONT Note how the two girls weren’t mentioned. One of them died young, and
2 CONC most likely the other did also.
