1 SEX M
1 NOTE This identity of Richard’s father is not certain?
2 CONT
2 CONT Geoff West writes:
2 CONT “The information above Richard was supplied by a Mr. Stanford- Beale i
2 CONC n 1999 who is a descendant of Thomas Beale and Anne Elwin .... it show
2 CONC s the parents of Richard Beale (d 1691) as John Beale 1580-1645 -linne
2 CONC nweaver of Biddenden and Margaret Clark-widow. John's parents are give
2 CONC n as Richard Beale 1560-1621 and Elizabeth Brattell who were married o
2 CONC n 1 July 1578. Richard is a clothier of Biddenden and his parents are
2 CONC given as Thomas Beale died 1567 and Alyce and Thomas Beale's father is
2 CONC  given as another Thomas who died in 1559.
2 CONT I have not been able to verify any of this information.Some of these n
2 CONC ames appear on LDS John Beale and Margaret Beale -Thomas Beale and Ali
2 CONC ce Hasden-William Beale and Alice Hasnode -and two different Richard B
2 CONC eales who,once again, are attributed with the same children.If you can
2 CONC  make any order out of it ,please let me know.
2 CONT The pencil comments at the bottom of the page are to do with River Hal
2 CONC l, the house which passes down through the generations and is said to
2 CONC have been the home of the Beale(Beald) family from 1465- it has a late
2 CONC  medieval origin for the older part of the building.”
2 CONT
2 CONT So any earlier Beale pedigree seems pretty uncertain.
