1 NOTE Agnes appears in the Roper line in the 1619 Kent Visitation, with husb
2 CONC and given, and brother as Edmund. (Agnes ux Walteri Colepeper de Bedge
2 CONC bery in co’ Cantij ar.)  A nice clear identification. However, the Col
2 CONC epeper line in the same source lists her as Agnes filia Edmundi Roper
2 CONC de St. Dunstans p’pe urbem Cantuariae.  I’m not sure what’s going on h
2 CONC ere.
2 CONT
2 CONT Also, as  points out, it seems that the Visitation of Kent confuses he
2 CONC r first marriage with the wife of the son, John. I have followed that
2 CONC version here, making her the widow of John Bedgebery, so I don’t quite
2 CONC  agree with what the Visitation says.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the Visitation Agnes was the daughter of Rodolphus Roper
2 CONC (and Beatrix Lewknor) son of Thomas Roper (and a daughter of Thomas Ap
2 CONC ledore), son of Adae(?) Roper, son of Ewin Roper. That’s all the infor
2 CONC mation it contains.
