1 NOTE Died without issue? (natu s.p.) The first son (Fil. maximus) according
2 CONC  to  but this is disputed by .
2 CONT
2 CONT From :
2 CONT “22 Sep 1516, 8 Henry VIII. I Richard Culpeper of the parish of Arding
2 CONC ly, co. Sussex, Esq. and son of Walter Culpeper late of Goudhurst co.
2 CONC Kent Esq. and brother of Sir John Culpeper late of Goudhurst aforesaid
2 CONC  make my testament. To be buried in the chancel of the church of Ardin
2 CONC gly next the sepulture of Margaret Culpeper late my wife. Bequests to
2 CONC the brothers of the house of Moatenden in Kent, Lewes in Sussex, Newga
2 CONC te in London and Lossenham in Kent. To Anne Pympe my cousin 10 marks a
2 CONC t marriage or at 26. To the mending of the roads within the manor of W
2 CONC akehurst and Seldwyke Cross 13s 4d. To Richard Culpeper son and heir o
2 CONC f Nicholas Culpeper a bond or obligation of the said Nicholas for £5 6
2 CONC s 8d. To Master Edward Culpeper brother of the aforesaid Richard 40s.
2 CONC Residuary legatee Elizabeth Culpeper widow of my late brother Nicholas
2 CONC , and I appoint her together with Thomas Culpeper, George Culpeper and
2 CONC  Richard Culpeper, younger sons of the aforesaid Nicholas Culpeper exe
2 CONC cutrix and executors. And I make Richard Culpeper, Esq. and Master Edw
2 CONC ard Culpeper brother of the aforesaid Richard my overseers. Witnesses
2 CONC John Yonge, Vicar of West Hoathly, Henry Wellys, Thomas Doggett, Chris
2 CONC topher Payne, and William Hordys with others.
2 CONT .
2 CONT Will as to lands of Richard Culpeper, Esq. "one of the sons of Walter
2 CONC Culpeper of Goudhurst, Esquire, and brother to Sir John Culpeper, some
2 CONC time of Goudhurst, Knight" 22 Sep 1516. To Elizabeth Culpeper my siste
2 CONC r a croft (a small piece of land, usually attached to a house, used fo
2 CONC r farming or pasture) in Horsemonden in Kent, with remainder to Alexan
2 CONC der Culpeper, and no more for "thanks be to God he has no need." The m
2 CONC ale heirs of Walter Culpeper my nephew to have the manor of Heronden,
2 CONC and the tenement of the Bavre. Loggelond in Ardingly to the churchward
2 CONC ens to keep an obit, with beer bread and cheese, by 10 priests at 8d e
2 CONC ach to pray for self, Margaret my wife, Walter Culpeper and Agnes his
2 CONC wife my father and mother, Richard Wakehurst the elder and Richard Wak
2 CONC ehurst the younger and Agnes his wife, my wife’s father and mother. Pa
2 CONC rishes of Ardingly, Balcombe, West Hoathly, Lindfield and Whyhyme. Eli
2 CONC zabeth Culpeper, late the wife of Nicholas Culpeper my brother to take
2 CONC  up the rents and issues of all other lands in Horsemonden or Goudhurs
2 CONC t in Kent, and in Monfield, Salehurst, Ifeld, Crawley, Slaugham, Worth
2 CONC  and West Hoathly in Sussex and in Leigh in Surrey or elsewhere in Eng
2 CONC land for life, and after her death the lands in Leigh, which I bought,
2 CONC  to Richard Culpeper son and heir of Nicholas and Elizabeth. To Thomas
2 CONC  Culpeper one of the sons of the said Nicholas and Anne wife of the sa
2 CONC id Thomas, lands in Ifeld, Crawley, Slaugham and Worth which I bought
2 CONC of John Wodye &c. To George Culpeper (after Elizabeth's decease) the m
2 CONC essuage and lands of Stroudgate for life, with remainder to Richard Cu
2 CONC lpeper son and heir of the aforesaid Nicholas. Also to the said George
2 CONC  Busses in West Hoathly and a mill called Hope Mill in Southerst (Goud
2 CONC hurst?) and the halfendele of a fulling mill in Horsemonden to him and
2 CONC  his heirs. And as for Pipstye I cannot put it from George for it is c
2 CONC opyhold. To Richard Culpeper, youngest son of the foresaid Nicholas an
2 CONC d Elizabeth, a messuage or tenement called the Feryn in Ninfield and S
2 CONC alehurst co Sussex, and land and messuages at Turnerhill also two tene
2 CONC ments in Southerst sometime John Bechefeld, Richard Mylis, Thomas Burg
2 CONC es. Remainder after death of Elizabeth to foresaid Richard his heirs a
2 CONC nd assigns. If Thomas Culpeper, George Culpeper, or Richard Culpeper t
2 CONC he youngest son die during the lifetime of the said Elizabeth, without
2 CONC  wife or children, his part to remain to the other living of the afore
2 CONC said three.Proved at Lambeth 8 Nov 1516 by Richard Culpeper, George Cu
2 CONC lpeper, and Thomas Culpeper in person and by Elizabeth Culpeper in the
2 CONC  person of William Crowland.”
