2 CONT Extract from :
2 CONT “Sir John, who in 1348 had purchased the manor of Wigsell, in Salehurs
2 CONC t, co. Sussex, from Simon de Etchingham,34 by marriage with Elizabeth,
2 CONC  daughter and co-heiress of Sir John Hardreshull, of Hardreshull, co.
2 CONC Warwick, considerably augmented his patrimonial estates, and left at h
2 CONC is death an only son and heir, Sir Thomas Colepeper, of Bayhall, in Ke
2 CONC nt., and Hardreshull, in Warwickshire.”
2 CONT
2 CONT In Burke's "Extinct and Dormant Baronetcies of England, Ireland & Scot
2 CONC land", p. 144-145, is the following on John Culpeper, Sheriff of Kent:
2 CONC  "John Colepeper, esq. of Bay Hall, who was sheriff of Kent in the 43r
2 CONC d [year] of Edward III [around 1370]. He m. Elizabeth, daughter and co
2 CONC -heir of Sir John Hardrishall, knt. of Hardrishall, in the county of W
2 CONC arwick, by Maud Mussenden, an heiress, and thereby became possessed of
2 CONC  divers manors."
