2 CONT
2 CONT The 1592 Visitation of Kent reads:
2 CONT “Sir John de Hardishull of ...... in the Countie of Warwicke, Knight,
2 CONC maried to his firste wiffe Mawde Daughter of .... and by her had issue
2 CONC  William de Hardishull Died sans issue Johan eldist Daughter and one o
2 CONC f theires maried to Sr James Burforde knight, whoe had issue John [sic
2 CONC ] his onlye Daughter and heire, Elizabeth Hardishull seconde Daughter
2 CONC and one of theires of Sr John maried to John Coulpper of .... in the C
2 CONC ountie of Kent Esquire, Margaret thirde Daughter and one of theires ma
2 CONC ried to Sr John Talbott knight who had issue John Talbott who Died wit
2 CONC hout issue. Note also that the aboue named Johan who was the Daughter
2 CONC and sole heire of James Burforde knighte was maried to one Garton a Me
2 CONC rcer of London, who had issue John Garton that Died also sans issue, w
2 CONC erevppon the hole inheritance of the three Daughters and coheires Dide
2 CONC  After wardes descende vnto Sr Thomas Colpepper knighte as Sonne and h
2 CONC eire to the saide Elizabeth. After the saide Sr John maried to his sec
2 CONC ond wiffe Dame Margarett by whome he had no issue, vt pate[t]ex script
2 CONC is Colpeperij.”
2 CONT
2 CONT Not quite sure what to make of all that.
