1 NOTE Extract from :
2 CONT “Sir Thomas Colepeper married, first, Alianora, daughter and heiress o
2 CONC f Nicholas Greene, of Exton, in Rutlandshire, by whom he had issue:--
2 CONT (i.) Alianora, who married Sir Reginald Cobham, of Lingfield, in Surre
2 CONC y.
2 CONT (ii.) Sir John Colepeper, of Bayhall, Hardreshull and Exton, who, by J
2 CONC uliana, his wife--who remarried, first, John Braunspath, Esq.,35 and,
2 CONC secondly, Robert Fenne, Esq.,36 -- had issue an only daughter Katherin
2 CONC e, who by her first marriage with John Harrington, Esq., carried the E
2 CONC xton estates to that family, and married, secondly, Brian Talbot, Esq.
2 CONT Sir Thomas Colepeper married, secondly, Joyce, widow of John Vyne, Esq
2 CONC .,37 by whom he had four sons:--
2 CONT (iii.) Walter.
2 CONT (iv.) Nicholas.
2 CONT (v.) Thomas.
2 CONT (vi.) Richard.
2 CONT Sir Thomas Colepeper died a very old man, about 1428/9....”
2 CONT
2 CONT Translation of his will, from :
2 CONT “26 Oct 1427, THOMAS COLPEPER, Knight, Sunday next before the Feast of
2 CONC  the Apostles Simon and Jude the 7th year of the reign of Our Lord the
2 CONC  King Henry VI after the conquest. My body to be buried in the Abbey o
2 CONC f Begghame because that church is dedicated the Annunciation of Our La
2 CONC dy, in the place where my sepulture of "Alebastre" is made. I leave to
2 CONC  Nicholas my son all my horses and to Elizabeth his wife my paternoste
2 CONC rs of gold and I leave to Jouet Topymoye if she is alive 5 marcs.
2 CONT      To John Bayhalle, Bastard, if he helps my executors 10 marcs. To
2 CONC Thomas Payn my ‘cuc’ 40s. To my ‘butiller’ 13s. 4d. My ‘Baker’ 13s. 4d
2 CONC . To Cristiane Brayley 13s. 4d., John Bosvyle 13s. 4d., John Coppyng 1
2 CONC 3s. 4d., my Parker 13s. 4d., John Dwale 13s. 4d. To each ‘garson’ 3s.
2 CONC 4d., to each ‘page’ and ‘hyne’ 20d., ‘a Malyne ma petite Chaumberer’ t
2 CONC o her marriage and advancement 20s.
2 CONT I leave to aid the church of Pepynbery to diverse good works 40s. To t
2 CONC he high altar there 13s. 4d. To Sr. John Trot 20s. To the Abbot of Beg
2 CONC gham 20s., to each chanon 3s. 4d., to each curate (curatour) of seven
2 CONC parishes nearest for Placebo, Dirige and Commendation and mass by note
2 CONC  of Requiem 6s. 8d. To Five of the poorest men of the same parishes 5d
2 CONC . To the Abbot and Convent of Beggham each year for 7 years 10s. to ho
2 CONC ld my anniversary and the Anniversary of Joyouse (Joyce) my wife. I le
2 CONC ave to Walter my son 200 marcs. To Nicholas my son 200 marcs. To Thoma
2 CONC s Fitz (sic) 200 marcs. To John Copeper my son £40.
2 CONT      To Abbot and Convent of Begghame £35. 6. 8. To the church of Nuns
2 CONC  of Mallyng 40s., the Priory church of Tonbregge 20s., the Friars of A
2 CONC ylesforde 20s., the Austyn Friars of Rye to hold my obit and anniversa
2 CONC ry 40s. I leave to the light of the Tapers of the schryne of Cantirbur
2 CONC y 20s. I pray and charge John Colpeper and all my other sons by the bl
2 CONC essing of God and of myself that they do not hinder my executors or my
2 CONC  feoffees. I leave for the administration of my goods on the manor of
2 CONC Baghalle at my decease if need be £20. The Residue the one moiety to m
2 CONC y sons and to Joyce my wife and the other moiety to the Abbey of Begha
2 CONC me on condition they find a chaplain to sing for the souls of me and J
2 CONC oyce my wife at the altar where our bodies lie for ten years as my exe
2 CONC cutors and the abbot can agree.
2 CONT Executors. Sire John Langdon, Bishop of Roucestre, John Chetham Abbot
2 CONC of Beghame, Walter and Nicholas my sons, Wm. Burgoyne, Roger Honyton,
2 CONC Wm. Bernes and Thomas Festynden and I give to the Bishop of Rochester
2 CONC for his diligence and labour 10 marcs and to each of the others 5 marc
2 CONC s.
2 CONT      This is the Will of Master Thomas Colpeper Knight, made in the Fe
2 CONC ast of St. Margaret in the 3rd year of the reign of Our Lord the King
2 CONC Henry VI since the conquest charging his enfeoffees Wm. Bernes, Richd
2 CONC Ruyton, Sire Robert Clerk, Robert Sprynget in all lands and tenements
2 CONC in the Counties of Kent and Sussex who were enfeoffed by deed bearing
2 CONC dated in the Feast of the Annunciation of Our Lady 10th years of King
2 CONC Henry the Fourth (8 September 1407) and afterwards by a charter to cer
2 CONC tain feoffees Thomas Longle bishop of Durham, Wm. Cheyne justice, Walt
2 CONC er et Nicholas Colpeper my sons, Wm. Bernes, Ric Ruyton and Robert Spr
2 CONC ynget carrying the date the Feast of the Annunciation of our Lady in t
2 CONC he 10th year of the King Henry the Fifth (25 March 1422) concerning th
2 CONC e Manor of Bayhalle with all lands etc., which were of old time given
2 CONC by fine to John Colpeper my father and his heirs males in the parishes
2 CONC  of Pepyngbery, Tonbregge and Tudele. I will and charge my said feoffe
2 CONC es Thomas, William, Walter and Nicholas Wm. Bernes, Richard and Robert
2 CONC  the said manor to go to my sons by partition in Gauylkynde.
2 CONT      And touching the Manor of Badeselle after the death of me Sr. Tho
2 CONC s. Colpeper to go to Walter my son and his heirs males and in default
2 CONC to the heirs of me and Dame Joyce and then to my right heirs.      And
2 CONC  touching the Manor of Bernet in the parishes of Leghe, Penserst, Bite
2 CONC hergh and Tonbregge with the ‘molyne a brente’ of Gretenerssh, with al
2 CONC l the lands and tenements called Scottegrove in the parish of Asshe, G
2 CONC atewikemede in the parish of Otteforde, with the rents and farms in th
2 CONC e parishes of Sele and Sevenoke, to Thomas my son and for default to N
2 CONC icholas his brother and for default to the heirs male of me and Joyce
2 CONC my wife and in default to my right heirs.
2 CONT      And touching the lands etc of Coluerden, two windmills, Coluerden
2 CONC  mede, the lands etc of Bokstede, Marsfelde, with all the lands etc in
2 CONC  the parishes of Fernthe (Frant) and Wadeherst with the mill of Berkel
2 CONC eghe and three marcs of fee farm which the Sire de Ponynges pays for t
2 CONC he lands called Hosilhothe, to Nicholas my son. In default to the heir
2 CONC s males of me and Joyce lately my wife. And I will that the said Nicho
2 CONC las shall have ‘en ennuatage’ all the lands etc which are of fee simpl
2 CONC e belonging to the Manor of Bayhalle which were bought by Walter Colpe
2 CONC per my uncle, John Colpeper my father or by me Sir Thos. Colpeper Knig
2 CONC ht, which were bought since the Fine was made and I charge my feoffes
2 CONC after my death to enfeoff the said Nicholas my son therein.
2 CONT      Touching the Manor of Wyggesele and lands of Hernden in the paris
2 CONC hes of Sandherst and Newynden because the said manor of Wiggesele is o
2 CONC f fee and was given and granted by deed indented at the marriage betwe
2 CONC en Joyce my wife and me Sr. Thomas Colpeper and to the heirs males and
2 CONC  in default to the right heirs of me the said Sr. Thomas, not withstan
2 CONC ding that since our marriage I have made other feoffement to Wm. Berne
2 CONC s and others I will after my death the said Manor be granted by the fe
2 CONC offees as was arranged at our marriage.
2 CONT      Done at Bayhalle the year etc abovesaid. I Thomas Colpeper Knt, t
2 CONC he Sunday next the Feast of the Purification of Our Lady the 7th year
2 CONC of the reign of King Henry VIth ordain: that Nicholas my son in his pr
2 CONC oper person shall go a pilgrimage to Norwich and there offer ‘a le Sei
2 CONC nt vicair on coer quest en mon chapel d’oor’ and that he have the cost
2 CONC  of his expenses of my goods. That the same Nicholas make another Pilg
2 CONC rimage to the ‘Shryne’ of St. Thomas of Caunterbury in his proper pers
2 CONC on and there offer ‘vn roll d’oor’ and have for himself the costs and
2 CONC expenses.
2 CONT      I leave in the church in the Town of Pountose in Normandy where t
2 CONC he body of Richard my son lies a chalys and a chaplain to sing there f
2 CONC or his soul for a year. To Marion Chamberer my ‘hopland’ of Scarlet an
2 CONC d furred with ‘Mesines’ and 20s. To Alison for her labour another ‘hop
2 CONC land’ with the fur and 13s. 4d. (Hopoland = a cloak).
2 CONT      To Nicholas my son a suitable bed such as his brother Walter had
2 CONC at his marriage. I will that Thomas Festynden have £10 on condition he
2 CONC  find surety to pay to Cristian Braylez each year during her life 20s.
2 CONC  To the Prior and Convent of Cumbwelle 100s.
2 CONT      I will that Thomas Peche farmer of Wiggessele be pardoned his deb
2 CONC t of last year of 100s. My feoffees in a piece of land called Gatewikm
2 CONC ede in Otteforde to sell and buy other land for Thomas my son.
2 CONT      Proved 8 March 1428 at Slydon and administration granted to Walte
2 CONC r Colpeper, Roger Honyton and Thos. Festynden executors and afterwards
2 CONC  at Lambeth to Wm. Burgoyne and Nicholas Colpeper. (403b Chichele I).”
