1 FAMC @F1702@
1 FAMS @F1695@
0 @I2538@ INDI
1 NAME Margaret /de Cralle/
2 DISPLAY Margaret de Cralle
2 GIVN Margaret
2 SURN de Cralle
1 POSITION 1960,2070
2 GENOMAP Thomas Boileau's descendants and related
2 BOUNDARYRECT 1931,2096,1990,2009
1 SEX F
1 NOTE Margaret presumably inherited the manor of Cralle from her brother, Ri
2 CONC chard Cralle, and passed it on to her younger son, Simon.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------
2 CONT From soc.genealogy.medieval, an extract from a post by Louise Staley,
2 CONC Fri, Jun 9 2006.
2 CONT
2 CONT *CROWHAM:* “The manor seems to have been in the family of *Peplesham*,
2 CONC
2 CONT [1]   although William de Lessingham was returned as holding it
2 CONT (probably on lease) in 1339, [2]  for at the end of that century, *on
2 CONT the death of Simon Peplesham, Crowham passed through his daughter and
2 CONT heir Margaret to her husband Robert Cralle*, [3]  and their son Richar
2 CONC d
2 CONT Cralle was holding it in 1411-12. [4]  Richard’s heirs were his two
2 CONT sisters, Isabel, who married Vincent Finch, and Margery, the wife of
2 CONT Richard Cheyney. [5]  Crowham evidently formed part of Margery’s
2 CONT portion, and later that of her younger son Simon Cheyney. Simon and hi
2 CONC s
2 CONT eldest son Alexander had land in Westfield in 1437 [6] but Crowham aft
2 CONC er
2 CONT Simon’s death about 1455 must have passed to the youngest son, William
2 CONC
2 CONT Cheyney of Warbleton, and through his son John (d. 1494) and grandson
2 CONT William (d. 1508), to his great-grandson, also William, for it was
2 CONT ultimately inherited by Pelham Cheyney, second son of this last
2 CONT William.[7] (VCH Sussex 9: 91).”
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.      VCH Sussex 9: 119.
2 CONT 2.      /Coll. Top. Et Gen/. vii, 119.
2 CONT 3.      /Suss. Arch. Col/l. Lxv, 47.
2 CONT 4.      Ibid. x, 145 (Subsidy Roll)
2 CONT 5.      Ibid. xxxvii, 34; lxv, 47.
2 CONT 6.      Ibid. 48; Add. Ch. 24861.
2 CONT 7.      /Suss. Arch. Coll/. Lxv, 49.
2 CONT 8.      Add. Ch. 20163. Will. Battesford, one of the trustees, was the
2 CONC  first
2 CONT husband of Margery de Peplesham, who afterwards married Robert Cralle,
2 CONC
2 CONT father of Richard.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------------------------------
