1 NOTE From Hasted's History of Kent
2 CONT
2 CONT ALEXANDER de CHENEY; Sir; Of Patrixborne Cheney which manor was given
2 CONC to him in Hy III reign by Sir WILLIAM de SAY; In 1299/1300 attended th
2 CONC at king in the victorious expedition into Scotland and at the siege of
2 CONC  Carlaverock where he was knighted.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was father of WILLIAM de CHENEY (-1334/5 possesed of the manor of B
2 CONC asmangore); m Margaret d&h of Sir ROBERT de SHURLAND in whoes right he
2 CONC  held the manor of Shurland, Shepey, where he resided; He held many ot
2 CONC her estaes in Kent.
