2 BOUNDARYRECT 2381,1576,2440,1503
1 SEX M
1 NOTE So, Berry says that Jane’s father was John Cheyney of Cralle. Well, ye
2 CONC s, but WHICH John Cheyney of Cralle? There’s the rub.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Cheyne family of Cralle is well known. I did find a web page that
2 CONC purported to say which John Cheyney this was, but  NO references were
2 CONC given, and I have no idea how reliable it is. Probably not at all. Acc
2 CONC ording to this web page, Jane was the daughter of John Cheyney and Mar
2 CONC garet Oxenbridge. I doubt this very much.
2 CONT
2 CONT The genealogy of the Cheyneys of Cralle is documented in the Sussex Ar
2 CONC chive Collection v. 65 pp. 47-51, in an article by L.F. Salzman. John
2 CONC and Margaret are there, in detail, with extracts from their wills. Joh
2 CONC n’s will mentions a daughter, Joan, by his first wife, Agnes Farby. Jo
2 CONC an is also mentioned in Margaret’s will. However, there is no mention
2 CONC of any Thomas Newington anywhere. This Joan may, or may not, be my Jan
2 CONC e..
2 CONT
2 CONT On the other hand, this was the only John (Father) and Joan (daughter)
2 CONC  pairing in the Cheyney genealogy, as laid down by Salzman, so it’s th
2 CONC e only realistic possibility. If so, it would extend the genealogy for
2 CONC  an additional 6 generations, back to Alexander de Cheyney. That all s
2 CONC eems rather reliable, and done by an expert. Mind you, what do I know?
2 CONT
2 CONT The will of the John Cheyney in the Sussex Archives was proved in 1494
2 CONC . So that date is consistent with his daughter being my Jane.
