1 NOTE Some confusion about this person.
2 CONT The Elliots: The Story of a Border Clan, a genealogical history. By Th
2 CONC e Dowager Lady Eliott of Stobs and Sir Arthur Eliott, 11th Baronet of
2 CONC Stobs. Published 1974. ISBN 0 85422 081 X. p174 says:
2 CONT "Alicia Eling [Elliott], born 23rd Dec. 1832, married in 1863 Rev. Joh
2 CONC n Brattle and died in 1912, having had issue."
2 CONT This likely an error.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sneyd file gives this as "Reverend J. D. Cane"
2 CONT
2 CONT And Emily's Memoir, p42, probably the most reliable source, says:
2 CONT "Aunt Alicia had already left the home roof, having been married in th
2 CONC e previous Octr. at Berne, to the Rev.J.B.Cane, Rector of Weston, Nott
2 CONC s, after a very romantic courtship on the Nile the previous winter, an
2 CONC d a somewhat stormy engagement. 'The course of true love' did not run
2 CONC so smoothly alas! in their case, as in ours."
2 CONT
2 CONT The 'Canes' are mentioned elsewhere too, e.g. p61
2 CONT
2 CONT Perhaps Brattle is his middle name?
2 CONT
2 CONT His death is recorded in Emily's Memoir, p111
2 CONT
2 CONT His first name is given as John in Emily's Memoir, Appendices, Large F
2 CONC amily Tree
2 CONT
2 CONT In Rev. John Barton's Family Tree book, p23, on p45 it says:
2 CONT "son of Rev. John Brattle Cane of Brackenhurst, Newark, Notts"
