1 NOTE From BBB:
2 CONT b in Dublin 6 Nov 1785.  RN.  Ist-Cl Vol, Aug 1798, "Van Tromp".   Mid
2 CONC shipman "Temeraire", Jun 1799 to end of 1802, in Channel and West Indi
2 CONC es.  Master's Mate, "Constance" (24) 1803.  Ag Lt, "Powerful", Aug 180
2 CONC 5;  Sub-Lt "Imogene" sloop Sep 1805.  Lt Jan 1806.  In Feb 1807 when a
2 CONC  sqn forced the passage of the Dardanelles he was sent ashore with a p
2 CONC arty of seamen and marines to destroy the redoubt and spike the guns.
2 CONC  In Aug 1807 present in "Comus" (22) when she captured a Danish frigat
2 CONC e at Copenhagen.  In Apr 1808 present in "Grasshopper" (18) when in co
2 CONC mpany with other ships she took part in cutting-out action at Rota, ne
2 CONC ar Cadiz, and captured Spanish gunboats and merchantmen off Faro, in S
2 CONC  Portugal.
2 CONT
2 CONT From 1808 successively in "Conqueror" in the Mediterranean;  in "Tened
2 CONC os" on the N American station;  in "Grampus" on the China station;  an
2 CONC d in "Doris" on the E India station.   Invalided from the end of June
2 CONC 1815.  Inspecting Commander in the Coastguard 1824 to 1849.
2 CONT
2 CONT He m 7 Mar 1826 Charlotte, dau of Joseph Packer, Lt RN.  They had issu
2 CONC e: Neil Edmonstone i, Joseph Robert, John Peter Hamilton, Lestock Fran
2 CONC cis ii, Samuel Davis.  Residing at Gorey, Wexford in 1845.  d 25 Mar 1
2 CONC 849.
