1 NOTE From BBB:
2 CONT b at Gorey, Co. Wexford, 8 Apr 1827.  2/Lt Bengal NI, 5 Jul 1843.  Arr
2 CONC ived in India Dec 1843.  Joined 27th NI, Mar 1844 at Moradabad   1st S
2 CONC ikh War, 1845-46;  Sutlej Campaign, inc defence of Ferozepore;  after
2 CONC the battle of Sobraon moved to Lahore;  medal.   Contd with the regt a
2 CONC t various stations till Apr 1851, being appt Interpreter and QM  Appt
2 CONC to duty with the Arakan Bn Apr 1851, and took part in the 2nd Burma Wa
2 CONC r, receiving the medal and clasp "Pegu".   Contd with the regt until A
2 CONC pr 1853, when he went home on furlough;  returning to India in Mar 185
2 CONC 6 he rejoined the 27th NI at Peshawar.  Official Interpreter to his ow
2 CONC n and other regts.
2 CONT
2 CONT In May 1857 he was appt Adjt & QM at Sialkot Musketry Depot, but the c
2 CONC risis arising at Peshawar in connection with the Indian Mutiny, and th
2 CONC e disarmament of the native troops, incl the 27th, prevented him from
2 CONC taking up the appt.   In Aug 1857 was appt 2ic 9th Punjab Infantry, th
2 CONC en being formed at Kohat;  actually he officiated as Comdt, and is cre
2 CONC dited in the Indian Army list with having raised the Bn.  In Jun 1858
2 CONC he joined the Judge Advocate General's branch of the Staff, being appt
2 CONC  DJAG Peshawar;  he continued thus in Peshawar, Jhilum and Rawalpindi
2 CONC Divisions until Dec 1874;  he then, as Lt Col and Brevet Col in the Be
2 CONC ngal Staff Corps retired with the Honorary Rank of Maj-Gen, and d at M
2 CONC urree in the Punjab 21 years later, on 22 Dec 1895.
2 CONT
2 CONT He m 16 Oct 1866, at Mussoorie, Katherine, dau of Richard Bettesworth
2 CONC Flemyng, MA, of Dublin.   They had issue : 8 children : Katherine Edmo
2 CONC nstone, Lillian Mabel, Lestock Richard, Neil Edmonstone ii, Marguerite
2 CONC  le Flemyng, Hugh, Violet Alice Mary and Madeline Bettesworth.
