1 NOTE From BBB:
2 CONT b 26 Jun 1842.  Cadet at Addiscombe Military Seminary, Jun 1861.  On t
2 CONC he closing of that establishment, became a cadet at the RMA Woolwich,
2 CONC Jan 1862.  RE: Lt 18 Dec 1861.  Elected for continuous Indian svc.  PW
2 CONC D, Bombay Sep 1867, and in other parts of India.  Capt 1874;  Major 18
2 CONC 81.  Comd Bengal S&M employed in 1883-84 in the construction of the Ha
2 CONC rnai Rlys;  Sind-Pishin, Baluchistan;  this work was accomplished in t
2 CONC he face of extreme difficulties of terrain, climate and disease.   Lt
2 CONC Col  ??,  Bvt Col 1893.  No active svc.   Retd 1st Oct 1895.  Unmarrie
2 CONC d  d 14 Jun 1902 at Limpley Stoke, near Bath.
