1 NOTE From BBB:
2 CONT b in Dublin 1787.  Bengal Horse Artillery, Cadet and Lt 19 Aug 1804.
2 CONC Joined at Muttra April 1805;  Lt-Fireworker;  took part in the pursuit
2 CONC  of Colkar to the Punjab, Oct-Dec 1805.  (A fireworker was trained in
2 CONC the use of rockets).   To Java 1812, where the Horse Arty were attd to
2 CONC  the Java Light Cavalry, but the force does not seem to have been acti
2 CONC vely engaged  It seems he remained in Java for about two years, and ma
2 CONC y have been back in time to take part in the Nepal EWar;  the records
2 CONC are confused with those of John Peter ii.   Comd 1st Tp, Bengal Horse
2 CONC Arty, at the siege of Hathras, in the Doab Feb-Mar 1817, during the 3r
2 CONC d Mahratta War.   The Horse Arty were commended in despatches.   With
2 CONC the same unit in the Central Div of the Army, in the Pindari War 1817-
2 CONC 18.   To comd Nagpore Div of Arty 18823.  Principal Dep Commissioner o
2 CONC f Ordnance 1824.  Went on leave to the Cape 1826.  Therefater was comd
2 CONC  brigades of Horse Arty in India.  Capt 1815;  Major 1821;  Lt Col 182
2 CONC 7;  Brevet Col 1831.
2 CONT
2 CONT He m at Meerut 31 Jul 1824, May dau of John Clarke, of Bauchor, Invern
2 CONC ess;  they had issue : Thomas Theophilus, John Peter vi;  Charles Elli
2 CONC ot, Simeon Richard, Lestock Alexander, Isabella Annie.  He d 6 Mar 183
2 CONC 8 at the Cape of Good Hope, having just arrived there on furlough.
