1 NOTE From BBB:
2 CONT “In spite of an allowance of £400 a year, a good income in those days,
2 CONC  John ii Elliot _, the eldest, overspent it regularly, failed to pass
2 CONC his examinations, was given a commission, but never took it up, travel
2 CONC led to Italy and Canada and the United States, and could not decide wh
2 CONC at he wanted to do in life.    Eventually he studied the law, was call
2 CONC ed to the Bar, and for two periods acted as Private Secretary to the P
2 CONC rime Minister, Lord John Russell, Lady C's brother-in-law.    Then jus
2 CONC t as the Crimean War was ending, he went out to take a look at it, cau
2 CONC ght or developed pulmonary tuberculosis in Roumania and died of it aft
2 CONC er six wretched years of travelling about in search of a cure, and bei
2 CONC ng treated by doctors who simply did not know the answer.”
