1 NOTE From BBB:
2 CONT b at Alcester, Warwickshire 1798.   Educ Harrow, 1814-17, Christ Churc
2 CONC h College, Oxford, BA 1822, MA 1835.   Took Holy Orders and became Rec
2 CONC tor of Little Bookham Surrey in 1823, continuing as such until his dea
2 CONC th.   He succeeded to the estate of Little Bookham on the death of his
2 CONC  maternal grandfather, and by Royal Letters of 1821 was authorised to
2 CONC use the additional surname of Pollen, thus becoming Boileau-Pollen.
2 CONC  M 1824, Elizabeth Primrose, dau of Sir James Gall, Bart., of Dunglass
2 CONC , Scotland.  She d 1873, having had issue :  2 sons and 2 daus : John
2 CONC Douglas, Charles Edward, Georgina and Elizabeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT George had several apoplectic seizures in 1847 and died that year.  Jo
2 CONC hn Peter iv found that his affairs were better than he had expected, a
2 CONC nd says he thought Elizabeth good but strange.   There are inscribed m
2 CONC onuments for them both at Little Bookham Church where there are also a
2 CONC  number of other inscriptions of Boileau connections.
