1 NOTE From BBB:
2 CONT
2 CONT John Theophilus iv _, having qualified as a doctor at Trinity College,
2 CONC  Dublin, in 1841 and obtained an appointment as an Assistant Surgeon i
2 CONC n the Bengal Medical Service, promptly married a cousin and went off w
2 CONC ith her to India.  But when he reached Calcutta he was sent on to Chin
2 CONC a, where war had broken out, and he died in Hong Kong a year later.
2 CONT
2 CONT Again from BBB:
2 CONT b in Dublin, 21 Mar 1819.   Trinity College, Pensioner, 4 Jul 1836.
2 CONC  BA 1841.   m in Dublin, 28 July 1841, his 2nd cousin, Charlotte Franc
2 CONC es, dau of Col Thomas Hawkins, Bengal NI, by his 2nd wife, Elizabeth F
2 CONC riell, dau of Peter Friell and Anne Charlotte (i) Boileau.   They had
2 CONC issue :  John Theophilus vi.
2 CONT
2 CONT John was appointed Asst Surgeon Bengal Medical Service, 20 Aug 1841, a
2 CONC nd he and Charlotte went straight out to India.   John went on to Chin
2 CONC a, where the first China War had broken out, amd he d at Hong Kong 27
2 CONC Nov 1842.
