1 NOTE Not the Highlander. One hopes. A lieutenant-general in the Bengal army
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------
2 CONT From the Dictionary of National Biography (entry for his son, Donald F
2 CONC riell McLeod):
2 CONT
2 CONT Duncan McLeod, of the McLeods of Assynt, had joined the Bengal Enginee
2 CONC rs in 1794 and eventually became chief engineer for Bengal. Among his
2 CONC creations were the Murshidabad palace and the iron bridge over the Gum
2 CONC ti River at Lucknow. Returning to England in 1841, he became a directo
2 CONC r of the Agra Bank. He died in London on 8 June 1856.
2 CONT -----------------
