1 NOTE From BBB:
2 CONT
2 CONT b probably in Dublin 1821.   Cadet Addiscombe Military Seminary 1938-3
2 CONC 9.   2nd Lt 34th Bengal Native Infantry 1839.   2nd Oudh Irregular Inf
2 CONC antry Adjt 1846;  2ic 1849, Comdt 1856.  Capt 1854.  Bvt Major 1858.
2 CONC Retd, with rank of Lt Col 1862.
2 CONT
2 CONT Actively engaged on several occasions in the province of Oudh 1850-57.
2 CONC   In 1850 commanded a wing of the regiment when, with other troops, it
2 CONC  was employed in putting down a rebellion about 20 miles from Lucknow,
2 CONC  when an attempt was made to take the fort of Bihta by storm.  The att
2 CONC empt was signally repulsed, and 2nd Oudh Infantry lost 7 men killed an
2 CONC d 20 wounded, while the other regt engaged had 40 casualties.   But th
2 CONC e fort was evacuated the same night.
2 CONT
2 CONT In March 1857 he commanded a mixed force of cavalry and infantry in pu
2 CONC rsuit of the outlaw Fazl Ali, who had killed Charles Boileau earlier t
2 CONC hat month.   Fazl Ali was defeated and killed.   George received the t
2 CONC hanks and commendation of Sir Henry Lawrence, Chief Commissioner of Ou
2 CONC dh.  For his services in the campaign he received the thanks of the Go
2 CONC vernor-General-in-Council on several occasions, the brevet rank of maj
2 CONC or and the Indian Mutiny medal.
2 CONT
2 CONT He then joined the Oudh Military Police and took the field in August 1
2 CONC 858 in command of a regiment of cavalry and three regiments of infantr
2 CONC y.   They were engaged in the assault and capture of the fort of Boirw
2 CONC ah, which was described as a difficult undertaking, and George was men
2 CONC tioned in despatches and again thanked by the Governor General.   At t
2 CONC he conclusion of the campaign, he received the approbation of the Quee
2 CONC n in a letter addressed to him by the Secretary of State.
2 CONT
2 CONT Meanwhile his wife Fanny, and their children, had sustained the whole
2 CONC of the siege of the Residency in Lucknow.  a résumé of her experiences
2 CONC  as she recorded them in a diary is to be found in the Chronicles.
2 CONT
2 CONT George retd in 1862 and after a period in Ireland he settled in Norfol
2 CONC k at Hethel Hall, which was one of John Peter's possessions.   He was
2 CONC Lt Col commanding the 1st Norfolk Rifle Volunteers 1869-83, then Hon C
2 CONC ol, and was awarded the Volunteer Decoration.   He was a JP and DL, No
2 CONC rfolk.
2 CONT
2 CONT m 1850 Fanny Elizabeth, dau of General W. Knyvett.  She d in 1895 havi
2 CONC ng had 14 children, as follows :  Anna, Brandram Theophilus, George Wi
2 CONC lliam Knyvett, Georgina Emma, Charles iv, Archibald, Henry Willock, Co
2 CONC lin Campbell, Blanche Etiennette, Madelaine Harriette, Mary Theresa, K
2 CONC nyvett, Lucy Frances, Muriel Knyvett and Edmund Knyvett.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had had a great reputation in India as a tiger hunter.  He d in 190
2 CONC 2.
1 _UID 5A2323FD158E4B42A81ADF2793270DD32F67
1 CHAN
