1 NOTE From BBB:
2 CONT b 1820, probably in Dublin, and nominated to a cadetship in the HEICS
2 CONC by Neil Edmonstone, s-in-law of Anne Charlotte i.   Cadet in the Compa
2 CONC ny's Military Seminary, Addiscombe, 1836-37.    Commissioned as Ensign
2 CONC , Dec 1837 and arrived at Calcutta 1838.   Joined one of the Company's
2 CONC  European regts at Agra.   For his services in the 1st Afghan War, see
2 CONC  the Chronicles, Section 'Afghanistan and Sind'.   Tfd to 35th Bengal
2 CONC NI Nov 1839.   Lt 1841.   Adjt 1843 and official interpreter to the re
2 CONC gt the same year.  Agra 1843-45;  Allahabad 1845;  d at Jehanabad, Bih
2 CONC ar, 1847.    The 35th was one of the best regts of that daym composed
2 CONC of high-caste Brahmans;  it formed a great friendship with the 13th Fo
2 CONC ot, the British regt with which it served during the siege of Jelalaba
2 CONC d, which lasted for two months, March-May 1842.   Edward was entitled
2 CONC to the medal for the Capture of Ghuznee, and that for the Siege of Jel
2 CONC alabad.
2 CONT
2 CONT He m 1846 Caroline Elizabeth Davies, and they had a dau Fanny Elizabet
2 CONC h.
