1 NOTE From BBB:
2 CONT b in Dublin, 10 Mar 1790.  Cadet EICS, 1804;  arrived in India, Sep 18
2 CONC 05.    Ensign, Bengal Native Inf.   Served with Col Ochterlony's det i
2 CONC n the Punjab, 1809.   Appt to comd escort of Major Paris Bradshaw, Nep
2 CONC al Border, 1814.  Svd in Nepal War, 1814-15.  In an action on 24/25 No
2 CONC v 1814 in which he greatly distinguished himself, receiving a deep sab
2 CONC re cut in the face, and slaying his opponent with the help of a sepoy,
2 CONC  he was mentioned in despatches for gallantry, and presented with a sw
2 CONC ord by  Dublin Corporation in recognition of his exploit.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1816 he was appointed  to assist Maj Gen Ochterlony, the victorious
2 CONC  British Comd in the now completed Nepal War and Agent to the Governor
2 CONC -General on the Frontier, in the Political Dept, on account of his loc
2 CONC al knowledge and experience.   For an account of how he became acting
2 CONC Resident in Nepal as a young officer and completely established the co
2 CONC nfidence of the Nepalese, see Section II, 'Nepal, 1814-18' et seq.   E
2 CONC vidently an officer of exceptional quality, both as soldier and admini
2 CONC strator, he might have gone far, if he had not unfortunately died of p
2 CONC enumonia at Patna, whilst on leave on 1st Dec 1818.   He was unmarried
2 CONC .
