1 NAME Samuel Brandrum /Boileau/
2 DISPLAY Samuel Brandrum Boileau
2 GIVN Samuel Brandrum
2 SURN Boileau
1 SOURCES @S74@, @S21@
1 POSITION 7381,149
2 GENOMAP Anne Boileau's descendants
2 BOUNDARYRECT 7344,182,7418,88
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1801
2 SOURCE @S74@
1 DEAT Y
2 DATE 23 DEC 1860
2 SOURCE @S21@
1 ISDEAD Y
1 NOTE From BBB:
2 CONT
2 CONT b in Dublin 15 Jun 1801.  Educ at Trinity Coll, Dublin;  fellow-common
2 CONC er 1819.   Apparently did not graduate.  Ensign (by purchase) 22nd Foo
2 CONC t, 4 Oct 1821;  Lt: 1 Aug 1826.  The regt went back to Jamaica at the
2 CONC end of 1826 from Ireland, and remained there until early 1837;  during
2 CONC  1831-32, it was employed in the suppression of a formidable insurrect
2 CONC ion among the slaves.   It returned to Ireland in 1837, staying there
2 CONC until 1840.  Capt: 1828, and Major: 1836, both by purchase.   Lt Col,
2 CONC by purchase: 1840.   In 1841 the regt went to India, and was in the Sc
2 CONC inde campaign;  but Samuel was not present at the battles of Meeanee a
2 CONC nd Hyderabad, as he appears to have been comd the garrison at Karachi.
2 CONC    The 22nd then returned to Poona;  in 1844-45 took part in ops in S
2 CONC India; and back to Poona and Bombay for the next 4½ years.
2 CONT
2 CONT By 1849 Samuel was comd the Poona Bde, and later that year the regt we
2 CONC nt to the Bengal Presidency, being engaged in 1853 in punitive ops aga
2 CONC inst an Afridi tribe in Peshawar Dist under Samuel's comd (he then hav
2 CONC ing been promoted Col in 1851) successfully completing its mission in
2 CONC one day.  The regt returned to England in 1855;  Samuel went on to hal
2 CONC f-pay in 1857, and was granted the rank of Hon Maj-Gen.
2 CONT
2 CONT He m (1st) in Ireland, 4 Jun 1823, Frances True Bigham;  they had issu
2 CONC e: Jane iii, Frances Maria, Anne v and Elizabeth Ruth.   Frances d in
2 CONC 1843, and Samuel m (2nd) 4 May 1844, Mary Harriet Coombe;  they had is
2 CONC sue: Brandram Henry Sydenham, and Ethelreda Caroline Annie.   Samuel d
2 CONC  at Monkstown, Co. Dublin, 23 Dec 1860.
