1 NOTE From BBB:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1851/1935.   Guinness Brewers.  m Grace Hayes, issue:  three daus, Mar
2 CONC y Elizabeth Etheldreda, Edith Grace, Olive, and a son, Lawrence.
2 CONT
2 CONT Another member of the family engaged in trade in Ireland was Brandram
2 CONC Henry Sydenham _, son of Major General Samuel Brandram i, who entered
2 CONC the employment of Guinness the brewers in 1871 and continued with them
2 CONC  for 47 years, being latterly manager of the firm's store at Belfast.
2 CONT
2 CONT b 1851, prob in India.  Was employed in the brewery firm of Guinness f
2 CONC or 47 years from 1871, working successively in the cask, brewhouse, sh
2 CONC ipping, registry, accounts and trade (travellers) depts, and finally f
2 CONC or some years as Mgr of the firm's Belfast store.    He was remembered
2 CONC  in the firm as a man of outstanding personality.  He m Grace..., and
2 CONC had three daus : Mary Elizabeth Etheldreda, Edith Grace and Olive.  He
2 CONC  d at Teignmouth 1935.
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------
