1 NOTE Graham died from a coronary on his daughter, Christina’s, wedding rece
2 CONC ption (to put a bit of a dampener on things, Mum said, no doubt correc
2 CONC tly).  The story goes that Glenda, another of the daughters, said to h
2 CONC im “If you’d wanted to create a stir, why didn’t you just stand on the
2 CONC  table and down trou.” They carted him out to the ambulance, and the l
2 CONC ast thing he said was “If I’d known this was going to happen, I would
2 CONC have changed my underpants.” He died soon after.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the second world war he had the same rifle number as his father did
2 CONC  in the first world war. Quite a coincidence.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mum says he was very funny, great repartee, and very slick talker. Lov
2 CONC ely man, apparently.
