2 CONC 1735.   Present at the siege of Ingolstadt and in the campaigns in Bav
2 CONC aria 1742-43;  siege of Tournai 1745;  battle of Fontenoy 1745;   batt
2 CONC le of Mesle 1745;  siege of Brussels 1746;  siege of Bergen-op-Zoom 17
2 CONC 47;  battle of Maestricht 1748.    Promoted captain 1745, he was Capta
2 CONC in of Grenadiers in the Regt about 1758, present at the battle of Clos
2 CONC tercamps 1760 and wounded.   Retd as bvt Lt Col 1774.   m 1773 in Pari
2 CONC s, Marie-Anne Babeaud, widow of Regnaud de la Chenay.
2 CONT
2 CONT Normandie was fifth in order of the six senior French regiments of foo
2 CONC t, known collectively as 'les vieux'.   They were permanently embodied
2 CONC , and the purchase of commissions in them was expensive, as it was a l
2 CONC asting investment.   One of Maurice's younger sons, Henri-Camille i, c
2 CONC alled the Chevalier de Castelnau, was also in the Regiment, serving fo
2 CONC r about 40 years, and so was a son of Jean-Louis iii, an Uzès branch c
2 CONC ousin, but he died as quite a young man.
2 CONT
2 CONT 	Henri-Camille was with Normandie at the battle of Fontenoy in 1745, w
2 CONC hen it was part of the picked French reserve, and was one of the Regim
2 CONC ents which, when all else had failed to stop the British and Allied co
2 CONC lumn, was extended along the latter's flank and, by volleys at short r
2 CONC ange, obliged it to withdraw.   Two of the de Vignolles cousins servin
2 CONC g in British Regiments were taken prisoner;  and Henri later recorded
2 CONC with evident delight how he had met them at Lille, and heard news of t
2 CONC he two families.   During his service, he took part in nine campaigns
2 CONC and a number of actions, in the Low Countries, Germany and Bohemia.
2 CONC He was Captain of the Regimental Grenadiers, the picked body which gua
2 CONC rded the Colour and often led the attack.  He was wounded at the Battl
2 CONC e of Clostercamps in 1760, against British and Hanoverians, who were d
2 CONC efeated;  the victory cost Normandie 11 officers killed and 50 wounded
2 CONC , and over 600 men lost.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------
