1 NOTE ------------------
2 CONT From BBB:
2 CONT Another of Maurice's sons, Louis iv, styled Chevalier de Montredon, wa
2 CONC s for nine years in the Regiment de Poitou, taking part in the campaig
2 CONC n in Piedmont in 1744.   Later he transferred to the Regiment de Foix,
2 CONC  with which he was on active service in Westphalia in 1759.
2 CONT ------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT BBB says nothing more about this Louis at all, which is odd. A Chevali
2 CONC er de Montredon appears as a captain in a military list “Etat Militair
2 CONC e de France pour l’annee 1789”. I have no way of knowing whether or no
2 CONC t it’s the same person, but I presume it is.
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis de la Roque in his Armorial de la Noblesse de Languedoc, says th
2 CONC at this Louis, the Chevalier de Montredon, died in 1805 in Nimes.
