1 NOTE This is the Edward Jessup who is the subject of the book “Edward Jessu
2 CONC p of West Farms, Westchester Co., New York, and his Descendants”.. I c
2 CONC all it [JB] for short. This book is widely available online (for a pri
2 CONC ce, of course) and is the definitive work for anybody interested in th
2 CONC is Jessup family. There is far too much detail to include here. It inc
2 CONC ludes a lot of detail of his movements, land purchases, court cases, a
2 CONC nd conflicts with the local Indians.
2 CONT
2 CONT He went to the US before 1649, which is very early, considering that t
2 CONC he Mayflower arrived in 1620 (Jamestown was first established in 1607)
2 CONC , and his will was one of the earliest recorded in English in the US.
2 CONC  [JB] gives the will in full.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was magistrate of Middleborough from 1659-1662, and there are many
2 CONC entries in the records of the town court, apparently in his handwritin
2 CONC g. He was appointed magistrate in Westchester in 1663-1664, where he p
2 CONC urchased from the Indians a tract of land subsequently called West Far
2 CONC ms.
