1 NOTE Rector of Somerton (Bury St. Edmunds), Suffolk Co., from 1799 to 1853.
2 CONC  From Herefordshire, and had been tutor to the Marquis of Downshire, t
2 CONC he patron of Somerton. Also Canon of Ely and chaplain to four successi
2 CONC ve sovereigns (George III, George IV, William IV and Victoria). So say
2 CONC s [JB]. I’m not entirely sure I believe this information. Perhaps.
2 CONT
2 CONT His second wife was Finetta Hale, whom he married in 1831. Why is this
2 CONC  interesting? Well, because there is a Finetta Maddy Boileau, daughter
2 CONC  of John Theophilus (iii) Boileau, who died young. The names cannot be
2 CONC  a coincidence, so there was obviously some connection there, but it’s
2 CONC  not clear what, exactly. Maybe just trying to impress the rich rellie
2 CONC s.
