1 NOTE A George Peddie is buried in the same plot as Janet Peddie and is almo
2 CONC st certainly her elder brother. He was only 4 years older than Janet.
2 CONC George died Sept 14, 1863 of Dropsey.  Aged 29. Draper. Resident of Du
2 CONC nedin. Born Scotland. Lived 5 years in Otago.
2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~nzbound/nzbound/gloucester.ht
2 CONC m says that the “Gloucester”, arrived in Port Chalmer Dec 28 from Lond
2 CONC on had, as passenger, Peddie, G. and Janet. This has to be the same Ge
2 CONC orge Peddie that is buried with Janet and her husband, Adam Sprott Cla
2 CONC rk. The Peddies came out as Second Cabin passengers, not Steerage, so
2 CONC they must have had a bit more money. This squares with the description
2 CONC  of Janet’s father as a writer, Esq.
