1 NOTE Buried at the Carmelite Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was killed at the Reduction of Guadeloupe, commanding the 63rd Regi
2 CONC ment of Foot, blown up while defending the Fort of Basou Terre against
2 CONC  the attack of the Enemy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Letter from the Imperial War Museum and dated 11 Feb 1955:
2 CONT ".... with regard to Lt. Col. Thomas Desbrisay in Col. H.C. Wylly's "H
2 CONC istory of The Manchester Regiment (Late 63rd and 96th Foot), Vol. 1, 1
2 CONC 758 - 1883" published by Forster Groom in 1923, there are several refe
2 CONC rences to Lt. Col. Peter Desbrisay, who had formerly served in the 11t
2 CONC h, 50th, and 52nd Regiments of Foot. On 11th of February 1759, he was
2 CONC appointed Governor of Fort Royal, Guadeloupe. On 23rd March he was kil
2 CONC led during an attack by the French."
