1 NOTE He became a bookseller. He had a son born who was named Edwin born 182
2 CONC 1. William never married the mother Janet Haugh and Edwin died unmarri
2 CONC ed in 1868. William Peddie, a bookseller in King Street, Stirling, die
2 CONC d aged 92 in 1891 at 10 Queen Street, Stirling.
2 CONT
2 CONT In his will William Peddie mentions his  brother James’ children in Ne
2 CONC w Zealand. James Peddie in Dunedin and Mrs Janet Peddie or Clark who w
2 CONC ere both to receive £100 each. (George was dead by this time, as he di
2 CONC ed of dropsy in Dunedin in 1863). Cecilia their sister  was of indepen
2 CONC dent means which I think her father arranged when he remarried. Willia
2 CONC m  also left 2 nieces £100 each, Catherine and Caroline Peddie, childr
2 CONC en of  his brother Robert, who were of an age with Cecilia Peddie who
2 CONC was probably closest to William living as she did in Stirling.
