1 NOTE Death Notes: He died at his home, which was called "Ellen's Grove".
2 CONT Burial Notes: Old Protestant Burying Ground.
2 CONT General Notes: He was a colonial administrator, office holder, and pol
2 CONC itician.
2 CONT
2 CONT From The Dictionary of Canadian Biography, by F.L. Pigot:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Of Huguenot ancestry, Thomas Desbrisay was a member of "one of the ol
2 CONC dest branches of a highly respectable family." Appointed an ensign in
2 CONC the 35th Foot (Donegall's) at the age of 10, he attained the rank of c
2 CONC aptain in the Royal Irish Artillery on 8 Feb 1760. This career was ter
2 CONC minated when on 31 Jul 1769, he was commissioned lieutenant governor,
2 CONC secretary and registrar of St. John's (Prince Edward) Island. Ten year
2 CONC s were to elapse before he took up the appointment. Having acquired la
2 CONC nd on the Island, he busied himself for a few years with attempts to r
2 CONC ecruit settlers in Ireland. In 1773, however, the British Government,
2 CONC unwilling to encourage emigration, expressly forbad him to continue hi
2 CONC s efforts.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 8 Jul 1771, apparently believing that Desbrisay was soon to arrive,
2 CONC  Governor Walter Patterson had appointed him a justice of the peace fo
2 CONC r Queens County. Three years later Patterson was to describe the absen
2 CONC tee lieutenant governor as "very unfit to hold any Offices under His M
2 CONC ajesty." He charged that Desbrisay had attempted to interfere in the p
2 CONC roper allocation of colonial funds; moreover, he had mortgaged his pro
2 CONC perties and, without discharging the mortgages, sold parcels of land t
2 CONC o prospective settlers who were subsequently ruined by the expense of
2 CONC a voyage from the British Isles and the loss of their purchase money,
2 CONC the deeds they had received from Desbrisay being of no effect. Desbris
2 CONC ay was nevertheless retained as lieutenant governor, and in the summer
2 CONC  of 1779 was ordered by the secretary of state for the American Coloni
2 CONC es to take up his appointment."
2 CONT
2 CONT His descendants given in detail in  http://jmw.dynip.com/Genealogy/
