2 CONT Mary Elizabeth i came out with her husband and kinsman, Henry Davis Wi
2 CONC llock, and they went to Shahjehanpore in Oudh, where he was magistrate
2 CONC .   Although in the Civil Service he had served as a Volunteer with th
2 CONC e forces in the Mutiny at Lucknow and in Central India.   Mary's fathe
2 CONC r was Charles Lestock i (2), who had retired to Barnes, and Henry's mo
2 CONC ther was Henrietta ii Boileau.   That small section of the family was
2 CONC very much of the Diplomatic and Civil Service, but that did not save t
2 CONC hem from their share of serious civil unrest and rebellion.
