1 NOTE [C-D, II, 443]. He inherited from his mother, becoming the Baron d’Aub
2 CONC ais et du Caylar, Seigneur de Junas, de Gavernes, de Saussines & de Sa
2 CONC int-Félix. Louis XIII gave him, on 14 Oct 1629, a company of 50 Chevau
2 CONC x-Légers, and in 1632 he prevented the town of Nimes from being taken
2 CONC by the Duc de Montmorency. He distinguished himself at the battle of A
2 CONC vesnes in 1635; and on 24 January 1638 the king gave him one of the pr
2 CONC emier cavalry regiments that had been raised in France. On 11 June 164
2 CONC 2, the prince gave him a commission to command the cavalry of the army
2 CONC  of Catalogne, in a capacity of Mestre-de-Camp-Général; he distinguish
2 CONC ed himself greatly at the battle of Lérida, on 7 Oct 1642; he was made
2 CONC  Maréchal-de-Camp on 31 December 1642, and died at Château d’Aubais on
2 CONC  13 Nov 1646.
