1 NOTE [C-D, XV, 833].
2 CONT [ES XIV:35].
2 CONT ---------------------------------
2 CONT In article <88abeaa.0402161903.7ce8839a@posting.google.com>, p_m_stewa
2 CONC rt@msn.com (Peter Stewart) wrote:
2 CONT According to ES, neue Folge XIV, Tafel 35 this Vierna was daughter of
2 CONC Bertrand, sire d'Anduze who married ca 1150 Adelais de Roquefeuil.
2 CONT However, the same table states that Vierna was herself married before
2 CONC 1161, so at the very least the chronology wasn't carefully worked out.
2 CONC  Vierna was certainly born before 1150.
2 CONT In any case, she was named Vierna de Brissac and belonged to a differe
2 CONC nt family: she called herself daughter of Pons de Agone (whose wife in
2 CONC  1137 was Alamandina), "Eu Vierna de Breisac, que fui filla den Ponszo
2 CONC  Daguo" [_Cartulaire de Gellone_, edited by Paul Alaus, Léon Cassan &
2 CONC E Meynial (Montpellier, 1897), no 368, unseen by me but as quoted by C
2 CONC laudie Duhamel-Amado in _Genèse des lignages méridionaux_, tome I: L'a
2 CONC ristocratie languedocienne du Xe au XIIe siècle (Toulouse, 2001), p 28
2 CONC 6].
2 CONT In 1170 Vierna made a promise of fidelity pending her son Pons Pierre'
2 CONC s coming of age [Cartulaire de Gellone_ no 543 pp 465-466, quoted by D
2 CONC uhamel-Amado, op cit p 320 n 140]. Her younger son Guillem Pierre was
2 CONC bishop of Albi from 1185.
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter Stewart
2 CONT ----------------------------------------------------------
