2 CONT [DHSP, 145]. In 1143 he assisted at the act by which Alphonse-Jourdain
2 CONC , Count of Toulouse, paid homage to the Archbishop of Arles. In 1155,
2 CONC he and his wife, as well as their son Rainon, confirmed the donation o
2 CONC f the town Saint-Maurice, with all its dependencies, & 4,000 sols, fro
2 CONC m the mother and father of Roscie to Pierre de Vezenobre. In 1156 he a
2 CONC nd his brother Guillaume III participated in the peace treaty between
2 CONC the Count of Barcelona and Hugues de Baux and his brothers. Rostaing p
2 CONC layed an important role in the war which the Count of Barcelona, the u
2 CONC ncle and tutor of the Count of Provence, waged with the house of Baux,
2 CONC  from 1151 to 1161, for the possession of Provence. He was not living
2 CONC in August, 1180, when his wife and his son Rainon approved the sale of
2 CONC  some land.
2 CONT [C-D, XVIII, 8].
2 CONT [ES, XIV, 179].
