1 NOTE Went from Ivegill to Carlisle.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to BB, quoted in MFG:
2 CONT "Why did his son, my grandfather, after whom I was
2 CONT named, ever leave that pleasant dale, and go
2 CONT and set up a manufactory in Carlisle; in-
2 CONT venting a piece of machinery J for which he
2 CONT had a medal from the Royal Society?  so
2 CONT says Pennant."
2 CONT
2 CONT Footnote by EF in MFG:
2 CONT The manufactory was one of calico-printing. The
2 CONT "piece of machinery " is thus described by Pennant :
2 CONT "Saw at Mr. Bernard Barton's a pleasing sight of
2 CONT twelve little girls spinning at once at a horizontal wheel,
2 CONT which set twelve bobbins in motion ; yet so contrived,
2 CONT that should any accident happen to one, the motion of
2 CONT that might be stopped without any impediment to the
2 CONT others."
2 CONT
2 CONT Invented spinning jenny modification:
2 CONT
2 CONT from http://www.theloomexchange.co.uk/books.htm:
2 CONT "Twelve Bobbins Spinning" - the story surrounding a horizontal flax wh
2 CONC eel invented by Bernard Barton c1766 £1
2 CONT
2 CONT Age and dates of death, plus some additional info on his family, given
2 CONC  in:
2 CONT Bernard Barton and His Friends: A Record of Quiet Lives. By Verrall Lu
2 CONC cas, p16
2 CONT see: http://books.google.co.uk/books?id=2z7iH9FIS58C&pg=PA15&dq=john+b
2 CONC arton+of+ivegill&lr=
2 CONT
2 CONT Dates and names (including wife and dead infants) given in
2 CONT Transactions of the Cumberland & Westmorland Antiquarian & Archaeologi
2 CONC cal Society volume 7, 1884
2 CONT Available online at: http://www.archive.org/details/transactionsofcu07
2 CONC cumb
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Also given in "Annals of Smith..."
2 CONT
2 CONT Mentioned in his mother Ann's will. His signature is on a related docu
2 CONC ment.
2 CONT
2 CONT In Rev. John Barton's Family Tree book, p6.
2 CONT
