1 NOTE http://www.chichesterquakers.org/John%20Barton.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Details in 'Barton Family Tree' from Robert Barton's biography of John
2 CONC  Barton of Chicester.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mentioned in Emily's Memoir In Emily's Memoir, p95-96:
2 CONT "Carol brought the four younger ones direct to Peel from Cambridge; an
2 CONC d I think Fred and Cecil cycled to Barrow and crossed thence to the Is
2 CONC land; or that C. was in N.Ireland that summer with John Robinson of Ch
2 CONC rist Coll. and only Fred came to Peel.  Alice was with us also this mo
2 CONC nth; and it was here that we received the sad news of her brother Cam'
2 CONC s death in Sierra Leone.  This was a heavy blow in every way to his go
2 CONC od Father (Un. Joseph) who lent much on his eldest son; and looked to
2 CONC him to father the four young step brothers and sisters when he should
2 CONC himself be taken.  Dear 'Cam' was most genuinely mourned by the young
2 CONC cousins, as he deserved; and they can never forget his unselfish devot
2 CONC ion to them all."
2 CONT
2 CONT Lived at East Leigh, Havant, until his death (Emily's Memoir, p128)
2 CONT
2 CONT Full name and d.o.b. in Rev. John Barton's Family Tree book, p10, 12
