1 NOTE Details in 'Barton Family Tree' from Robert Barton's biography of John
2 CONC  Barton of Chicester.
2 CONT
2 CONT In Emily's Memoir, p95-96:
2 CONT "June 20.1887 was our beloved Queen Victoria's Jubilee Anniversary, an
2 CONC d we had great illuminations & decorations in Cambridge, though we did
2 CONC  not go to London.  In July Father & I went to Lowestoft as I had been
2 CONC  ill, and took rooms near Uncle Gerard, whom I then saw for the last t
2 CONC ime.  Madge sat by him shampooing his poor paralized hands and legs to
2 CONC  ease him. He was only 52 but had suffered from 'creeping palsey' for
2 CONC 7 years.  His was a philosophical and reverent mind; he was a deep stu
2 CONC dent of theology, and something of a mystic.  He took a very unusual s
2 CONC tep in being ordained at 40 by the Bishop of Norwich, after having far
2 CONC med his own land at Fundenhall, Norfolk for years; and acted as Chapla
2 CONC in to his tenants there as a layman, no clergyman being resident there
2 CONC .  He had a very steady eye, and quiet restrained manner; and impresse
2 CONC d you always with the idea that he left unsaid a good deal more than h
2 CONC e said of what was in his mind on any given subject."
2 CONT
2 CONT Full name and d.o.b. in Rev. John Barton's Family Tree book, p16
2 CONT
2 CONT In Emily's Memoir, Appendices: The John Barton Family
