1 NAME Elspeth /Arnott/
2 DISPLAY Elspeth Arnott
2 GIVN Elspeth
2 SURN Arnott
1 POSITION -14060,-4380
2 BOUNDARYRECT -14097,-4347,-14023,-4427
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1917
1 DEAT Y
2 DATE 2001
1 ISDEAD Y
1 NOTE Year of death from Barton family tree (hand-drawn by Malcolm Barton)
2 CONT
2 CONT MAJB met Elspeth and I have a letter from her enquiring about the fami
2 CONC ly history (plus a hand-written family tree):
2 CONT The letter reads:
2 CONT
2 CONT "28 Crick Road, Rugby, CV21 4DX
2 CONT 22nd Jan
2 CONT Dear Margaret,
2 CONT I hope you remember me - we met at Southwell Regional Day, and discove
2 CONC red a mutual relationship in the six Barton brothers. You very kindly
2 CONC said that you would send me a copy of the family tree. Unfortunately,
2 CONC since my grandmother [Lilian Wyatt] divorced my grandfather [Arthur El
2 CONC liott Barton] and my surviving aunt [Vyvian Griffith nee Barton?] died
2 CONC , I really know very little about the Barton side of the family, and w
2 CONC ould love to know more. You also said you had a copy of the biography
2 CONC of ? The Rev Elliott - or was it Barton - I believe Ted Barton once sh
2 CONC owed me a copy.
2 CONT I do hope I'm not asking too much - but I don't like to bother Bernard
2 CONC  Barton for details, and haven't the address of any of his sons.
2 CONT With all good wishes
2 CONT Yours sincerely,
2 CONT Elspeth (Gardner)
2 CONT nee Arnott - mother Doris Barton, grandmother Lilian Barton."
1 FAMC @fam155588772@
1 FAMS @fam155588774@
1 FAMS @fam155588775@
