2 CONT Later a prosperous coal merchant with a town house near his business a
2 CONC t Bankside, Southwark, looking out across the river (Southwark Bridge
2 CONC not built then) and a country house in Tottenham.
2 CONT d 1802- buried (like his father and his wife) at Friends burial ground
2 CONC , Long Lane, Bermondsey
2 CONT
2 CONT Details of descendants given in NJB Papers: "The Hornes and Jansons" t
2 CONC ree.
2 CONT
2 CONT NJB Papers: "From Quaker records in the London Euston Road Library" gi
2 CONC ves year of birth as 1726, and says he is 'of Old Street London'.
