1 NOTE from
2 CONT The Elliots: The Story of a Border Clan, a genealogical history. By Th
2 CONC e Dowager Lady Eliott of Stobs and Sir Arthur Eliott, 11th Baronet of
2 CONC Stobs. Published 1974. ISBN 0 85422 081 X.
2 CONT p170
2 CONT
2 CONT "With his brother he took part in the Jacobite Rising of 1715, and bei
2 CONC ng wounded at Preston, was smuggled out of the Kingdom by his family,
2 CONC who adhered to the Hanoverian dynasty. He took refuge in Holland, wher
2 CONC e he married a Dutch lady of good family, by whose influence he obtain
2 CONC ed a post in the Dutch East India Company in Java. Eventually his outl
2 CONC awry was reversed and he settled in Essex, first at Maldon and later a
2 CONC t Burnham. His brother also lived in Java for many years, and his desc
2 CONC endants migrated to California, where the family is still represented.
2 CONC  Charles Edward has issue twelve children, of whom the first nine were
2 CONC  born in Java and died young."
