1 NOTE from NJB Papers: "From Quaker records in the London Euston Road Librar
2 CONC y"
2 CONT
2 CONT Vivienne Lewis (nee Horne) quoted at http://bloomsburypeople.blogspot.
2 CONC com/2009/03/horne-family-and-benjamin-franklin.html:
2 CONT
2 CONT "I found the modern day descendents of the Horne branch which emigrate
2 CONC d to America in the early 1700s to Philadelphia. Benjamin Horne, who w
2 CONC as the founder of the coal merchant business, had an elder brother cal
2 CONC led Edward who emigrated with a number of other Quakers. I googled 'Be
2 CONC njamin Horne' and came up with a family tree of the Knox-Johnson famil
2 CONC y who were descended from Edward and Benjamin's mother and father, Tho
2 CONC mas and Susannah Horne. I contacted them and they were amazed as they
2 CONC had only known about Edward and five of his siblings, and were unaware
2 CONC  that there were four more children. They have now added the family tr
2 CONC ee that Rosemary and I had compiled, to their own.
2 CONT
2 CONT I have also found a reference to Edward Horne being a friend and mento
2 CONC r to the young Benjamin Franklin, but have been unable to verify this
2 CONC as yet."
