1 NOTE from NJB Papers: "Rickman Family Tree"
2 CONT
2 CONT DBHB: This tree appears to have the later Rickmans (tentatively) desce
2 CONC nded from this John Rickman and Margaret Edwards. It's a poor quality
2 CONC photocopy though, with a note in a box that I can't read.
2 CONT
2 CONT At any rate "The Hack Family Documents by Chris Durrant", Figure O.9 i
2 CONC s less ambiguous and has the later Rickmans descended from a Joseph Ri
2 CONC ckman who was married in 1713. This seems unlikely to be the elder Jos
2 CONC eph Rickman in the NJB Papers "Rickman Family Tree", whose dates are g
2 CONC iven as 1657-1745, as he would be getting married when he was 56! It c
2 CONC ould be that John Rickman and Margaret Edwards had a son called Joseph
2 CONC  who got married in 1713, when John was 57.
2 CONT
2 CONT Since there it's so ambiguous at the moment, I won't link the two toge
2 CONC ther.
