2 CONT
2 CONT In http://www.chichesterquakers.org/John%20Barton.htm:
2 CONT
2 CONT Fanny's guardian, James Rickman, was concemed as to whether John could
2 CONC  provide Fanny with 'those comforts the wife of a person of such prope
2 CONC rty should have', as her own income would only amount to about £110 pe
2 CONC r annum and Barton apparently had a reputation for living very simply;
2 CONC  although in 1827 he estimated his income and outgoings to be £770 and
2 CONC  £600 respectively. Fanny was some 18 years younger than her husband a
2 CONC nd she produced nine children between 1829 and 1842.
