1 NOTE from
2 CONT The Elliots: The Story of a Border Clan, a genealogical history. By Th
2 CONC e Dowager Lady Eliott of Stobs and Sir Arthur Eliott, 11th Baronet of
2 CONC Stobs. Published 1974. ISBN 0 85422 081 X.
2 CONT
2 CONT on p10: '"dau. of Buccleuch"
2 CONT on p33: a "sister of Buccleuch"
2 CONT on p349: a "sister of Buccleuch"
2 CONT
2 CONT She was married ~1550 (p32), so can't have been the daughter of "the B
2 CONC old Buccleuch" Walter Scott, 1st Lord Scott of Buccleuch (1565 – 15 De
2 CONC cember 1611; http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walter_Scott,_1st_Lord_Scott
2 CONC _of_Buccleuch)
2 CONT
2 CONT At http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walter_Scott_of_Branxholme_and_Buccleu
2 CONC ch#Murder, it says the "Bold Buccleuch" was the son of Sir Walter Scot
2 CONC t (d. 1574), who was the son of William Scott of Kincurd (d. May 1552)
2 CONC , who was son of Sir Walter Scott of Branxholme and Buccleuch, 3rd lor
2 CONC d of Buccleuch (c. 1495–killed 4 October 1552), known as "Wicked Wat"
2 CONC (see above link).
2 CONT Most likely, from the dates, Jean Scott was a daughter of Wicked Wat a
2 CONC nd a sister of William Scott of Kincurd.
1 FAMS @fam155588887@
1 FAMS @fam155588892@
