2 BOUNDARYRECT 77,133,163,39
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 15 AUG 1840
1 DEAT Y
2 DATE 1924?
1 ISDEAD Y
1 NOTE from
2 CONT The Elliots: The Story of a Border Clan, a genealogical history. By Th
2 CONC e Dowager Lady Eliott of Stobs and Sir Arthur Eliott, 11th Baronet of
2 CONC Stobs. Published 1974. ISBN 0 85422 081 X.
2 CONT p174
2 CONT
2 CONT In Rev. John Barton's Family Tree book, p51, with note: "Mr Young knig
2 CONC hted K.C.S.I. and Lt Govr Punjab 1897-1902"
2 CONT
2 CONT Mentioned in Emily's Memoir, p43; John and Emily first met him in Indi
2 CONC a, while on their way to Calcutta to return to England a few months af
2 CONC ter their marriage. He was brother of John's college friend Sir George
2 CONC  Young.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is also (at least, it's probably him) mentioned in http://rulers.or
2 CONC g/indprov.html:
2 CONT Chief Commissioner of Coorg
2 CONT 18 Sep 1895 -  7 Dec 1896  William Mackworth Young            (b. 1840
2 CONC  - d. 1924)
2 CONT
2 CONT There is a later William Mackworth Young, possibly related, listed at
2 CONC http://thepeerage.com/p25089.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT
