1 NAME Handley Carr Glyn /Moule/
2 DISPLAY Rev. Handley Carr Glyn Moule
3 FORMAT Custom
2 GIVN Handley
2 MIDDLE Carr Glyn
2 SURN Moule
2 NPFX Rev.
1 POSITION -30,160
2 GENOMAP Family of (Mary) Harriet Mary Moule nee Elliott
2 BOUNDARYRECT -69,193,10,99
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 23 DEC 1841
1 DEAT Y
2 DATE 8 MAY 1920
1 ISDEAD Y
1 NOTE from
2 CONT The Elliots: The Story of a Border Clan, a genealogical history. By Th
2 CONC e Dowager Lady Eliott of Stobs and Sir Arthur Eliott, 11th Baronet of
2 CONC Stobs. Published 1974. ISBN 0 85422 081 X.
2 CONT p174
2 CONT
2 CONT Vicar of Fordington, Dorset; became Bishop of Durham
2 CONT The 'Vicar of Fordington' bit may be a mistake, based on Rev. John Bar
2 CONC ton's Family Tree book, p53, where that note appears to apply to his f
2 CONC ather.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Principal of Ridley Hall, Cambridge
2 CONT
2 CONT Emily's Memoir, p86:
2 CONT "In 1879 or '80 we saw the foundation stone laid of Ridley Hall - at N
2 CONC ewnham – and your Father being one of the Council of this new Theologi
2 CONC cal College, persuaded Mr.Handley Moule (46), after some difficulty, t
2 CONC o accept the post of Principal of this Hall, when opened, and to combi
2 CONC ne with it the Evening Lectureship at Holy Trinity Church.  He was wel
2 CONC l known in Cambridge, having been Dean of Trinity College for some yea
2 CONC rs - but had given up this post three years previously in order to act
2 CONC  as curate to his revered old Father at Dorchester - whose death in 18
2 CONC 60 set his son free to return to Cambridge; and many both amongst 'tow
2 CONC n and gown' rejoiced at his return.
2 CONT In January 1881 'Ridley' was opened with its first 8 graduate students
2 CONC .  Canon Girdlestone, who was one of the large company present on the
2 CONC occasion, when congratulating Father on his success in persuading the
2 CONC new Principal to accept the post, added (prophetically!) "the next thi
2 CONC ng you must do is to get him a good wife"!  The remark was not made se
2 CONC riously - and at the time nothing seemed more unlikely; and yet, as yo
2 CONC u all know, that very year, in August '81, he married your Aunt Mary (
2 CONC 26) and became your 'Uncle Handley' - and has ever since enriched our
2 CONC family by his prayers, his sermons, and many other gifts; and has prov
2 CONC ed a 'Brother indeed' - for no man living loves your Father so much."
1 HYPERLINK http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Handley_Moule
