1 NAME Mary Amy /Elliott/
2 DISPLAY Mary Amy Elliott
2 GIVN Mary
2 MIDDLE Amy
2 SURN Elliott
1 POSITION 3210,-780
2 GENOMAP Other Eliotts, Ellots, Elliotts
2 BOUNDARYRECT 3173,-747,3247,-841
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 13 APR 1867
1 DEAT Y
2 DATE 1947
1 ISDEAD Y
1 NOTE from
2 CONT The Elliots: The Story of a Border Clan, a genealogical history. By Th
2 CONC e Dowager Lady Eliott of Stobs and Sir Arthur Eliott, 11th Baronet of
2 CONC Stobs. Published 1974. ISBN 0 85422 081 X.
2 CONT p177
2 CONT
2 CONT had issue
2 CONT
2 CONT The above gives her year of birth as 1876, which is probably a mistake
2 CONC  since she is listed first amongst the children. Moreover, Emily's mem
2 CONC oir, p48, says:
2 CONT
2 CONT "[In 1867] I spent a quiet month at Fatehgarh, N.W. Provinces, with my
2 CONC  cousins the C.A.Elliotts (34) keeping the Baby-boy, while Father took
2 CONC  Arthur, now nearly 3 years old, to Simla.  He wrote me that Arthur wa
2 CONC lked & rode famously everywhere, proving quite a companion to him.  Ou
2 CONC r friends, Dr. & Mrs.Farquhar put them up, in one of the houses occupi
2 CONC ed by Lord Lawrence's suite, as Dr.P. was his private medical attendan
2 CONC t.  Meanwhile my cousin, Louise Elliott (1st wife of the present Sir C
2 CONC harles Elliott) and I, enjoyed ourselves quietly with our little ones
2 CONC - their 'Minnie' being a little older than our 'Johnnie'. Harry & Alfy
2 CONC , whom you all know, & Frank, were not then born."
2 CONT
2 CONT 'Minnie' must be Mary (Harry=Henry, Alfy=Alfred), so the above suggest
2 CONC s that Mary was probably born in 1866, not 1876.
2 CONT
2 CONT In Rev. John Barton's Family Tree book, p33, 63 it clarifies the issue
2 CONC  with the date here used.
1 FAMC @fam155588965@
1 FAMS @fam155588984@
