2 CONC ed by Mrs.Llewelyn, Susie's aunt, and where she has finished building
2 CONC a Church begun by her husband who had died four years previously, for
2 CONC the thousands who live in and over his mines.  They spent £25,000 on t
2 CONC his beautiful Church, sparing no money to procure marbles & carving wh
2 CONC erewith to embellish God's House.  When complete Mrs.Llewelyn had a sm
2 CONC all brass plate let into the marble Chancel wall giving her husband's
2 CONC name and date of death &c. and underneath these words "Of Thine own ha
2 CONC ve we given Thee"."
