1 NOTE From Malcolm's "Descendants of Samuel Smith" doc.
2 CONT
2 CONT Governor of Bank of England 1793-5
2 CONT Of Moggerhanger House, Moggerhanger
2 CONT Got Sir John Soane to redesign house - now grade 1 listed
2 CONT Wilberforce probably stayed en route for his Yorks constituency
2 CONT
2 CONT Additional details (including above) from email from Malcolm dated 15
2 CONC October 2009:
2 CONT
2 CONT "> Extracts from Thornton family tree
2 CONT > >
2 CONT > > Godfrey Thornton b. 16/10/1737  d. 5/11/1805
2 CONT > >    Governor of Bank of England 1793-5
2 CONT > >    of Moggerhanger House, Moggerhanger,
2 CONT > >    Got Sir John Soane to redesign house -
2 CONT > now grade 1 listed
2 CONT > >    Wilberforce probably stayed en route for
2 CONT > his Yorks constituency
2 CONT > >    >
2 CONT > >    Stephen Thornton (eldest son) inherited
2 CONT > MH b. 8/7/1767 d. 26/8/1850
2 CONT > >    Director of B of E
2 CONT > >
2 CONT > > Claude George Thornton 3rd son of Godfrey above b.
2 CONT > 20/1/1776 d. 4/8/1866
2 CONT > > (aged 90!)
2 CONT > >
2 CONT > > The Revd. Spencer Thornton 2nd son of Claude George
2 CONT > above b. 12/10/1814 d.
2 CONT > > 12/1/1850
2 CONT > >
2 CONT > > Henry Edward Thornton 2nd son of Spencer above b.
2 CONT > 31/10/1842 d. 26/10/1926
2 CONT > >    Partner in Smiths Bank, Nottingham
2 CONT > >    m 15/2/1871 (1) Katherine Charlotte
2 CONT > Grenfell daughter of Pascoe St Leger
2 CONT > > Grenfell
2 CONT > >
2 CONT > > Susan Theresa Thornton 2nd daughter of HET b. 3/3/1875
2 CONT > d. 30/7/1958
2 CONT > >    m 31/7/1895 The Revd John Bernard Barton
2 CONT > >
2 CONT > > BCLB etc."
1 FAMS @fam155589131@
