1 NAME John Campbell /Barton/
2 DISPLAY (Cam) John Campbell Barton
3 FORMAT Custom
2 GIVN John
2 MIDDLE Campbell
2 SURN Barton
2 NICK Cam
1 POSITION -15280,-3940
2 BOUNDARYRECT -15317,-3907,-15243,-4001
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 30 NOV 1858
1 DEAT Y
2 DATE 20 AUG 1889
1 ISDEAD Y
1 NOTE Full name and d.o.b/d. in Rev. John Barton's Family Tree book, p12
2 CONT
2 CONT In Emily's Memoir, p93-94:
2 CONT "In July '85 we had a delightful family gathering at Colwyn Bay, a Wel
2 CONC sh resort which will always be associated with dear 'Cam' who died in
2 CONC his prime four years later of blackwater fever in Sierra Leone.  The M
2 CONC ackworth Youngs (30) (47), and their baby boys Gerard & Hubert, and Is
2 CONC a, you three elder Boys and Ethel (at Cam's special invitation), Aunt
2 CONC Emily Barton, Effie and Alice, besides the whole Causton clan, made a
2 CONC party of 30 in different houses.  Most of us met for morning prayers a
2 CONC t 'Penrhyn Ho.' and for evenings of singing, where Uncle Willy conduct
2 CONC ed the large choir of voices; and joined in the many long excursions a
2 CONC nd picnics arranged by your Father and Aunt Phena, who were the two en
2 CONC terprising spirits.  'Cam' was the idol of all the young ones; because
2 CONC  he loved them, and had great sympathy with those on the threshold of
2 CONC life.  He was on leave from his Regt. in Jamaica, and this autumn was
2 CONC a turning point in his life in more senses than one.  He was keen on t
2 CONC emperance too; having realized that alcohol is injurious, as well as a
2 CONC n unnecessary luxury for young people in health; and made his cousins
2 CONC sew a bit of blue ribbon on to all his coats. He stayed with us at Tri
2 CONC nity Vicarage later in the year, and drew Jack & Ethel together as fri
2 CONC ends; and proved a wise counsellor to Arthur who that autumn joined hi
2 CONC s Regt., The Kings Own Yorkshire Light Infy. at Malta - accompanied by
2 CONC  many prayers."
2 CONT
2 CONT Death in p95-96:
2 CONT "Carol brought the four younger ones direct to Peel from Cambridge; an
2 CONC d I think Fred and Cecil cycled to Barrow and crossed thence to the Is
2 CONC land; or that C. was in N.Ireland that summer with John Robinson of Ch
2 CONC rist Coll. and only Fred came to Peel.  Alice was with us also this mo
2 CONC nth; and it was here that we received the sad news of her brother Cam'
2 CONC s death in Sierra Leone.  This was a heavy blow in every way to his go
2 CONC od Father (Un. Joseph) who lent much on his eldest son; and looked to
2 CONC him to father the four young step brothers and sisters when he should
2 CONC himself be taken.  Dear 'Cam' was most genuinely mourned by the young
2 CONC cousins, as he deserved; and they can never forget his unselfish devot
2 CONC ion to them all."
2 CONT
2 CONT
1 FAMC @fam155589144@
