1 NOTE In Emily's Memoir, p95-96:
2 CONT "June 20.1887 was our beloved Queen Victoria's Jubilee Anniversary, an
2 CONC d we had great illuminations & decorations in Cambridge, though we did
2 CONC  not go to London.  In July Father & I went to Lowestoft as I had been
2 CONC  ill, and took rooms near Uncle Gerard, whom I then saw for the last t
2 CONC ime.  Madge sat by him shampooing his poor paralized hands and legs to
2 CONC  ease him. He was only 52 but had suffered from 'creeping palsey' for
2 CONC 7 years."
2 CONT
2 CONT In Emily's Memoir, Appendices: The John Barton Family
2 CONT
