2 DATE ~1720
1 ISDEAD Y
1 NOTE This John's death is not recorded in the Dalston Parish Registers, but
2 CONC  we do have his will and associated documents.
2 CONT He gives his point of origin as Ivegill Head, Hesket.
2 CONT The will is in the Index to the wills proved in the Consistory court o
2 CONC f Carlisle, 1661-1750; Published by British Record Society, 1998, as:
2 CONT "John, yeo., Hesket-in-the-Forest (Ivegill Head). 1720 WI"
2 CONT Hesket is just a couple of miles to the east of Ivegill.
2 CONT
2 CONT He names his sons (an elder son William and another son John), and his
2 CONC  wife Isabell. There are signatures for all three on a document relati
2 CONC ng to the execution of this will, and the signature of John closely re
2 CONC sembles the signature of John Barton who died in 1747. On this basis,
2 CONC I hesitantly conclude that they are father and son.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Barton house at Ivegill has the following inscription in the linte
2 CONC l above the door (see pictures):
2 CONT "IB:IB * 1694"
2 CONT These initials might very well stand for John Barton : Isabell Barton
2 CONT
2 CONT
