1 NOTE The Parish registers of Dalston, Cumberland. Edited with an introducti
2 CONC on and indexes by James Wilson . Vol.2: Baptisms, 1679-1812; marriages
2 CONC , 1679-1812; burials, 1678-1812; 1895:
2 CONT "1715 / Novemb 14 Barnard Barton of Hivegill buried"
2 CONT
2 CONT We have his will. Dated Oct 22 1715, it begins “I Bernard Barton”, but
2 CONC  is very clearly signed “Barnard Barton”, and this looks very much lik
2 CONC e (a shakier version of) the signature on the 1682 Highhead Chapel doc
2 CONC ument.
2 CONT Mentions son John Barton, daughter Margaret Barton, son Bernard Barton
2 CONC , daughter Jane Barton, wife and executor Maball (?) Barton.
2 CONT Witnessed by John Barton (son? Very different signature from other Joh
2 CONC ns we have signatures for) and Robert Fidler (?) who signs his mark ‘R
2 CONC ’.
2 CONT Will also contains line:
2 CONT “& for my body, I commend it to the Earth to be Buried in a Christian-
2 CONC like & decent manner in Dalston Church yard”
2 CONT
2 CONT Transactions of the Cumberland & Westmorland Antiquarian & Archaeologi
2 CONC cal Society, Volume 5, 1905 p96-97 mentions a Bernard Barton of Ivegil
2 CONC l licensed as reader and schoolmaster in 1713, and ordained deacon in
2 CONC 1715. Maybe this is he, and he died soon after (seems unlikely, since
2 CONC the next curate was appointed in 1721) or maybe (more likely, I think)
2 CONC  it is his son Bernard.
