1 NAME Grace /Trotter/
2 DISPLAY Grace Trotter
2 GIVN Grace
2 SURN Trotter
1 POSITION -2070,400
2 GENOMAP Thornton ancestors
2 BOUNDARYRECT -2096,426,-2044,353
1 SEX F
1 NOTE Mentioned in Emily's Memoir, p106:
2 CONT "In May [1894] I had found myself seated at the C.M.S. Annual Meeting,
2 CONC  at Exeter Hall, behind Mr.H.E.Thornton, and spoke to him for the firs
2 CONC t time though we had known and loved his mother, Mrs. Spencer Thornton
2 CONC , & sisters at Broxbourne for years.  Mr.Thornton asked me whether our
2 CONC  son Jack was in the Hall? as he had often heard of but never seen him
2 CONC ; and I pointed Jack out to his future Father-in-law!  A week later th
2 CONC e Father received one of Mr.H.E.T's amusing postcards saying "Swansea
2 CONC Vicarage is to let; and we are to be at the Grenfells' old home there
2 CONC en famille. Do come." And thus it came about that our two families wer
2 CONC e thrown together almost daily for a month.  Six young Thorntons, and
2 CONC their cousin Grace Trotter and five of ours swam dived and bathed, cyc
2 CONC led walked picniced and sang together whilst we six elders, the Thornt
2 CONC ons Trotters and ourselves, talked over many mutual interests.  Amongs
2 CONC t these the Welsh clergy were not forgotten, and Father convened a gat
2 CONC hering of 40 of these for the day, and we entertained them at luncheon
2 CONC  and tea at a Parish Hall in Swansea before and after their discussion
2 CONC s."
