1 TITL BBB
1 SUBTITLE The Chronicles of the Family of Boileau known as de Castelnau de la Ga
2 CONC rde de Sainte-Croix de Boiriac; Digby Whicher Boileau et al
1 DESCRIPTION Compiled by DIGBY WHICHER BOILEAU over many years and  up to his death
2 CONC  at the age of 82, in 1976. Subsequently the work was continued by his
2 CONC  brother,  THOMAS WHICHER BOILEAU, who produced the first version of t
2 CONC he book before his own death at the age of 85. This later, and where p
2 CONC ossible, more complete<BR>version is now presented by PETER MUDIE BOIL
2 CONC EAU, son of Digby and nephew of Tom. A detailed, and very well sourced
2 CONC , history of the Boileau family. With thanks to Vincent O’Grady for se
2 CONC nding this to me. <BR><BR>As a chronicle it’s heavily weighted towards
2 CONC  military matters, which are described in loving detail. The wives and
2 CONC  daughters get very little mention at all, except when they impinge br
2 CONC iefly on more manly pursuits, like killing people.
1 MEDIATYPE Book
1 ORIGINATOR Digby Whicher Boileau
1 QUOTEDTEXT BBB:  The Chronicles of the Family of Boileau known as de Castelnau de
2 CONC  la Garde de Sainte-Croix de Boiriac, Compiled by DIGBY WHICHER BOILEA
2 CONC U over many years and  up to his death at the age of 82, in 1976. Subs
2 CONC equently the work was continued by his brother,  THOMAS WHICHER BOILEA
2 CONC U, who produced the first version of the book before his own death at
2 CONC the age of 85. This later, and where possible, more complete
2 CONT version is now presented by PETER MUDIE BOILEAU, son of Digby and neph
2 CONC ew of Tom. A detailed, and very well sourced, history of the Boileau f
2 CONC amily. With thanks to Vincent O’Grady for sending this to me.
2 CONT
2 CONT As a chronicle it’s heavily weighted towards military matters, which a
2 CONC re described in loving detail. The wives and daughters get very little
2 CONC  mention at all, except when they impinge briefly on more manly pursui
2 CONC ts, like killing people.
