1 TITL BBC
1 SUBTITLE The Big Boileau Chart
1 DESCRIPTION This is the chart of Boileau descendants that was finished and compile
2 CONC d in December 1867 by Jane Alicia Innes, and a copy of which is still
2 CONC in the possession of Chris Read, who sent me a copy. It is clearly the
2 CONC  original from which Granny copied out her Red Book, and also the orig
2 CONC inal of the chart owned by Leigh Boileau. It has handwritten additions
2 CONC  from the 1890s on.<BR><BR>Of course, its information is only as relia
2 CONC ble as that given to the original compositor, as she herself points ou
2 CONC t on the chart.<BR><BR>The dates and names are often difficult to read
2 CONC , and thus the information shown here, as I’ve transcribed from the ch
2 CONC art, might be faulty in places. Tough. So sue me.<BR><BR>BBB refers on
2 CONC ce to something it calls “The Innes chart”. It’s hard to believe that
2 CONC this refers to something other than this chart, but no more detail is
2 CONC given. Furthermore, the reference in BBB to the Innes chart doesn’t se
2 CONC em to be consistent with the chart I’ve seen. It seems to be referring
2 CONC  to something quite different. Unlikely though this might seem, it’s p
2 CONC ossible that BBB didn’t refer to this chart at all. However, in BBB th
2 CONC ere is another oblique reference made to an attempt to list all the de
2 CONC scendants, including those in the female line, and this almost certain
2 CONC ly refers to this chart.
1 MEDIATYPE Document
1 QUOTEDTEXT BBC: The Big Boileau Chart. This is the chart of Boileau descendants t
2 CONC hat was finished and compiled in December 1867 by Jane Alicia Innes, a
2 CONC nd a copy of which is still in the possession of Chris Read, who sent
2 CONC me a copy. It is clearly the original from which Granny copied out her
2 CONC  Red Book, and also the original of the chart owned by Leigh Boileau.
2 CONC It has handwritten additions from the 1890s on.
2 CONT
2 CONT Of course, its information is only as reliable as that given to the or
2 CONC iginal compositor, as she herself points out on the chart.
2 CONT
2 CONT The dates and names are often difficult to read, and thus the informat
2 CONC ion shown here, as I’ve transcribed from the chart, might be faulty in
2 CONC  places. Tough. So sue me.
2 CONT
2 CONT BBB refers once to something it calls “The Innes chart”. It’s hard to
2 CONC believe that this refers to something other than this chart, but no mo
2 CONC re detail is given. Furthermore, the reference in BBB to the Innes cha
2 CONC rt doesn’t seem to be consistent with the chart I’ve seen. It seems to
2 CONC  be referring to something quite different. Unlikely though this might
2 CONC  seem, it’s possible that BBB didn’t refer to this chart at all. Howev
2 CONC er, in BBB there is another oblique reference made to an attempt to li
2 CONC st all the descendants, including those in the female line, and this a
2 CONC lmost certainly refers to this chart.
0 @S7@ SOUR
1 TITL RBB
1 SUBTITLE Red Book of Boileaus; Catherine Charity Graham Bond
1 DESCRIPTION Old Granny’s “Red Book of Boileaus”, or so I call it. Handwritten note
2 CONC s, kept by the old Granny, and obtained I don’t know when. However, ju
2 CONC st about all the details I can check independently are agree with othe
2 CONC r sources.
2 CONT
2 CONT Interestingly, in 2004, another Boileau descendeant, Leigh Boileau, se
2 CONC nt me a copy of a wall chart that one of her relatives  picked up on a
2 CONC  trip to the UK in 1929. This wall chart is quite clearly the place th
2 CONC at Old Granny got her information, as it is word-for-word identical to
2 CONC  what is written in RBB. Old Granny claims she got the information whi
2 CONC le on a visit to Edmond Castle, and one suspects that the original wal
2 CONC l chart was hanging up there.
1 MEDIATYPE Document
1 QUOTEDTEXT RBB: Old Granny’s “Red Book of Boileaus”, or so I call it. Handwritten
2 CONC  notes, kept by the old Granny, and obtained I don’t know when. Howeve
2 CONC r, just about all the details I can check independently are agree with
2 CONC  other sources.
2 CONT
2 CONT Interestingly, in 2004, another Boileau descendeant, Leigh Boileau, se
2 CONC nt me a copy of a wall chart that one of her relatives  picked up on a
2 CONC  trip to the UK in 1929. This wall chart is quite clearly the place th
2 CONC at Old Granny got her information, as it is word-for-word identical to
2 CONC  what is written in RBB. Old Granny claims she got the information whi
2 CONC le on a visit to Edmond Castle, and one suspects that the original wal
2 CONC l chart was hanging up there.
