1 TEXT Dalston fell under the authority of the ancient diocese of Carlisle an
2 CONC d wills prior to 1858 were proved in the consistory court there. Recor
2 CONC ds from 1548 to 1858 include original wills, letters of administration
2 CONC  and inventories, although there are significant gaps in the years bef
2 CONC ore 1661. These are deposited with the CRO at Carlisle.
2 CONT
2 CONT Comprehensive indexes exist, at the Carlisle CRO, in card files easily
2 CONC  accessible in the reading room. The indexes cover from 1617 to 1941,
2 CONC listing the year of probate and the residence of the deceased. This is
2 CONC  extraordinarily helpful in distinguishing between many individuals of
2 CONC  the same name. Microfilm of many of these records, and a partial type
2 CONC script of the indexes, is available at the Kendal office of the CRO.
2 CONT
